window.BIZ_BOOKS=[{"bookId":"biz1","title":"外贸开发电话","sub":"冷call 八步 · 真实案例原文 + 推演示范","chapters":[{"cid":"mia1","title":"冷call 八步：从自报家门到引客户开口","blocks":[[9,"一个刹车片工厂的销售，在 Facebook 上看到客户在找货，直接打电话过去。原文只录到第 5 步，所以这一篇是很短的一通开场——重点不在谈成什么，而在看它怎么在两三句话里把「我是谁、我做什么、我为什么找你」说清楚。读的时候留意：她每一句都在回答客户心里的下一个疑问，而不是背公司介绍。","连连国际案例 · B1 · 冷call / 外贸开发"],[3,"原文对话","Transcript"],[0,"Mia：早上好！我是瑞安金汽配的 Mia，我们做刹车片的。请问 Bruce 在吗？","Mia: Good morning! This is Mia from Rian Golden Auto Parts Company, a supplier of brake pads. May I speak to Bruce?"],[0,"Bruce：我就是。你是说你们有刹车片现货？","Bruce: Speaking. Are you saying you have brake pads available for sale?"],[0,"Mia：是的，我们在 Facebook 上看到您在找刹车片。","Mia: Yes, we learned from Facebook that you are in the market for brake pads."],[0,"Bruce：你们是工厂吗？","Bruce: Are you factory?"],[0,"Mia：是，我们做刹车片二十多年了。有 E-mark 认证，客户遍布全球，也给不少知名品牌代工过。","Mia: Yes, we have been producing brake pads for over 20 years. We have E-mark certification and customers worldwide. We have collaborated with many well-known brands."],[0,"Bruce：听着不错。刹车片是安全件，质量非常关键。","Bruce: Sounds great! Brake pads are a type of safety component. The quality is very important."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我是瑞安金汽配的 Mia，我们做刹车片。","This is Mia from Rian Golden Auto Parts Company, a supplier of brake pads."],[0,"请问 Bruce 在吗？","May I speak to Bruce?"],[0,"你是说你们有刹车片可以供货？","Are you saying you have brake pads available for sale?"],[0,"我们在 Facebook 上看到你们在找刹车片。","We learned from Facebook that you are in the market for brake pads."],[0,"你们是工厂吗？（客户最常问的一句，比 Are you a factory 更口语）","Are you factory?"],[0,"我们做刹车片二十多年了。","We have been producing brake pads for over 20 years."],[0,"我们和不少知名品牌合作过。","We have collaborated with many well-known brands."]]},{"cid":"mia2","title":"后半场：把客户推到「发询价」","blocks":[[9,"原文到「质量很重要」就断了，后面六步（提供资料、引导发询价、致谢收尾）没有逐字稿。下面这一段是按八步框架补的示范，不是原文——可以当话术模板用，但别当成真实语料背。看点是：客户提了「质量」，她怎么把质量接成具体做法，再顺势要到型号和量。","推演示范 · B1 · 要资料 / 要询价"],[3,"推演示范","Demonstration"],[0,"Mia：我们有自己的质检实验室，每批货出运前都要过 E-mark 和我们内部的检测。","Mia: We run a full in-house QC lab, and every batch passes E-mark plus our own internal tests before shipment."],[0,"Bruce：行。能把目录和报价单发我吗？","Bruce: Good. Can you send me your catalog and a quotation sheet?"],[0,"Mia：当然。我马上把公司简介、目录和参考价发过去。另外能否告诉我您要的型号和月用量？这样报价才准。","Mia: Sure. I'll email our company profile, catalog and a sample price list shortly. Could you also tell me your target models and monthly volume so I can quote accurately?"],[0,"Bruce：轿车用的，一个月五千套左右。","Bruce: Around 5,000 sets a month for sedans."],[0,"Mia：记下了。我按这个做一份专门的报价，再发个询价表请您填。","Mia: Noted. I'll prepare a tailored quote and send an RFQ template for you to fill in."],[0,"Bruce：可以。","Bruce: Sounds good."],[0,"Mia：谢谢您的时间，Bruce，等您的询价。","Mia: Thank you for your time, Bruce. Looking forward to your inquiry."],[9,"八步框架原文要点：①自我介绍 ②我们供应什么 / 提供什么服务 ③我们的特色 ④提出诉求 ⑤引导客户说需求（产品 / 是否从中国进口 / 付款方式）⑥提供公司资料 ⑦引导客户发询价 ⑧感谢通话机会。",""],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我们有自己的质检实验室。","We run a full in-house QC lab."],[0,"能告诉我型号和月用量吗？这样报价才准。","Could you tell me your target models and monthly volume so I can quote accurately?"],[0,"我做一份针对性的报价。","I'll prepare a tailored quote."],[0,"我发个询价表请您填。","I'll send an RFQ template for you to fill in."],[0,"谢谢您的时间，等您的询价。","Thank you for your time. Looking forward to your inquiry."]]}]},{"bookId":"biz2","title":"客户与交期","sub":"客户压价、要账期、催交期时怎么说","chapters":[{"cid":"bc01","title":"把账期从 30 天延到 60 天","blocks":[[9,"客户安德莉亚现金流吃紧，打电话给供应商森顺子，想把账期从 30 天延到 60 天。她没有硬求，而是顺手抛出一张新订单当筹码。听的时候留意森顺子怎么既不一口回绝，也没马上松口。","British Council · B1 · 付款条件 / 现金流"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Junko：你好，我是森顺子，有什么可以帮您？","Junko: Hello, Junko Mori speaking. How can I help you?"],[0,"Andrea：顺子你好，我是 Red Band 的安德莉亚。我打电话是想问一下我们最近那张订单。","Andrea: Hi, Junko, it's Andrea here from Red Band. I'm calling about our latest order."],[0,"Junko：货都到了吧？我们这边收到签收确认了。","Junko: Everything arrived OK, right? We got the delivery confirmation at our end."],[0,"Andrea：订单没问题。我打电话是为了发票和付款条件，想请你帮个忙。","Andrea: Yes, everything's fine with the order. I'm calling about the invoice and the payment terms. I need a favour."],[0,"Junko：帮忙？你说。","Junko: A favour? What do you need?"],[0,"Andrea：这事有点不好开口，我想把付款期限延长一下。","Andrea: This is a little difficult, but I need an extension on the payment terms."],[0,"Andrea：我知道一般是 30 天，可我们最近现金流有点问题。要是能延到 60 天，那真是帮了我们大忙。","Andrea: I know they're usually 30 days, but we're having some cash flow problems. You'd really be helping us out if you could extend it to 60 days."],[0,"Junko：这事我不确定能不能办，安德莉亚。我们这边有规定，而且我们自己也得管现金流。","Junko: I'm not sure if I can do that, Andrea. We've got regulations at our end, and also have to manage our own cash flow."],[0,"Andrea：我保证不会成惯例，顺子。其实我还想再下一张新订单，跟上次一样大的量。","Andrea: I promise this won't become the norm, Junko. Actually, I also want to place another new order. The same size order as last time."],[0,"Andrea：是给一个重要客户的，他们货到就付款。","Andrea: It's for an important customer and they pay on delivery."],[0,"Junko：明白了。那这批新货一交，你的现金流问题就解决了。","Junko: I see. So your cash flow problem will be solved after this new order is delivered."],[0,"Andrea：就是这个意思。","Andrea: Exactly."],[0,"Junko：听着不错。你等一下，安德莉亚，我看看能不能想想办法。","Junko: That sounds good. Hold on, Andrea. Let me see what I can do."],[0,"Junko：行，这次我想我们可以破个例。","Junko: Yes, I think we can make an exception this time."],[0,"Andrea：太好了，顺子，谢谢你帮忙。","Andrea: That's great, Junko. I appreciate your help."],[0,"Junko：也谢谢你的生意，安德莉亚。这是相互的。","Junko: And we appreciate your business, Andrea. It works both ways."],[0,"Andrea：再谢一次，顺子。你能发个邮件，把延长账期的事确认一下吗？","Andrea: Thanks again, Junko. Can you send me a quick email confirmation of the payment terms extension?"],[0,"Junko：没问题，我们乐意帮忙。","Junko: Sure, no problem. We're happy to help you."],[0,"Andrea：好，那张新订单我邮件发你。","Andrea: Great. And I'll email you the new order."],[0,"Junko：好，我留意着。回头再聊。","Junko: Thanks. I'll keep an eye out for it. Talk to you soon."],[0,"Andrea：好，再见。","Andrea: You too. Goodbye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我打电话是想问一下我们最近那张订单。","I'm calling about our latest order."],[0,"我想把付款期限延长一下。","I need an extension on the payment terms."],[0,"要是能延到 60 天，那真是帮了我们大忙。","You'd really be helping us out if you could extend it to 60 days."],[0,"我们这边有规定。","We've got regulations at our end."],[0,"我保证不会成惯例。","I promise this won't become the norm."],[0,"这次我想我们可以破个例。","I think we can make an exception this time."],[0,"这是相互的。","It works both ways."]]},{"cid":"bb01","title":"客户不满意，第一句别急着解释","blocks":[[9,"把客户伺候好，靠的不是陪笑脸，而是把预期先摆到桌面上。这段里两个人一遍遍演练同一件事：怎么问出客户真正在意的点，怎么在出问题时第一句话就稳住对方，怎么跟老板反映一个难缠的客户又不显得在抱怨。留意那些听着很软、其实很有分量的句式。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 客户管理"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Phil：工作中你怎么应付客户？","Phil: How do you deal with clients and customers at work?"],[0,"Sian：我觉得最关键的是对人家实话实说。一有问题就沟通，马上告诉人家，别让人家突然被将一军。","Sian: I think the main thing is to be very honest with them. Communicate if there's any problems, let them know straight away so you're not suddenly springing a surprise on them."],[0,"George：我觉得照着客户的需求去做，效果一直不错。先听人家要什么，再想办法给到。","George: I think trying to tailor something to the customer's needs always works quite well. Listening to what the customer wants and then trying to deliver that."],[0,"Phil：客户这个词，具体指什么人？","Phil: What do we mean by customers or clients?"],[0,"Phil：好，皮帕，假设你公司刚接了个大客户，活儿一下多了不少，老板让你负责对接这个客户。你怎么让人家满意？","Phil: OK, Pippa, let's imagine that you work at a company that has a big new client and lots of new work. Your boss puts you in charge of managing the client. How can you keep them happy?"],[0,"Pippa：菲尔，我第一件事是先弄清楚这个客户到底要什么，他期待跟我们公司是一种什么关系。所以我会问，在您看来，什么样的合作才算成功？或者问，我们这边怎么做，才能保证您那边一切顺利？","Pippa: So, Phil, the first thing I do is try to establish what this client wants. What are their expectations of their relationship with my company? So, I might ask something like, 'what does a successful partnership look like for you?' Or I might ask, 'what can we do to make sure things run smoothly on your side?'"],[0,"Phil：对，也可以把你的计划跟他们核一下。你可以说，我们打算月底先把项目第一部分交给您，这符合您的预期吗？","Phil: Yeah, and you might want to check your plans with them. So 'we're looking to deliver the first part of the project to you by the end of the month. Is that in line with your expectations?' you could say."],[0,"Pippa：对。也可以这么说，我们一般会留一周，按客户的反馈做修改，您那边这样行得通吗？把自己的做事方式讲清楚很有用，能免掉后面扯皮——不然客户可能以为你能更快，或者以为你会换个做法。","Pippa: Yeah. Another way you could phrase this is saying 'we usually allocate a week to make improvements based on client feedback. Will that work on your end?' So, explaining the way you work can be really useful because it avoids conflicts further down the line. In case maybe the client thought you could be quicker or do something in a different way."],[0,"Phil：对，最重要的就是一直保持沟通。时不时跟客户对一下，定期碰个头看看进展。关键是出了问题、有了延误，你能第一时间跟客户提出来，别等后面给人一个坏消息。","Phil: Yeah, and what's really important is just to keep communicating. So maybe check in with your clients. You might want to have regular catch ups to just check on progress. What's really important is that if there are any problems or any delays, that you're able to flag those up very quickly with your client so that there aren't any bad surprises down the line."],[0,"Pippa：那有时候客户对你或者你公司的活儿不满意，这种情况怎么处理，还能保持专业？","Pippa: Now, sometimes a client or customer might be unhappy about the work you or your company has done. So how can you deal with this Phil, and stay professional?"],[0,"Phil：还是那句话，先回到客户到底要什么。你可以跟他说，抱歉这次没达到您的预期，我们要在哪方面改进才能做对？怎么样才能让您这边更顺？","Phil: OK, well, I think again, the most important thing is to go back to what does the client want? So, you could say to them, 'I'm sorry we didn't meet your expectations. What can we improve on to get this right? How can things work better for you?'"],[0,"Pippa：对，这很重要，你得弄清人家想要什么。别一上来就防着。你得明白他为什么觉得你做错了。也可以给对方吃颗定心丸，说我们以后一定避免这个问题。或者，您的意见我已经转给团队了，您放心，不会再出现。","Pippa: Yes, I think that's important because you need to understand what they want from you. You don't want to get defensive. You need to understand why they think what you've done is wrong. You can also reassure them so you can tell them, 'we'll be sure to avoid this problem in the future'. Or 'I've shared your feedback with the team and rest assured, this won't happen again'."],[0,"Phil：有时候你会觉得客户的期望根本不现实。交期给得太紧，或者对你的活儿提一堆你不认同的修改。这时候怎么办？","Phil: Sometimes you might feel like your client has unrealistic expectations. Maybe they give you deadlines that are too tight, or they ask for lots of changes to your work that you don't agree with. What can you do?"],[0,"Pippa：这挺难的，因为钱是客户付的，你得在让人家满意和别白耗时间之间找平衡，别干出超出这单价值的活儿。你得一直哄着，可你也得干活，还有别的客户。","Pippa: Well, it's tricky because usually the client is paying you, so you have to balance keeping them happy with making sure that you're not wasting time or doing more work than the job is worth. You have to always keep them happy, but you also have to do your job and you have other clients."],[0,"Phil：这里真正重要的是摸清客户最看重什么，因为很可能能找到折中方案。就是跟你原先说的不一样、但对方也认的做法，因为它对上的是人家最在意的那一点。可能是人家只要按时拿到东西，也可能交期没那么死，但质量标准一点不能让。摸清优先级，才谈得成。","Phil: What actually can be really important here is to try and identify what the actual priorities are that your clients have, because it may be that you can find a compromise. That's an agreement that's different to what you originally said that they're happy with, because it meets what their priorities are. Whether it's they just need something that's ready on time, or whether the deadlines aren't actually as strict as they said, but the quality standard absolutely has to be there. Finding their priorities can help you come to an agreement."],[0,"Pippa：对，就是个平衡和折中的事。","Pippa: Yeah, it's all about balance and compromise."],[0,"George：我觉得就是把情况解释清楚，然后给人家一个现实的预期。","George: I think just trying to explain what the situation is and try and give them some realistic expectations."],[0,"Sian：站在人家的角度看看，可能我们觉得不现实，可对人家来说，那明明就是现实的。反正就是多点耐心吧。","Sian: See it from their point of view, I guess, because it may seem unrealistic to us, but for them, it obviously does seem realistic. Yeah, it's just be patient, I think."],[0,"Pippa：西安提到沟通的重要，哪怕你觉得客户不讲理。你可以试着先就做事方式达成一致。比如可以说，我想确认一下咱们理解是一致的。或者，我想确保双方流程对得上，这件事您希望怎么个做法？","Pippa: So, Sian mentioned the importance of communication, even if you think a client is being unreasonable. So you can try and agree a particular way of working. So, you could say something like, 'I just want to be sure we're on the same page', or 'I want to make sure our processes are aligned. What's your preferred way of working on this?'"],[0,"Phil：对。有时候你得跟老板谈谈某个客户，尤其是出了点岔子的时候。但尽量专业一点，别变成抱怨。你可以说，这个项目有个问题想跟您提一下，对方额外加活的要求，您希望我怎么回？或者，这个客户怎么应对最好？我想让人家满意，但他要求挺多，已经影响到别的活儿了。","Phil: Yeah. And sometimes you might need to talk to your boss about a client and particularly if something's gone a little bit wrong. But do try to remain professional rather than moaning. So, you might say, 'can I flag a problem with this project? How would you like me to respond to requests for extra work?' Or 'what's the best approach with this client? I want to keep them happy, but they're quite a demanding client, and it's impacting other work.'"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"马上告诉人家，别让人家突然被将一军","let them know straight away so you're not suddenly springing a surprise on them"],[0,"在您看来，什么样的合作才算成功？","What does a successful partnership look like for you?"],[0,"这符合您的预期吗？","Is that in line with your expectations?"],[0,"您那边这样行得通吗？","Will that work on your end?"],[0,"抱歉，这次没达到您的预期。","I'm sorry we didn't meet your expectations."],[0,"您的意见我已经转给团队了，您放心，不会再出现。","I've shared your feedback with the team and rest assured, this won't happen again."],[0,"我想确认一下咱们理解是一致的。","I just want to be sure we're on the same page."],[0,"这个项目有个问题，我能跟您提一下吗？","Can I flag a problem with this project?"]]},{"cid":"bb02","title":"交期要延，怎么说客户才不炸","blocks":[[9,"交期这件事，难的不在技术，在你敢不敢把做不完说出口、以及怎么说。这一段谈的是给别人的死线、给自己留的缓冲，还有临时要改期时怎么开口。注意他们把催和改分得很清楚：催要给理由，改要留台阶。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 交期与物流"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Pippa：工作中你觉得自己很难有条理吗？","Pippa: Do you find it hard to stay organised at work?"],[0,"Beth：我特别喜欢列待办清单，做完一项打个勾，那种满足感特别好。","Beth: I love a to-do list, and then I tick off when I've done that task and I get a great feeling of satisfaction."],[0,"Neil：这方面我不够有条理。一开始我总觉得事儿太多，后来想想，其实还行，结果该做的规划反倒一直没做。","Neil: I'm not as organised as I should be about it. I think probably at first I think it's too much. And then I think about it and I realise it's OK, and then I don't do the planning I should have done in the first place."],[0,"Pippa：菲尔，咱们先从交期说起。工作中有时你得靠别人交东西，得把时间点说清楚，才能保证自己按时交付。怎么才能把交期讲明白？","Pippa: So, Phil, let's start with deadlines. Sometimes at work you rely on the work of other people, and you need to set clear deadlines to make sure that you can deliver everything on time. How can you make deadlines clear at work?"],[0,"Phil：你可以这么说，要想赶上客户那个交期，你这份活儿我明天下班前必须拿到。差不多这个意思。","Phil: Yeah, you can say stuff like, 'if we're going to meet that client's deadline, I need this work from you by the end of the day tomorrow' or something like that."],[0,"Pippa：对，我会再跟对方确认一下，比如问，这个时间你看可行吗？你得保证给出去的时间，人家真的做得到。","Pippa: Yeah, I might then check that deadline with them so I could say something like, 'does that sound feasible?' You want to make sure the deadline you're giving to someone is something that they can actually realistically do."],[0,"Phil：对。你可以说某件事是 firm deadline，或者说 hard deadline，意思就是动不了。这个点一过，事情就黄了。","Phil: Yeah. You can say that there is a 'firm deadline' for something or a 'hard deadline', and what that means is we can't move it. If we miss the deadline, it's not going to work."],[0,"Pippa：我还有一种说法，就是把我的流程跟对方讲一遍。比如，我在排这个项目的计划，你那一块要是在这个日子前弄完就太好了。","Pippa: Another way I might communicate it is I might just talk someone through my process. I might say 'I'm mapping out our plan for this project. If you could finish your part by this date, that would be great'."],[0,"Phil：对。也可以从终点往回倒推，看看中间每个环节最晚得什么时候完成。","Phil: Yeah. It might be a good idea to look at the deadline and then work backwards and think of when the other stages need to be done by."],[0,"Pippa：对，而且一定要留缓冲。就是万一出岔子，手上还有几天余地。跟那种你觉得可能会拖的人合作，我尤其会这么干。就是给出问题的空间，或者人家生病了、有别的原因干不了。","Pippa: Yeah, and you definitely want to add in contingency. And that means a little bit of time in case something goes wrong. And I especially like to do this when you're working with someone who you think might miss the deadline that you give them. So, you're just allowing for problems, or just for someone to be ill or unable to do the work for another reason."],[0,"Phil：交期这事我有一条铁律。","Phil: I have a golden rule with deadlines."],[0,"Pippa：什么铁律？","Pippa: What's that?"],[0,"Phil：永远别把真实交期告诉别人。","Phil: Never tell anyone your real deadlines."],[0,"Pippa：对，很多人都这么干。给一个比真实交期早一周的假日子。所以我总是先定死真实交期，再往回排，这样按我告诉别人的日子算，自己手上就多出时间。","Pippa: Yes, that's something a lot of people do. They'll give them a fake deadline that's maybe a week earlier than the real deadline. Yeah, so that's why I would always sort of start with the real deadline and then map backwards. So, I'm giving myself enough time based off what I'm telling other people."],[0,"Phil：有时候是别人给你交期，有时候是别人问你要多久、让你自己定。这种情况要考虑什么？","Phil: Sometimes at work, you're given a deadline. In other situations, you're asked to give an idea of how long something will take and set your own deadlines. What do we need to consider here?"],[0,"Pippa：这种时候最容易把话说满，张口就是没问题，这个我很快就能弄完。但宁可多给自己点时间，提前交出去，也别因为时间估得太乐观，最后不得不改期。","Pippa: Well, Phil, the temptation in this situation is to overpromise, so to say, oh, yeah, I can do that really easily. But it's better to give yourself more time, I guess, and deliver something early, than have to move a deadline because you were too optimistic about how much time you had."],[0,"Phil：有句话怎么说来着，先把话往低了说，再超额交付。","Phil: What's that saying? It's best to under promise and overdeliver."],[0,"Pippa：没错。而且你不知道说多久才算合适，这本身就让人紧张。很多人其实有时间盲区，根本估不准要花多久。所以你得想想怎么跟问你的人商量，用什么话去说。","Pippa: Exactly. And it can be stressful when you're not sure what an acceptable answer is, for how long something will take. A lot of us actually have time blindness and really struggle to judge how long things will take. So you should probably think about how you can discuss it with the person who's asked you and what language you can use."],[0,"Phil：对，你可以说，我们下周把报告交出来，这个时间听着合理吗？也可以先跟同事核一下，看这个说法是不是真的靠谱。","Phil: Yeah, so you could say 'if we delivered the report by next week, does that sound reasonable?' And you might want to check your ideas with your colleagues to see if it actually sounds realistic."],[0,"Pippa：对。也可以这么说，说实话，这个要做好得花点时间，我建议……然后说出你的建议，再问，这个跟您的时间安排对得上吗？这样既表示你算过了，又还在确认是不是合人家的预期——因为人家问你的时候，你根本不知道他心里那个大概数字是多少。","Pippa: Yeah. Another way you could phrase it is saying something like 'realistically, we need a while to do this properly. I would suggest...' and then give your suggestion. 'Does that fit in with your timeline?' So you're showing that you've thought about how long you think it will take, but you want to check still that it fits in with the expectations, because it's really hard when someone asks you and you don't know what their ballpark figure was for something."],[0,"Phil：对。还有一点值得问清楚，就是咱们前面说的死线，这件事有没有死线？就是摸一下有没有余地，还是说没得谈，就得那时候完成。","Phil: Yeah. Another thing that might be good to check here, we talked earlier about hard deadlines, is like, do we have a hard deadline on this? It's trying to find out if there is flexibility or if actually, no, it has to be done by then and that's it."],[0,"Pippa：对。而且如果人家让你估时间，答案可能有好几个，取决于做到多细。你也可以把问题扔回去，问，您理想中希望什么时候完成？然后看看两个人想的是不是差不多。","Pippa: Yeah. And if someone's asked you to estimate how long it will take to do something and there could be several answers, it depends how much detail you go into, for example. So, you could just throw the question back to them and say 'when would you like it finished ideally?' and then kind of see if you've got similar ideas in mind."],[0,"Pippa：工作安排里还有一块叫 logistics，就是把一堆不同的事协调好，让整件事顺顺当当跑起来。","Pippa: Another aspect of work organisation is something called logistics. This is what we call the coordination of lots of different things to make sure something runs smoothly."],[0,"Phil：对。这就意味着你得同时跟很多人沟通，细节一变就得通知到。怎么做既专业又不招人烦？","Phil: Yes. And this can mean that you need to be in communication with lots of people at the same time, and update them about changing details. How can you do this professionally and without annoying someone?"],[0,"Pippa：我语气上一直保持客气，但话说清楚。比如发邮件约时间，日子还没定，你可以问，这个日子我先暂定，回头再跟您确认，行吗？","Pippa: Well, I would always keep my tone friendly, but be clear. So, one thing you can do if you're emailing people but you're not sure about a day is ask, 'can I pencil in this date and come back to confirm later?'"],[0,"Phil：对，也可以说，临近了我再把细节发您。","Phil: Yeah, you could always say 'I'll follow up with more details closer to the time'."],[0,"Pippa：还有时候你不得不调安排，又不想惹人不高兴，那就一定要道歉。就说，实在抱歉，这个约能不能改一下？我们这边出了些躲不开的延误。得让人看出你在意人家的时间。","Pippa: Sometimes as well, you'll have to move things around and you don't want to annoy someone doing this, so I would always apologise. Just say, 'I'm so sorry. Is it possible to move the appointment? We've had some unavoidable delays'. So you want to show that you're being considerate of someone else's time."],[0,"Phil：对。通知的时候，邮件标题和日历邀请都要写清楚。一定要回一封确认，别让人糊涂。相当于把这个沟通的环闭上。","Phil: Yeah. And when you're communicating that, make sure that you're clear with your email subjects and any calendar invites that you've sent. Always reply to confirm so that there's no confusion. It's kind of, you're closing the loop of the communication."],[0,"Pippa：对。你问人家某个日子行不行，人家回说行，你就再回一封，说太好了，那我就定这个日子。这样双方都确定这事就是定了。","Pippa: Yes. So if you ask someone, can they do a date and they come back and say yes. Then you email them back and say, 'that's great, I'll book in this date'. So everybody is sure that it's definitely happening."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这个时间你看可行吗？","Does that sound feasible?"],[0,"这个有死线，动不了。","There's a firm deadline on this — we can't move it."],[0,"一定要留出缓冲时间。","You definitely want to add in contingency."],[0,"先把话往低了说，再超额交付。","It's best to under promise and overdeliver."],[0,"这个跟您的时间安排对得上吗？","Does that fit in with your timeline?"],[0,"这个日子我先暂定，回头再跟您确认行吗？","Can I pencil in this date and come back to confirm later?"],[0,"我们这边出了些躲不开的延误。","We've had some unavoidable delays."],[0,"临近了我再把细节发您。","I'll follow up with more details closer to the time."]]}]},{"bookId":"biz3","title":"求职与面试","sub":"十集连续剧：从筛简历到谈薪资","chapters":[{"cid":"bc02","title":"炒掉销售总监，重写招聘条件","blocks":[[9,"WebWare 的 CEO 菲利普因为丢了 DollarMart 这个大客户，在电话里当场把销售总监布莱恩辞了。挂了电话他打给 HR 玛西亚，一条条列出新销售总监该是什么样的人。整集几乎都是菲利普一个人在说，注意他怎么下这个狠手，又怎么把自己的要求包装成“你觉得呢”。","British Council · B1–B2 · 招聘 / 岗位要求"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Philip：你说什么？什么意思？你把 DollarMart 的合同丢了？","Philip: You what? What do you mean? You've lost the DollarMart contract?"],[0,"Philip：布莱恩，你跟我说这是玩笑！那是我们最大的合同，你把它丢了！","Philip: Oh, Brian, tell me you're joking! That's our biggest contract and you've lost it!"],[0,"Philip：行，行。是，我知道你最近家里有些事。是，当然。我也知道对手的产品做得更好了，可布莱恩，这些说到底都是借口。","Philip: OK. OK. Yes, I know you've had some personal problems recently. Yes, sure. Yes, I know our competitors have improved their offer, but really, Brian, these are just excuses."],[0,"Philip：布莱恩，你别这样——你整个上季度都没完成既定目标。上次绩效面谈我们就谈过，我当时就说必须改，说实话，你没改。","Philip: Oh, Brian, come on – you failed to meet agreed targets for the entire last quarter. We talked about this in your last performance review and I told you then it had to improve, and to be quite honest – it hasn't."],[0,"Philip：丢了 DollarMart 这个合同，是最后一根稻草。不行，抱歉布莱恩，就这样了。机会已经给过你了。","Philip: Losing the DollarMart contract is the last straw. No, I'm sorry, Brian, that's it. That's your last chance."],[0,"Philip：我只能请你走了。请你走，对，就是这个意思，布莱恩。你被解雇了。","Philip: I'm going to have to let you go. Let you go. Yes, that's what it means, Brian. You're fired."],[0,"Philip：杰丝，帮我接一下 HR 的玛西亚。谢谢。","Philip: Hi, Jess. Can you put me through to Marcia in HR, please? Thank you."],[0,"Philip：玛西亚，我是菲利普。是这样，布莱恩我辞掉了。他把 DollarMart 这个客户弄丢了。","Philip: Hi, Marcia. It's Philip here. Listen, I've had to let Brian go. He lost us the DollarMart account."],[0,"Philip：是，但这事已经拖了一阵了，他就是不再出力了。警告也警告过，上次绩效评估很差，他自己也知道迟早有这一天。","Philip: Yeah, but it had been going on for a while, and he just wasn't pulling his weight any more. He'd been warned. His last performance review was really bad. He knew it was coming."],[0,"Philip：所以我们要找新人，得先把要什么样的人定下来。","Philip: So, we'll be looking for someone new and we'll need to decide on who that is."],[0,"Philip：要找什么样的人？问得好。我还指望你帮我定呢！","Philip: Who are we looking for? Good question. I was hoping you might be able to help me with that!"],[0,"Philip：我的想法是这样，你同意就说。","Philip: Here's what I'm thinking and let me know if you agree."],[0,"Philip：首先，本科是必须的，什么专业无所谓。然后我看还得有个硕士或者 MBA。","Philip: Well, obviously, they'll need to have a first degree. Doesn't matter what subject. And then a master's or an MBA, I'd say."],[0,"Marcia：经验呢？","Marcia: Experience?"],[0,"Philip：至少五年跨国公司的相关经验。我要的是有实打实业绩的人。","Philip: At least five years' relevant experience in an international company. I want somebody with a proven track record."],[0,"Philip：还有，必须能跟人合作——布莱恩从来做不到——所以要人际能力强。","Philip: Oh, they have to be a team player – Brian never was – so strong interpersonal skills."],[0,"Philip：还有，我要有眼光的人。对，就是“眼光”。我知道这词不好定义。我的意思是，这人得清楚我们处在一个变化很快的市场，而且能把这个变化变成我们的优势。","Philip: Oh, and I want someone with vision. Yes, 'vision'! Well, I know it's difficult to define. What I mean is, someone who knows we're in a rapidly changing market, and they can use it to our advantage."],[0,"Philip：线上销售的经验，也许吧，不过这个我会感兴趣。","Philip: Experience with online sales, perhaps, but yes, I'd be interested in that."],[0,"Philip：还有语言。这个我怎么强调都不为过。不一定要母语者，但英语必须非常好。还得会第二门语言——西班牙语，最好的是普通话。","Philip: Oh, language skills. I can't emphasise that enough. Not necessarily a native speaker, but they must be very good at English. And another language as well – Spanish, or Mandarin is best."],[0,"Philip：你觉得这样行吗？好。那你尽快把招聘广告发到网站上，还有行业媒体也发一份。","Philip: Does that sound OK to you? Great. OK, can you get an ad out on the website as soon as possible? Oh, and the trade press as well."],[0,"Philip：好，太好了，谢谢你玛西亚。月底之前我要见到新的销售总监。挂了！","Philip: OK, great. Thanks, Marcia. I want a new sales director by the end of the month. Bye!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这是最后一根稻草，我忍到头了。","That's the last straw."],[0,"我只能请你走了。","I'm going to have to let you go."],[0,"他就是不再出力了。","He just wasn't pulling his weight any more."],[0,"我要的是有实打实业绩的人。","I want somebody with a proven track record."],[0,"这一点我怎么强调都不为过。","I can't emphasise that enough."],[0,"他们能把这个变成我们的优势。","They can use it to our advantage."],[0,"你觉得这样行吗？","Does that sound OK to you?"]]},{"cid":"bc03","title":"两百份简历，只留十二个人","blocks":[[9,"招聘广告发出去，两百多份申请涌进来，玛西亚硬是筛出 12 个人的面试名单，再和菲利普敲定面试怎么考。两人从“常规流程”一路聊到临时加一场短演示。注意他们怎么用半句话就把一件事定下来。","British Council · B1–B2 · 筛选 / 面试安排"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Philip：玛西亚，我们收到多少份申请？","Philip: So, how many applications did we get, Marcia?"],[0,"Marcia：总共两百多份！","Marcia: Well, overall we've got over 200!"],[0,"Philip：这么多？","Philip: That many?"],[0,"Marcia：是，不过大部分可以直接扔掉——经验不对、学历不对，诸如此类。","Marcia: Yes, but most of which we can discard right away – people who don't have the right experience, qualifications, that kind of thing."],[0,"Philip：那当然。","Philip: Of course."],[0,"Marcia：剩下的还有交十页长简历的，简历用漫画字体的，用绿墨水打印的，还有人附一张自己在迪厅跳舞的照片。","Marcia: And then we get the people who submit ten-page-long CVs, or CVs in comic book font, or green ink, or they attach a photo of themselves disco dancing."],[0,"Marcia：你懂那种感觉吧？所以我把真正靠谱的筛出来，定了 12 个人的面试名单。","Marcia: You know the kind of thing? So, I've whittled down the serious candidates to a shortlist of 12 people."],[0,"Philip：这 12 个都要面？","Philip: And we'll interview all of them?"],[0,"Marcia：我觉得该都面，不过当然，先让你过一遍。","Marcia: I think we should but, obviously, I'll let you have a look first."],[0,"Philip：好。那都有些什么人？","Philip: Great. So, who have we got then?"],[0,"Marcia：有几个相当不错的，特别是两个。","Marcia: Well, I think we've got some pretty strong candidates. Two in particular."],[0,"Philip：条件都对得上吗？","Philip: They have the right kind of profile?"],[0,"Marcia：绝对对得上。学历背景硬，有跨国销售经验，语言也行。","Marcia: I'd certainly say so. Strong educational background, experience in multinational sales, language skills."],[0,"Philip：好，我挺想见见他们。","Philip: Good. I look forward to meeting them."],[0,"Marcia：那咱们就走常规面试流程吧。","Marcia: So, I'd say we do the standard interview format."],[0,"Philip：行。","Philip: Sure."],[0,"Marcia：先问几个笼统的，再进细节。","Marcia: A few general questions, then on to specifics."],[0,"Philip：对，就是这样。我想听他们具体讲过哪件事、怎么解决的。","Philip: Yes, exactly. I want to hear specific details of when they've solved problems."],[0,"Marcia：对，然后就是你说的那个“眼光”。","Marcia: Yes, and then something about 'vision', as you put it."],[0,"Philip：对。让他们做个简短的演示，你觉得怎么样？","Philip: Yes. What do you think about a brief presentation?"],[0,"Marcia：我觉得这主意不错。可以让他们做个短演示，讲讲他们觉得公司该往哪走，以及他们打算怎么带我们走到那儿。","Marcia: I think that's a good idea. We could ask them to give a short presentation on where they see the company going and how they see themselves taking us there."],[0,"Philip：太好了！跟你说，我现在特别期待这场面试！","Philip: Great! You know something? I'm really looking forward to this!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"大部分可以直接扔掉。","Most of which we can discard right away."],[0,"我把真正靠谱的筛出来，定了 12 个人的面试名单。","I've whittled down the serious candidates to a shortlist of 12 people."],[0,"他们条件都对得上吗？","They have the right kind of profile?"],[0,"咱们就走常规面试流程。","We do the standard interview format."],[0,"先问几个笼统的，再进细节。","A few general questions, then on to specifics."],[0,"还有你说的那个“眼光”。","Something about 'vision', as you put it."],[0,"让他们做个简短的演示，你觉得怎么样？","What do you think about a brief presentation?"]]},{"cid":"bc04","title":"电话通知面试：当天怎么走","blocks":[[9,"玛西亚分别打给两位入围者丹尼尔和莎拉，把面试当天的安排讲一遍：谁来接、路费怎么报、分几轮、要准备什么。丹尼尔急着表现，莎拉一路追问细节，两个人的反应完全不一样。注意玛西亚怎么把一场考试说成“我们很期待见到你”。","British Council · B1 · 面试 / 流程说明"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Marcia：你好，我是 WebWare 的玛西亚·博德曼。","Marcia: Hi, I'm Marcia Boardman. I'm calling from WebWare."],[0,"Daniel：玛西亚你好，接到你电话太好了。","Daniel: Oh, hi, Marcia. Great to hear from you."],[0,"Marcia：你应该已经收到通知，你进面试名单了。","Marcia: You'll have already been told you've been shortlisted for interview."],[0,"Sarah：是，太好了。喂？你听得见吗？","Sarah: Oh, yes, great. Hello? Can you hear me?"],[0,"Marcia：听得见。现在说话方便吗？要不要我晚点再打？","Marcia: Yes. Is it OK if I call you now? Would you like me to call you back later?"],[0,"Sarah：不用不用，现在可以。","Sarah: No, no, no, that's OK."],[0,"Marcia：好。我们很期待见到你。","Marcia: Good. Well, we're very excited about meeting you."],[0,"Marcia：我想把当天的流程跟你说一遍。你到了会有人接你，路费可以报销，然后带你上来见我和 CEO 菲利普·哈特。","Marcia: OK, I just want to talk you through the procedure for the day. Someone will meet you when you arrive, reimburse you for any travel expenses you may have, and then bring you up to meet myself and Philip Hart, the CEO."],[0,"Daniel：好，听着不错。那面试官就你们两位吗？","Daniel: OK, sounds good. So, will you be the only members of the interview panel there, then?"],[0,"Marcia：对，就我和菲利普跟你谈。面试分三部分。先问一些关于你本人、学历和职业背景的常规问题，然后进细节。","Marcia: Yes, it'll be just me and Philip who will talk to you. The interview will be in three parts. First of all we'll ask you some general questions about yourself and your educational and professional background, then we'll move on to specifics."],[0,"Sarah：细节？那具体会问些什么问题？","Sarah: Oh, specifics? Well, what kind of questions will you be asking?"],[0,"Marcia：跟你简历一起交的那份个人陈述差不多。我们会希望你举真实的例子，讲你遇到过、解决过什么问题，还有你觉得到目前为止职业上最大的成绩。","Marcia: Well, it'll be very similar to the personal statement you submitted with your CV. We'll be expecting you to give actual examples of problems you've faced and solved, and of what you feel are the major successes in your career so far."],[0,"Daniel：好，听着挺好，等不及了！","Daniel: OK, well, yeah, that sounds great. Can't wait!"],[0,"Marcia：然后会留时间让你问我们，关于这个职位或者 WebWare 本身都行。","Marcia: Then there'll be a chance for you to ask us any questions about the job itself or WebWare in general."],[0,"Sarah：好，我想想该问什么！","Sarah: Oh, OK. I'll think of something!"],[0,"Marcia：之后我们希望你做个短演示，讲讲你认为 WebWare 这家公司该往哪发展，以及你打算怎么带我们走到那儿。","Marcia: After that, we'd like you to give a short presentation on how you see WebWare as a company progressing, and how you see yourself taking us there."],[0,"Daniel：那我是不是得做得正式一点？","Daniel: OK, so will I be expected to give, like, a formal-style presentation?"],[0,"Marcia：正式还是随意，你自己定。现场有翻页纸和投影仪。还需要别的，跟我们说一声。","Marcia: It can be as formal or as informal as you like. There'll be a flip chart and a data projector there available. If you need anything else, just let us know."],[0,"Sarah：还要做演示啊。我得想想。这种我好久没做过了。","Sarah: Oh, OK, a presentation! I'll think of something. I haven't done one of those in a while."],[0,"Marcia：都清楚了吗？好。那丹尼尔，我们一周后的明天上午 11 点见。","Marcia: Is that all clear? Great. So, Daniel, I'll see you at 11 a.m., a week tomorrow."],[0,"Daniel：好，太好了，期待见到你！谢谢，再见。","Daniel: OK, great, yeah, I look forward to meeting you! Thanks, bye."],[0,"Marcia：莎拉，那我们一周后的明天下午 1 点见。祝你好运！","Marcia: OK, so, Sarah, we'll be seeing you at 1 p.m., a week tomorrow. Best of luck!"],[0,"Sarah：谢谢。我确实需要点运气！","Sarah: Oh, thanks. I'll need it!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"接到你电话太好了。","Great to hear from you."],[0,"现在说话方便吗？","Is it OK if I call you now?"],[0,"我想把当天的流程跟你说一遍。","I just want to talk you through the procedure for the day."],[0,"路费可以报销。","Reimburse you for any travel expenses you may have."],[0,"正式还是随意，你自己定。","It can be as formal or as informal as you like."],[0,"一周后的明天。","A week tomorrow."],[0,"我确实需要点运气！","I'll need it!"]]},{"cid":"bc05","title":"面试翻车：把公司当跳板","blocks":[[9,"丹尼尔走进面试间，对面坐着 HR 玛西亚和 CEO 菲利普。他简历漂亮、开场热络，可从“爱好”聊到“为什么离职”，回答越来越随口。这一集是标准的反面教材，听的时候分辨一下：哪些话听着像自信，其实是给自己挖坑。","British Council · B1–B2 · 面试 / 反面案例"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Daniel：你们好！","Daniel: Hi there!"],[0,"Marcia：早上好，丹尼尔！","Marcia: Good morning, Daniel!"],[0,"Daniel：叫我丹就行。","Daniel: Oh, Dan, please."],[0,"Marcia：我是玛西亚·博德曼，我们通过电话。这位是我们的 CEO 菲利普·哈特。","Marcia: I'm Marcia Boardman – we spoke on the phone – and this is Philip Hart, our CEO."],[0,"Philip：你好！","Philip: Hello!"],[0,"Daniel：很高兴见到两位。","Daniel: Nice to meet you both."],[0,"Philip：你简历上写着你对攀岩感兴趣。","Philip: So, it says here on your CV that you're interested in rock climbing."],[0,"Daniel：对，我特别喜欢！","Daniel: Yeah, I love it!"],[0,"Philip：太好了，我也是！你上次去爬是什么时候？","Philip: Great, so do I! When did you last go climbing?"],[0,"Daniel：有阵子了。","Daniel: Well, it was a while ago, now."],[0,"Philip：去过什么有意思的地方吗？","Philip: Anywhere interesting?"],[0,"Daniel：有啊，我爬了我家后面那座小山，走了大概 30 分钟！","Daniel: Yeah, I walked up the hill behind my house. Took me about 30 minutes!"],[0,"Philip：哦。","Philip: Oh."],[0,"Marcia：丹尼尔，能简单说说你现在的职位吗？","Marcia: OK, Daniel, can you tell us a little bit about your current position?"],[0,"Daniel：当然。简历上写了，我在 Networld 的欧洲销售团队。我们是全球领先的 IT 硬件供应商。","Daniel: Certainly. As it says in the CV, I'm part of the European sales team at Networld. We're the world's leading supplier of IT hardware."],[0,"Philip：那你为什么想换工作？","Philip: Why do you want to move on?"],[0,"Daniel：他们对我来说太小了！","Daniel: Well, they're too small for me!"],[0,"Marcia：Networld 对你来说太小？","Marcia: Networld are too small for you?"],[0,"Daniel：对，我想找个大得多的平台。","Daniel: Yeah, I'm looking for something much bigger."],[0,"Philip：我们可算不上大公司，不过我们正打算做大。你最初是看上 WebWare 哪一点？","Philip: Well, we're not a big company by any means, but we are looking to grow! What first attracted you to WebWare in particular?"],[0,"Daniel：我把 WebWare 差不多当成一块跳板。","Daniel: Well, I see WebWare as kind of like a stepping stone."],[0,"Marcia：不好意思，你说什么？","Marcia: Sorry?"],[0,"Daniel：先在这儿干，攒够经验，再往更大的地方走。","Daniel: Yeah, start here, gain the necessary experience, then move on to something bigger."],[0,"Philip：好吧，你的野心我确实佩服。","Philip: OK, well, I do admire your ambition!"],[0,"Daniel：谢谢，我野心多的是！","Daniel: Thanks. I've got lots of it!"],[0,"Marcia：我们说说带人。能不能举个例子，你处理过特别难搞的下属？","Marcia: Let's move on to managing people. Can you give an example of a time when you had to deal with a particularly difficult managee?"],[0,"Daniel：可以，这其实是我的强项。几年前有个同事，不出力，说白了就是懒，我就让他走人。","Daniel: Sure, well, I think that's one of my strong points, actually. A couple of years ago, I was working with a guy, he wasn't pulling his weight, basically being lazy – so I told him to get out."],[0,"Marcia：你没给他做绩效面谈、没警告过，也没试着调动一下他的积极性？","Marcia: Oh, you didn't give him a performance review or a warning or perhaps try to develop his motivation?"],[0,"Daniel：没有没有。那些啰嗦流程一概不做。谁不拼命干，谁就走人！我就这么干，我这人硬。","Daniel: No, no, no, no. None of that rubbish. If someone's not working hard enough, then they're out! That's the way I work. I'm a hard man."],[0,"Marcia：我明白了。","Marcia: I see."],[0,"Philip：市场变化很快，你会怎么应对？","Philip: How would you handle a rapidly changing market?"],[0,"Daniel：基本上什么都不改！照常干，不管外面怎么变。","Daniel: Basically not change anything at all! Just continue on as normal, regardless."],[0,"Marcia：你简历上写着普通话流利。","Marcia: According to your CV you are fluent in Mandarin."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"你为什么想换工作？","Why do you want to move on?"],[0,"我把 WebWare 差不多当成一块跳板。","I see WebWare as kind of like a stepping stone."],[0,"你的野心我确实佩服。","I do admire your ambition!"],[0,"他不出力。","He wasn't pulling his weight."],[0,"那些啰嗦流程一概不做。","None of that rubbish."],[0,"能不能举个例子，你处理过特别难搞的下属？","Can you give an example of a time when you had to deal with a particularly difficult managee?"],[0,"市场变化很快，你会怎么应对？","How would you handle a rapidly changing market?"]]},{"cid":"bc06","title":"同一套问题，她每条都落在例子上","blocks":[[9,"莎拉接着面，题目和丹尼尔那场几乎一样：为什么换工作、怎么带合不来的下属、怎么应对不确定的市场。她的答法几乎每条都落在一个具体例子上，最后还反问公司的碳排放政策。可以拿上一集对照着听。","British Council · B1–B2 · 面试 / 行为问题"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：莎拉你好，我是玛西亚·博德曼，我们通过电话。","Marcia Boardman: Hi Sarah! I'm Marcia Boardman – we spoke on the phone."],[0,"Sarah：记得，那天我状态特别差！","Sarah: Oh yes, I remember – I was having a bad day!"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：这位是我们的 CEO 菲利普·哈特。","Marcia Boardman: And this is Philip Hart, our CEO."],[0,"Philip Hart：你好！","Philip Hart: Hello!"],[0,"Sarah：你好，很高兴见到两位。","Sarah: Hello, it's very nice to meet you both."],[0,"Philip Hart：你简历上写着你在做志愿服务。","Philip Hart: It says on your CV that you do voluntary work."],[0,"Sarah：有时间的时候会去。我在一个儿童机构帮忙，那里都是有些障碍的孩子。","Sarah: Well, when I have time, yes! I do work at a centre for children with difficulties, yes."],[0,"Philip Hart：那一定很有意思。","Philip Hart: That must be very interesting."],[0,"Sarah：很有意义，也挺难。","Sarah: It's rewarding and challenging."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：莎拉，能简单说说你现在的职位吗？","Marcia Boardman: Sarah, can you tell us a little bit about your current position?"],[0,"Sarah：我是一家连锁语言学校的销售副总监。","Sarah: I'm assistant sales director for a chain of language schools."],[0,"Philip Hart：那这个职位对你来说变化挺大。","Philip Hart: So this post would be quite a change then."],[0,"Sarah：说实话我不这么看，产品不一样，但要用的本事是一样的。","Sarah: I don't think so honestly, because the skills are the same, despite the product."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：那你为什么想换工作？","Marcia Boardman: Why are you thinking of moving on?"],[0,"Sarah：我在现在这个位置上已经走到头了，我今年 28，想多担一点责任。","Sarah: Well, I've come as far as I can in my current position, I feel, and I'm 28 now and would love to take on some more responsibility."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：好，我们说说带人。能不能举个例子，你处理过特别难搞的下属？","Marcia Boardman: OK, let's move on to managing people. Can you give us an example of when you had to deal with a particularly difficult managee?"],[0,"Sarah：有。我手下有两个人根本合不来，价值观不一样，性格也差得远，老是吵，看着根本没法一起干活。","Sarah: Well, yes, I had two people working for me who didn't get along at all – they had no shared values, different temperaments – and they used to argue a lot. It looked like it was impossible for them to work together."],[0,"Sarah：我就把他们叫来坐下来，把彼此的分歧和问题都摆开谈，之后事情就顺多了。","Sarah: So, I sat down with them, and we talked about their differences and their problems, and after that, things went much more smoothly."],[0,"Philip Hart：全球市场变化快又不确定，你会怎么应对？","Philip Hart: How would you deal with a rapidly changing and uncertain global market?"],[0,"Sarah：这个我正想在演示里讲。简单说就是保持灵活，把市场和销售策略都分散开。","Sarah: OK, that's actually something I wanted to talk about in my presentation, but I'd say to stay flexible and to diversify markets and sales strategies."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：你简历上写着你会法语和西班牙语。","Marcia Boardman: It says on your CV you speak French and Spanish."],[0,"Sarah：会。我在法国和西班牙都住过一阵。","Sarah: Yes, I do. I lived in both France and Spain for a while."],[0,"Philip Hart：还打算学别的语言吗？","Philip Hart: Any plans to learn other languages?"],[0,"Sarah：很想试试！","Sarah: I'd love to try!"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：能不能讲讲你拿下过的一笔特别难的生意？","Marcia Boardman: OK, can you tell us about a time you closed a particularly challenging deal?"],[0,"Sarah：我拿下最大的一个合同，也是我职业上最得意的一件事，是给印度一所很大的大学做语言培训。","Sarah: Well, the biggest contract I won – and the thing I'm most proud of professionally – was with a large university in India, to provide language training."],[0,"Sarah：合同里全是技术条款，客户又特别挑剔。不过我还是把它拿下来了。","Sarah: The contract was full of technicalities and the client was very picky! But I still pulled it off."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：好。你有什么想问我们的吗？","Marcia Boardman: OK. Do you have any questions for us?"],[0,"Sarah：有，关于你们的道德准则和碳排放。我想知道你们有没有减碳的计划，还有你们的产品是不是都来自合规的采购渠道？","Sarah: Yes – about your ethical policy and your carbon footprint. I was wondering whether you are planning to reduce your carbon footprint and whether all your products are ethically sourced?"],[0,"Philip Hart：这问题问得很好，这方面我们正在往那个方向走。","Philip Hart: That's a very good question, and that's something we're moving towards at the moment."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：好，那我们接着做演示吧。","Marcia Boardman: OK, well, let's move on to the presentation."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我在现在这个位置上已经走到头了。","I've come as far as I can in my current position."],[0,"我想多担一点责任。","I'd love to take on some more responsibility."],[0,"他们根本合不来。","They didn't get along at all."],[0,"之后事情就顺多了。","After that, things went much more smoothly."],[0,"客户特别挑剔，不过我还是把它拿下来了。","The client was very picky! But I still pulled it off."],[0,"你们的产品是不是都来自合规的采购渠道。","Whether all your products are ethically sourced."],[0,"这方面我们正在往那个方向走。","That's something we're moving towards at the moment."]]},{"cid":"bc07","title":"面试演示：浮夸派对上谨慎派","blocks":[[9,"面试最后一关是做一场短演示，题目是“WebWare 该往哪走，我能帮上什么”。丹尼尔把它讲成了自我推销，还放了首歌；莎拉拿出 SWOT 分析，句句都留余地。同一个题目两种路数，台下那两句“我们几天内联系你”也说得很不一样。","British Council · B2 · 面试演示"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Daniel：让我讲“WebWare 要往哪走，我能帮上什么”，我第一个念头很简单：我！","Daniel: When I was asked to do a presentation on 'Where WebWare is going, and what I can do to help it get there,' my first thought was simple: me!"],[0,"Daniel：你们也看到了，我技能很多，干这活要的那种性格我也有。","Daniel: As you've already seen, I've got a lot of skills, and the right kind of personality needed to do a job like this."],[0,"Daniel：这是我做的一页幻灯片！看到没，这是我的销售团队，他们可喜欢我了。我走他们肯定舍不得。","Daniel: Here's a slide I made! You see that – that's my sales team – they love me! Certainly going to be sad to see me leave."],[0,"Daniel：跳出框子想问题，这就是我的本事！","Daniel: Outside the box thinking – that's what I've got!"],[0,"Sarah：好。首先，我用手头能拿到的数据认真做了个 SWOT 分析，当然这些数据只是一部分。","Sarah: OK. To start with, I did a careful SWOT analysis using the data I had available, which is obviously only partial."],[0,"Sarah：我看的是竞争对手、线上曝光度、技术变化和研发这些方面。","Sarah: I looked at aspects such as competitors, online visibility, changing technologies and R&D."],[0,"Sarah：基于这些，我认为 WebWare 应该认真做一轮市场调研，加强在次级市场的品牌认知，同时让报价更有弹性。","Sarah: On the basis of this, I believe WebWare should carry out some careful market research, strengthen its brand awareness in secondary markets, and improve the flexibility of its offer."],[0,"Sarah：如果这些见了效，我觉得维持高定价策略是有可能的。","Sarah: If this produces positive results, I think it should be possible to maintain the premium pricing policy."],[0,"Daniel：这是我上一份工作的销售数据，全靠我！这叫天马行空地想！","Daniel: Here's the sales figures for the last job I did – all down to me! Blue sky thinking!"],[0,"Daniel：最后，作为演示的结尾，我给你们放一首我自己写的歌。","Daniel: Finally, to finish my presentation, I'd like to play you a song I wrote."],[0,"Philip Hart：行了行了，可以了。谢谢你，丹尼尔。","Philip Hart: OK, OK. That's enough. Thanks, Daniel."],[0,"Daniel：太好了！这是不是说这工作是我的了？","Daniel: Great! So does that mean I've got the job?"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：我们五天内会联系你，告诉你结果。","Marcia Boardman: We'll be in touch over the next five days to let you know."],[0,"Daniel：好，太好了，谢谢。","Daniel: OK, great, thank you."],[0,"Sarah：我预计的销售走势大概是这样。我得强调一下，这些目前还只是推测。","Sarah: This is how I'd predict a sales pattern would go. I have to emphasise these are only speculative results at the moment."],[0,"Sarah：关键词是三个：谨慎、适应力，还有把主力产品线做扎实，也就是 WebWare 的“现金牛”。","Sarah: The key words are: caution, adaptability, and consolidation of main product lines – WebWare's 'cash cows,' if you like."],[0,"Sarah：既要灵活，又得让人信得过，这很重要。","Sarah: It's important to be flexible, yet reliable."],[0,"Sarah：还有一点，你们线上订单的交货时间得缩短。希望这些我说清楚了。你们有问题吗？","Sarah: Oh, and another thing is you need to improve the delivery times on your online orders! I hope all that's clear. Do you have any questions?"],[0,"Philip Hart：没有，谢谢你莎拉，说得很清楚，你这一讲让我们要想的东西不少。","Philip Hart: No, thank you Sarah – that's all very clear – you've given us quite a lot to think about there!"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：对，非常感谢莎拉。我们过几天会联系你，通知这次任命的结果。","Marcia Boardman: Yes, thanks a lot Sarah. We'll be in touch over the next few days to let you know about the appointment."],[0,"Sarah：谢谢两位抽时间，很高兴见到你们。","Sarah: Thank you both for your time. It's been a pleasure meeting both of you."],[0,"Philip Hart / Marcia Boardman：再见！","Philip Hart / Marcia Boardman: Bye!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我们五天内会联系你。","We'll be in touch over the next five days."],[0,"跳出框子想问题，这就是我的本事。","Outside the box thinking – that's what I've got."],[0,"天马行空地想！","Blue sky thinking!"],[0,"全靠我！","All down to me!"],[0,"我得强调，这些目前还只是推测。","I have to emphasise these are only speculative results."],[0,"认真做一轮市场调研。","Carry out some careful market research."],[0,"你这一讲让我们要想的东西不少。","You've given us quite a lot to think about."]]},{"cid":"bc08","title":"两个人选一个：简历好看未必行","blocks":[[9,"面试结束，菲利普和玛西亚关起门来比对两位候选人：简历、临场表现、肢体语言、答得实不实。这段最值得学的是英语里怎么评价一个人——褒和贬都留了分寸，用词却一点不含糊。","British Council · B1–B2 · 招聘 / 录用决策"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Philip：你觉得怎么样？","Philip: So, what did you think?"],[0,"Marcia：莎拉·蒂姆斯和丹尼尔·沃森之间，我觉得选谁挺明显的！","Marcia: Well, between Sarah Timms and Daniel Watson, I think the choice is pretty obvious!"],[0,"Philip：我也这么想。沃森纸面上看着特别好。","Philip: Yes, so do I. Watson looked so good on paper."],[0,"Marcia：可我第一次跟他通电话，也觉得他挺好。","Marcia: But he seemed very good when I first spoke to him too."],[0,"Philip：第一印象经常骗人！","Philip: First impressions often lie!"],[0,"Marcia：确实。我觉得他简历上很多东西，怎么说呢，跟事实有出入。","Marcia: Indeed. I think a lot of his CV was – how shall we say? Counterfactual."],[0,"Philip：对，就是假的。简历上绝对不能撒谎！","Philip: Yes. It just wasn't true. You should never lie on your CV!"],[0,"Marcia：不过他的推荐信很好，挺奇怪的。","Marcia: He had very good references, though. Very strange."],[0,"Philip：可能有人就吃这一套，但他跟我们合不来。自信是好事，可他是自信过头了。","Philip: I guess some people just like that sort of style, but he wouldn't fit in with us. I mean, it's important to be confident but he was overconfident."],[0,"Marcia：我完全同意。他的肢体语言全错了，给人的感觉就是傲慢。","Marcia: I couldn't agree more. His body language was all wrong. He came across as arrogant."],[0,"Philip：而且他回答得很空，具体干了什么一点细节都没有。","Philip: Then he gave very vague answers – no specific details of what exactly he'd done in his job."],[0,"Marcia：莎拉·蒂姆斯就不一样……","Marcia: Whereas Sarah Timms…"],[0,"Philip：……她说每句话心里都有底。","Philip: …knew exactly what she was talking about."],[0,"Marcia：对，很有说服力，很自信，但不傲慢。","Marcia: Yes, she was very convincing, self-assured, but not arrogant."],[0,"Philip：她显然研究过我们公司，说话是有根据的。","Philip: She'd clearly done some research on the company and knew what she was talking about."],[0,"Marcia：她那场演示我觉得非常好。","Marcia: Oh, I thought her presentation was excellent."],[0,"Philip：是很好。不过我有点担心她的经验够不够。","Philip: Yes, it was. But I am a little worried about how much experience she has."],[0,"Marcia：这倒是，不过她看起来挺愿意接这个岗位给她的挑战。","Marcia: Yes, true, but she seems very ready to take on the challenges the role would offer her."],[0,"Philip：那这工作给谁？","Philip: So, who do we give the job to?"],[0,"Marcia：莎拉！","Marcia: Sarah!"],[0,"Philip：我完全赞成！","Philip: Yes, I agree entirely!"],[0,"Marcia：好，我马上打电话给她发 offer，再给沃森先生写封拒信。","Marcia: Great! I'll phone her straight away offering the post and I'll write a rejection to Mr Watson."],[0,"Philip：好。","Philip: OK."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"他纸面上看着特别好。","He looked so good on paper."],[0,"第一印象经常骗人！","First impressions often lie!"],[0,"怎么说呢，跟事实有出入。","How shall we say? Counterfactual."],[0,"他跟我们合不来。","He wouldn't fit in with us."],[0,"他给人的感觉就是傲慢。","He came across as arrogant."],[0,"我完全同意。","I couldn't agree more."],[0,"她看起来挺愿意接这些挑战。","She seems very ready to take on the challenges."]]},{"cid":"bc09","title":"拒信怎么写得体面又不空","blocks":[[9,"有人已经口头答应入职，另一位还在等消息，玛西亚得亲手写这封拒信。她一边念一边改，菲利普在旁边把关语气：怎么把“你没戏了”说得体面，还得给出一条真能用的反馈。想学坏消息表达的，这段几乎是逐句示范。","British Council · B1–B2 · 拒信 / 委婉表达"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：好，好，太好了！我们很欢迎你加入！下周见！拜拜！","Marcia Boardman: OK. OK. That's great! We'll be pleased to have you on the team! Looking forward to seeing you next week! Bye!"],[0,"Philip Hart：是莎拉吗？","Philip Hart: Was that Sarah?"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：是，她答应来了，说想下周过来聊聊。","Marcia Boardman: Yes – she's going to accept the job, and wants to come in next week for a chat."],[0,"Philip Hart：好消息。现在你只需要告诉另一位，我们不要他。","Philip Hart: Great news. Now you just have to tell the other guy that we don't want him."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：我最讨厌说坏消息。","Marcia Boardman: I hate giving bad news."],[0,"Philip Hart：幸好这是你的活，不是我的！","Philip Hart: I'm glad that it's your job and not mine!"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：行，那干脆现在就做。尊敬的沃森先生，很遗憾地通知您，您没有得到这个职位。嗯，听着太直了。","Marcia Boardman: OK, may as well do it straightaway. 'Dear Mr Watson, we regret to inform you that you have not got the job.' Hmm, sounds a bit too direct."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：这样呢：尊敬的沃森先生，感谢您应聘 WebWare。很遗憾地通知您，您未能入选。","Marcia Boardman: How about: 'Dear Mr Watson, Thank you for your application to WebWare. We regret to inform you that you weren't successful.'"],[0,"Philip Hart：我觉得你该说点肯定的。","Philip Hart: Hmm. I think you should say something positive."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：可他表现得一塌糊涂！","Marcia Boardman: But he was terrible!"],[0,"Philip Hart：是不怎么样，但我觉得还是得正面一点、客气一点。","Philip Hart: Well, he wasn't great, no, but I think we should be positive and polite."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：你说得对。那这样：尊敬的沃森先生，感谢您应聘 WebWare。您是一位有潜力的候选人。但很遗憾，这个职位的竞争非常激烈，我们不会向您提供该职位。谨此，等等等等。","Marcia Boardman: Yes, you're absolutely right. OK, how about this: 'Dear Mr Watson, Thank you for your application to WebWare. You were a promising candidate. However, we regret to inform you that the competition for the post was very strong, and we will not be offering you the position. Yours sincerely, etc. etc.'"],[0,"Philip Hart：对，这样说就好多了。不过还得加点反馈。","Philip Hart: Yes, that's more like it. But we should include some feedback."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：当然。我加一句这个怎么样：以后建议您把个人风格收敛一些，并仔细核对简历里的事实。听着如何？","Marcia Boardman: Of course. How about if I add this: 'In future, you may wish to moderate your personal style, and carefully fact check your CV.' How does that sound?"],[0,"Philip Hart：我不太确定“把个人风格收敛一些”是什么意思，有点含糊。","Philip Hart: I'm not sure what 'moderate your personal style' means. It's a bit vague."],[0,"Marcia Boardman：那改成“多举一些具体的成绩例子，并体现你如何与人合作”，怎么样？","Marcia Boardman: Hmm. OK, how about 'give more specific examples of your achievements, and show how you work as part of a team'?"],[0,"Philip Hart：行，这个我喜欢。还有，结尾记得加一句“祝您今后一切顺利”！","Philip Hart: OK, yes, I like that. And remember to finish with something like, 'We wish you the best of luck in the future'!"],[0,"Marcia Boardman：那当然，我是真心祝他好运！好，写完了，我这就发。","Marcia Boardman: Of course – I certainly do wish him luck! OK. Done. I'll send it now."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"很遗憾地通知您，您未能入选。","We regret to inform you that you weren't successful."],[0,"您是一位有潜力的候选人，不过……","You were a promising candidate. However…"],[0,"这个职位的竞争非常激烈。","The competition for the post was very strong."],[0,"这样说就好多了。","That's more like it."],[0,"建议您把个人风格收敛一些。","You may wish to moderate your personal style."],[0,"仔细核对简历里的事实。","Carefully fact check your CV."],[0,"祝您今后一切顺利。","We wish you the best of luck in the future."]]},{"cid":"bc10","title":"签合同前：薪资、奖金、入职日","blocks":[[9,"入职前莎拉专门约玛西亚面谈，说有“一两个细节”想聊：为什么是宽带薪酬、奖金能不能补上、年假、还有入职时间。她每提一个要求都先给理由，被挡回来就换一条路走。看一个候选人怎么不撕破脸也把条件谈下来。","British Council · B1–B2 · 录用通知 / 薪酬谈判"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Marcia：你好，欢迎来 WebWare。","Marcia: Hi! Welcome to WebWare."],[0,"Sarah：谢谢，很高兴又见面。","Sarah: Thanks. Nice to see you again."],[0,"Marcia：我也是。你说入职前想过来聊聊。","Marcia: You too. So you said you wanted to come in and have a chat before you started."],[0,"Sarah：对，我想四处看看，顺便再问几个问题，如果可以的话。","Sarah: Yeah, I just wanted to have a look around and ask a few more questions, if I can."],[0,"Marcia：当然，尽管问！","Marcia: Sure, fire away!"],[0,"Sarah：收到这个 offer 我特别高兴。","Sarah: Well, I was delighted to receive the job offer."],[0,"Marcia：我们也特别高兴把它给你。","Marcia: Good. We were delighted to offer it to you."],[0,"Sarah：不过签合同之前，有一两个细节我想谈谈。","Sarah: But before I sign the contract there were one or two specifics I wanted to talk about."],[0,"Marcia：好，什么细节？","Marcia: OK, 'specifics'?"],[0,"Sarah：薪资是按薪级走，不是固定数？","Sarah: Well, there's a pay scale, instead of a fixed salary?"],[0,"Marcia：对，新员工都在薪级的下端。","Marcia: Yes, as a new employee you'd be at the lower end of the pay scale."],[0,"Sarah：可要是考虑我的经验……","Sarah: But taking my experience into account…"],[0,"Marcia：你的经验其实不算多。我们把你当成一项投资。","Marcia: Well, you haven't had that much experience. We see you as an investment."],[0,"Sarah：可这个数比我现在的收入只多一点。","Sarah: But that salary would only be a little more than I'm making now."],[0,"Sarah：所以我不要求往薪级上挪，我想能不能用奖金补回来。比如我完成了销售指标，甚至超额完成，我希望能拿到一笔像样的现金奖励或者公司期权。","Sarah: So, instead of asking for a higher level on the pay scale, I thought this could be compensated by adding certain bonuses. For instance, if I make certain sales targets, or even break them, I would be looking for a good cash payment or stock options in the company."],[0,"Marcia：这个我们有时候会给高层，不过为了表示诚意，我可以先初步答应你奖金方案，但得先跟菲利普确认。","Marcia: Well, that is something we sometimes offer senior members of staff, but to show good faith I'll provisionally offer you the bonus scheme, but I'll have to OK it with Philip first."],[0,"Sarah：行。我还看到年假是 25 天。","Sarah: That's fine. I also see that there are 25 days' holiday."],[0,"Marcia：对，这是标准。","Marcia: Yes. That's standard."],[0,"Sarah：可这么高压的岗位，这不算多。","Sarah: It's not very much for a high-pressure job, though."],[0,"Marcia：年假我这边加不了。","Marcia: I can't offer you any more holiday."],[0,"Sarah：那倒不用，我在想能不能把入职时间往后推，原来说好一周后，我能不能一个月后再来？","Sarah: No, but I was wondering if we could delay my start date, so instead of starting a week from now, as we discussed, I could start in a month's time?"],[0,"Marcia：莎拉，你谈判可真硬！","Marcia: You're a tough negotiator, Sarah!"],[0,"Sarah：这也是你们请我的原因之一啊！","Sarah: That's one of the reasons you hired me!"],[0,"Marcia：那倒是。行，这个可以。那一个月后见，也等着你把奖金挣到手！","Marcia: Yes, of course. OK, I think we can do that. I'll look forward to seeing you in a month and earning those bonuses!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"当然，尽管问！","Sure, fire away!"],[0,"有一两个细节我想谈谈。","There were one or two specifics I wanted to talk about."],[0,"可要是考虑我的经验……","But taking my experience into account…"],[0,"我们把你当成一项投资。","We see you as an investment."],[0,"为了表示诚意。","To show good faith."],[0,"我得先跟菲利普确认。","I'll have to OK it with Philip first."],[0,"你谈判可真硬！","You're a tough negotiator!"]]},{"cid":"bc11","title":"入职第一天：工位、午饭、例会","blocks":[[9,"莎拉第一天上班，菲利普和玛西亚带她看办公室、聊团队、过日程。全是寒暄和琐事，可这正是入职第一天最常听到的那一整套话：欢迎、工位、午饭、例会。适合拿来当口语素材，成句背。","British Council · B1 · 入职 / 办公环境"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Philip：莎拉，又见面了！欢迎加入。","Philip: Sarah, good to meet you again! Welcome on board."],[0,"Sarah：谢谢菲利普，我很高兴能来。","Sarah: Thanks, Philip. I'm very pleased to be here."],[0,"Philip：假期过得不错吧？去哪儿了？","Philip: I hope you enjoyed your holiday. Where did you go?"],[0,"Sarah：去了泰国，特别好，海滩漂亮，吃的也好。","Sarah: I went to Thailand. It was lovely – great beaches and lovely food."],[0,"Philip：真羡慕你！不过现在该干活了！","Philip: Oh, lucky you! It's time for hard work now, though!"],[0,"Sarah：我准备好了！","Sarah: I'm ready for it!"],[0,"Marcia：我带你去你的办公室。","Marcia: Let me show you to your office."],[0,"Sarah：我都不知道自己有单独办公室！你们这儿不用轮用座位？","Sarah: Didn't know I have my own office! So, you don't hot-desk here?"],[0,"Marcia：你看，大部分人都是轮着坐的，不过我们觉得你需要一块自己的地方。","Marcia: Well, most people do, as you can see, but we thought you'd need all your own private space."],[0,"Sarah：对，尤其是要直接见客户。","Sarah: Yes, especially if you're meeting clients directly."],[0,"Marcia：不过因为是大开间，气氛其实挺随意的。","Marcia: But the atmosphere is actually quite informal because it's open-plan."],[0,"Sarah：那挺好，我喜欢。能感觉到大家都很忙！","Sarah: Oh, that's good. I like that. You definitely get the sense of everyone being really busy!"],[0,"Philip：但愿如此！","Philip: Yes, they are, I hope!"],[0,"Marcia：这就是你的位置了！","Marcia: So, this is your space!"],[0,"Sarah：哇，真不错，地方很大！我上一个办公室小多了。","Sarah: Wow! Great, lots of space! My last office was much smaller."],[0,"Philip：你在那边带多少人？","Philip: How many people did you work with there?"],[0,"Sarah：三个人。","Sarah: I had a team of three."],[0,"Philip：这儿你手下有六个人。午饭之后我们带你去见销售团队。","Philip: Well, here you'll have six people under you. We'll introduce you to your sales team after lunch."],[0,"Sarah：听着不错。你们午饭一般怎么解决？","Sarah: Hmm, that sounds good. What do you usually do for lunch?"],[0,"Marcia：有人自己带饭，不过一楼有食堂。饭做得挺好，还挺便宜！","Marcia: Oh, well, some people bring it in, but there's a canteen on the ground floor. Food's actually quite good and pretty cheap!"],[0,"Sarah：不错。","Sarah: Great."],[0,"Philip：那我说说你的日程。每周一有销售和市场会，周四下午跟各部门负责人碰一次头，就是让大家对一下进度。","Philip: Now then, I'll tell you about your schedule. There's a sales and marketing meeting every Monday, as well as a meet-up with various heads of department on Thursday afternoons, just so we know what we're doing."],[0,"Marcia：除此之外，时间怎么安排你自己定。","Marcia: Other than that, how you organise your time is up to you."],[0,"Sarah：行，我时间管理还行！","Sarah: That's fine. I'm a good time manager!"],[0,"Philip：那我们就不打扰你了！","Philip: We'll leave you to it, then!"],[0,"Sarah：我觉得我会喜欢在这儿干！","Sarah: I think I'm going to like working here!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"欢迎加入。","Welcome on board."],[0,"真羡慕你！","Lucky you!"],[0,"你们这儿不用轮用座位？","You don't hot-desk here?"],[0,"你手下有六个人。","You'll have six people under you."],[0,"时间怎么安排你自己定。","How you organise your time is up to you."],[0,"那我们就不打扰你了！","We'll leave you to it, then!"],[0,"就是让大家对一下进度。","Just so we know what we're doing."]]}]},{"bookId":"biz4","title":"职场表达","sub":"同事、老板、会议室里的说法","chapters":[{"cid":"bb03","title":"第一次见客户，开口该多正式","blocks":[[9,"同一句话，正式版和随意版，效果差很远。这段按打招呼、提请求、下指令三道关过一遍，每关都给两种说法。留意他们判断该用哪一版，看的不是对方职位高低，而是场合和你跟这个人的关系。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 正式与随意"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Pippa：工作中该多正式？","Pippa: How formal should we be at work?"],[0,"Neil：我觉得关键在场合，而不在语言本身多正式。","Neil: I think it's more about the context than how formal the language should be."],[0,"Georgie：跟天天见的同事，其实可以随便些，因为跟天天见面的人说话还端着，太累了。","Georgie: I think with colleagues that you spend a lot of time with, you have a bit more freedom to be informal because it takes a lot of effort to be formal with people you see all the time."],[0,"Neil：跟同事处得不错，只是聊聊周末，那当然可以用一些你跟老板开会时不会说的说法。","Neil: If you get on quite well with your colleagues and you're just having a chat about the weekend, then of course you can speak using language you wouldn't use in a meeting with your boss."],[0,"Phil：好，先从打招呼和介绍开始。假设你因为工作要见一个陌生人，可能是开会。这时候该多正式？","Phil: OK, let's start with greetings and introductions. Let's imagine you're meeting somebody new as part of your job, maybe for a meeting. How formal should you be?"],[0,"Pippa：菲尔，这看场合。你得先想清楚见的是谁。这人有多重要？之前发过邮件吗，还是头一次见？他对这次见面有没有什么期待？可能是自己公司的人，那公司内部说话本来就有套路。也可能是别家公司的人，而那家你知道挺正式。这些都会影响你怎么开口。正式一点就是，早上好，很高兴见到您。","Pippa: Well, it depends on the context, Phil. You might want to think about the person you're meeting. How important are they? Have you emailed before, or is this the first time you're meeting them? Maybe do they have any expectations from the meeting? So maybe they're someone from within your organisation and there's certain ways that people talk to each other at your organisation. Maybe they're from a different business that you know is quite formal. That will change how you greet them. A formal greeting would be to say something like, 'Good morning. Nice to meet you.'"],[0,"Phil：对。对天天一起干活的人就可以随便点，一句嘿，最近怎么样就行。","Phil: Yes. With people that you work with every day, you might be more informal and just say something like, 'hey, how are you doing?'"],[0,"Pippa：对。或者很高兴认识你。从最正式到最随意，中间有好多版本。有时候对着很重要的人，也能用挺随意的说法。关键是你得看懂自己处在什么场面。","Pippa: Yeah. Or 'great to meet you.' There are kind of lots of different versions that go from the most formal to the least formal. And so you can use quite informal language even with important people sometimes. It's just trying to understand the situation you're in."],[0,"Pippa：菲尔，英国职场一般用称谓吗？就是叫先生、女士，或者叫伯德先生而不是直接叫菲尔？","Pippa: Now, Phil, do we tend to use titles in British workplaces? So that's saying sir or madam or calling someone Mr. Bird rather than just Phil?"],[0,"Phil：大多数英国职场我觉得不常见。也有例外。哪儿会不一样？","Phil: I don't think it's that common in most British workplaces. There are some exceptions. And where might it be different, Pippa?"],[0,"Pippa：在一些专业场合，比如医院，医生一般叫某某医生加姓；警队里几乎都按级别称呼。写字楼里其实不太这样，一般都是直接叫名字。","Pippa: Well, in more sort of professional contexts, such as in a hospital, doctors are often referred to as doctor and then their surname, in maybe the police force people would refer to people almost by their rank within the organisation. It's not so common in offices, really. We would tend to just use people's first names."],[0,"Phil：不光行业和公司不一样，国家之间也不一样。你会发现有些国家的人讲英语时更爱用称谓。","Phil: And as well as different industries or different companies, this can vary between different countries as well. So you might find that in other countries they're more likely to use titles when they're speaking English."],[0,"Pippa：好，换个场景。你在工作中要提个请求，比如请人帮你手上的项目。咱们说说正式和随意的两种说法？","Pippa: OK. Let's think about another scenario. You need to make a request at work, perhaps for some help on a project you're working on. Shall we talk about some formal and informal options, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：有些说法我们更常在正式场合用。比如，我能否请求，这个有没有可能，你这边还有余力吗？","Phil: Yeah. So there are just some expressions that we tend to use more in formal contexts. Things like 'could I request', 'would it be possible?', 'Do you have spare capacity?'"],[0,"Pippa：你想想，这些话我们跟朋友家人根本不会用。你不会看着饭桌说，我今晚的饭局还有些余量，您是否愿意出席？没人这么说话。","Pippa: And when you think about it, these are just not expressions we'd use with our friends and family. You wouldn't look at your dining table and go, oh, 'I have some spare capacity for my dinner party tonight. Would you like to attend?' It's just not how we'd say it."],[0,"Phil：对，就是这样。随意的说法可以是，能占用你一下吗？或者，你有空吗？有没有可能帮我个忙？这些都松一些。你可以想象跟朋友说，能借你一分钟吗？或者，有空聊两句吗？就是没那么绷着。","Phil: Yeah, exactly. So some informal alternatives would be saying something like, oh, 'could I borrow you?' or 'do you have a minute?' 'Is there a chance that you could help me?' These are all a little bit more informal. You can imagine saying to your friend, 'could I borrow you for a minute?' or 'are you free to chat?' They're just a little bit more relaxed."],[0,"Phil：跟正式不正式、客气不客气有关的事，永远看你们公司的氛围。你跟人熟不熟？大家默认你该怎么做？这些是你得跟着来的。还是那句话，先看别人怎么做，学着来。","Phil: As always, with things about formality and politeness, it depends on the context of your company. How well do you know people? What do people expect you to do? That's the kind of thing you need to follow. Again, look to see how other people do it and try to do something similar."],[0,"Pippa：请求说完了。那指令呢？该正式还是随意？","Pippa: So that's requests. But what about instructions? Should these be formal or informal, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：正式的指令分两种。有时候是特别客气、特别正式的结构，但可能反而不够清楚。也有时候特别直接，跟路牌似的全是祈使句，这种你肯定不能跟朋友说，会得罪人。","Phil: Formal instructions can vary because sometimes we have very polite, very formal structures which can perhaps not be that clear. But then also sometimes we have really direct instructions, almost like a road sign with lots of imperatives, which again, you probably wouldn't say to your friends because you wouldn't want to annoy them."],[0,"Pippa：正式但客气的说法是，我们希望您周二来办公室。而正式又直接的说法就是——","Pippa: So, a formal but polite way of giving an instruction would be to say something like, 'we would ask that you come into the office on Tuesdays'. But a formal, direct way of saying that would be..."],[0,"Phil：周二到办公室是强制要求。","Phil: 'Attendance at the office on Tuesdays is mandatory.'"],[0,"Pippa：这两句都正式，但感觉不一样。正式指令里还有一类很常见的，就是带 please 的，比如，请注意……想想我们说的朋友家人那个例子，你不会跟朋友说请注意。那随意的指令呢？什么时候用？","Pippa: Now, these are both formal ways of putting it, but they have a slightly different feel. Another really kind of common thing to see in formal instructions is things like please, saying something like, 'please be mindful that...' Let's think back to our sort of friends and family example. You wouldn't really say, please be mindful, to your friends. What about informal instructions? When would you use informal instructions, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：随意的指令是对朋友家人用的，也用于你很熟的同事。可以用，你要做的是……我一般是……我发现最好是……这类说法。就是松一点的指令。","Phil: So yes, informal instructions are what you'd use with your friends and family, but also with people you work with who you know quite well. We can have expressions like 'what you want to do is...' 'I tend to...', 'I've found it's best to...' things like that. They're just an informal way of giving instructions."],[0,"Pippa：对。口头带人、随口讲两句的时候很好用。前面那些正式说法，更适合写在邮件里，或者写进给一群人看的指南里。","Pippa: Yeah. And these could be useful if you're giving spoken instructions or training to a colleague if you're chatting about something. Whereas those formal examples we gave earlier, they might be more suited to an email or a guide that you're writing down and you're giving to lots of people in a more formal context."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"你这边还有余力吗？","Do you have spare capacity?"],[0,"能占用你一分钟吗？","Could I borrow you for a minute?"],[0,"有空聊两句吗？","Are you free to chat?"],[0,"这个有没有可能？","Would it be possible?"],[0,"我们希望您周二来办公室。","We would ask that you come into the office on Tuesdays."],[0,"周二到办公室是强制要求。","Attendance at the office on Tuesdays is mandatory."],[0,"请注意……","Please be mindful that..."],[0,"我发现最好是……","I've found it's best to..."]]},{"cid":"bb04","title":"跟老板提想法，别说成抱怨","blocks":[[9,"会上冒出一个想法，说早了怕被笑，说晚了怕被人抢先。这段讲怎么把想法递出去：先抛个软的、再补一句免责，然后一步步做成能落地的东西。注意那些降调的说法，既让话出口，又不给自己挖坑。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 提想法"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Pippa：工作中分享想法，最好的方式是什么？","Pippa: What's the best way to share ideas at work?"],[0,"Georgie：想点子我一般先自己闷头想。然后再找几个人一起把想法做深，这样有帮助。","Georgie: To come up with ideas, I usually start by myself. It's helpful to then get some other people to develop your ideas."],[0,"Becca：我喜欢听周围人聊，比如开会的时候。然后我会去听里面缺了什么。","Becca: I like to listen to conversations around me, maybe in meetings. What I'll then do is try and hear for things that could be missing."],[0,"Pippa：菲尔，你喜欢在工作中想点子吗？","Pippa: Do you enjoy coming up with ideas at work, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：喜欢，我觉得这在我们这行挺重要的。","Phil: I do, and I think it's quite a big thing in our job."],[0,"Pippa：我个人其实挺喜欢聊想法，但如果有人逼着你必须想出个点子，我就特别紧张。","Pippa: I actually, I personally do like talking about ideas, but I find it really stressful if there's a lot of pressure to come up with an idea."],[0,"Phil：你觉得一个人想容易，还是跟别人一起想容易？","Phil: Do you find it easier to come up with ideas yourself or working together with other people?"],[0,"Pippa：肯定是跟别人一起。","Pippa: Definitely working together with other people."],[0,"Phil：我说不好。我觉得一个人想馊主意可能更容易，但几个人一起，就能把想法打磨出来，做出真能用的东西。","Phil: I don't know. I think I might find it easier to come up with bad ideas on my own, but I think when you work together with other people, you can refine them and come up with something that actually works."],[0,"Pippa：好，先从想点子说起。假设你在团队会上，老板问大家对下一个项目有什么想法。这时候怎么把想法说出来最好？","Pippa: OK. Let's start with coming up with ideas. Let's imagine you're at a team meeting Phil, and your boss has asked everyone about their ideas for an upcoming project. What's the best way to share your ideas?"],[0,"Phil：首先，把脑子里的东西都说出来就好。我一直在想……或者，我有个想法……或者，要不咱们……就是在提一些可能可行的方案。","Phil: Well, first, it's probably good just to say all the things you've got in your head. 'I've been thinking...' Or 'one idea I had...' Or 'how about...' you're making suggestions of things that might be possible."],[0,"Pippa：对，这也看场合。可能人家让你提前准备，也可能是很松的闲聊。要是后者，你不一定非得提方案，可以先问问题。比如，优先级是什么？我们有哪些限制？这样大家反而更清楚要什么，也更容易想到自己的点子。","Pippa: Yeah, and it depends on the context and how you'll talk about ideas. So you might have been asked to prepare ideas in advance or this might be a more relaxed, informal discussion. And if it's the latter you could just ask some questions rather than kind of suggesting things. So you can ask things like 'what's the priority?' 'What limitations do we have?' And that kind of helps everyone kind of understand more about what's required and think about their own ideas."],[0,"Phil：对，这样想出来的点子更贴，因为是在那个框架里想。","Phil: Yes, it can help you come up with ideas that are more suitable or more appropriate because they fit into that framework."],[0,"Pippa：对。有时候聊开了，想法自己就冒出来了，我个人的体会是这样。这种时候你可以先说一句，这只是我随口一说，或者，我就是边说边想，然后再讲。你觉得呢？","Pippa: Yeah. And sometimes ideas come more naturally once the conversation begins. That's what I find personally. And so if that happens, you can say things like, oh, 'this is just off the top of my head', or 'I'm just thinking out loud here' before you introduce your idea. What do you think about that, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：我觉得挺好。如果氛围好，什么都能说、说了还能一起改，那这类话很有用。但随口说出来的东西，本来就没深想过，可能就是馊主意。有些场合你也不希望被当成老出馊主意的那个人。所以还是看你们那儿的气氛和文化。","Phil: I like them. And I think if you're in a good environment where you can say anything and work with it, then they can be quite good. But obviously ideas that just come off the top of your head are not things that you've necessarily thought about that deeply. So they might be bad ideas. And it could be that in some situations you don't want to be seen as the person who's coming up with bad ideas. And so that might depend on the atmosphere and the culture where you work."],[0,"Phil：好，分享说完了。接下来是把一个想法做深，就是拿一个初步的点子再讨论、再往下想。你觉得最好的做法是什么？","Phil: OK, we've talked about how to share ideas, but next we might want to develop an idea. And this means that you take an initial idea and discuss or think about it further. What do you think is the best approach?"],[0,"Pippa：有时候就在讨论中间做。有人讲了个想法，你有话要说，那就先问问题。先确认自己有没有听懂。你可以说，你的意思是不是我们……然后把你理解的讲出来；也可以直接提，要不我们这样？","Pippa: Well, sometimes you might want to do this in the middle of the discussion. So, someone's talked about an idea and you have things to say about it. So, you might ask some questions. So, you could just sort of check that you understand the idea. You'd say something like 'are you thinking we would...?' and then sort of say what you are imagining, or you could suggest something: 'what if we do this?'"],[0,"Phil：还有，对别人的想法先表示兴奋，再往上加东西，这样挺好。","Phil: And it's good to be enthusiastic about someone's idea and then build on it, I think."],[0,"Pippa：对。但也得想里面的漏洞和问题，因为你是在帮人家补。可以说，这个你考虑过吗，或者，这点我们怎么处理？还有个常用的招，就是我先唱个反调。","Pippa: Yes. But also we need to think about the holes or the problems because, well, you're helping someone fix them. So it could be, 'Have you thought about this or how will we deal with this?' And then there's a technique we use. We say, oh 'I'm just going to play devil's advocate'."],[0,"Phil：对。另一种说法是给这个想法做个压力测试。意思就是看它在实际中行不行，扛不扛得住各种问题和考验。","Phil: Yeah. Another way we can phrase is to talk about stress testing an idea. And that means basically, seeing whether an idea will work in practice, will it stand up to lots of different problems and tests?"],[0,"Pippa：还可以说换个帽子看看，就是站在不同角色的人的角度，看这事是什么样。","Pippa: You can also say that you might want to look at something with different hats on, to try and see how it might look to people doing different roles."],[0,"Phil：比如你可以说，这个想法我喜欢，但站在市场的角度，我担心怎么推。","Phil: So for example, you might say, 'I like this idea, but with my marketing hat on, I'm worried about how we would promote it.'"],[0,"Pippa：有时候讨论完了，你才想到一些东西，或者有些话在会上不方便说，那就事后找人聊。你可以说，我想接着你那个想法说两句，或者，我一直在想你那个想法，或者，我刚想到一点。","Pippa: Sometimes when you've been discussing an idea, there might be things that you didn't think of or you didn't feel you could say in the meeting, so you might want to speak to someone afterwards. You might say, oh, 'just to follow up on your idea', or 'I've been thinking about your idea' or 'something occurred to me'."],[0,"Phil：对，这些说法都能让人看出你确实想过他说的话，然后顺着往下加一句，把话接下去。","Phil: Yeah, those are all really nice ways to show that you've been thinking about what someone said and then just add to it, carry on the conversation."],[0,"Phil：好，分享和做深都说了。可一旦定了，怎么保证这个想法真能落地？","Phil: OK, we've talked about sharing and developing ideas, but once a decision has been made, how do we make sure that an idea actually happens?"],[0,"Pippa：要排的第一样就是时间。有没有必须完成的日子？有没有哪一步得等前一步？所以得把时间线拉出来：什么到什么时候做完，什么时候回头对进度。","Pippa: Yes. I mean, one of the things that you need to map out, you'll think about, are the timelines. Is there a deadline that something needs to be done by? Are there some things that depend on other things, other things that need to happen first? So you probably want to plan out your timeline. What needs to be done by when and when are you going to check in on things?"],[0,"Phil：这时候还会听到一个行话，deliverables，交付物。就是这个想法最后要做成什么东西。可能是一份演示、一个产品，也可能是一整场活动。所以你可以问，交付物是什么？其实就是把这事最终变成什么定下来。","Phil: Another piece of jargon that you might hear at this point in the discussion is deliverables. So the deliverables are the results of what you're going to do, what you're going to make. So for example, it might be a presentation or it might be a product or it might be a whole campaign. So you might ask 'what are the deliverables?' And that's just agreeing what this idea is going to become in reality."],[0,"Pippa：到这一步通常要定谁负责哪块。可能还有一个人总负责，确保这事真办成，这叫由他 take ownership，或者把项目 ownership 交给某人。如果是一个部门或团队，也可以说，我觉得这个项目放在市场部，或者财务部，用 sit within 这个说法，意思就是他们管。","Pippa: Often at this point, you'll decide who's responsible for certain things. And there may be one person who's responsible overall for making sure that something happens. And you say they take ownership of it or you give ownership of the project to someone. You can also say if you're talking about a department or a team, you can say, 'I think this project will sit within the marketing team' or the finance team, so we can use that expression, sit within. It just means they're the people who are in charge of it."],[0,"Phil：还得说眼下马上要做什么。这里就是 action points，行动项：这次聊完，为了让项目起步，我们各自要做什么？还有 next steps，下一步。团队常说，一周后我们对一下进度，然后一张清单，写着谁要干什么，事情才往前走。因为想法聊一百遍，没人动手，基本就是空的。","Phil: And you also probably want to talk about what is going to happen immediately now. So here we could talk about action points. What are the things we're going to do from this discussion right now to make sure that we start this project? And we could also talk about next steps. So the next things we're going to do. So often teams might say, oh, 'we'll check in on this in a week's time', and there'll be a list of action points that different people have got to do to make sure that things progress, because you can talk and talk and talk about ideas, but unless people do something about it, it's probably not going to happen."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这只是我随口一说。","This is just off the top of my head."],[0,"我就是边说边想。","I'm just thinking out loud here."],[0,"你的意思是不是我们……？","Are you thinking we would...?"],[0,"我先唱个反调。","I'm just going to play devil's advocate."],[0,"这个想法我喜欢，但站在市场的角度，我担心怎么推。","I like this idea, but with my marketing hat on, I'm worried about how we would promote it."],[0,"我想接着你那个想法说两句……","Just to follow up on your idea..."],[0,"交付物是什么？","What are the deliverables?"],[0,"我觉得这个项目放在市场部。","I think this project will sit within the marketing team."]]},{"cid":"bb05","title":"提案只有三十秒，开头怎么说","blocks":[[9,"提案最难的是前三十秒和后三十秒：开头抓不住人，后面讲得再好也没人听；结尾收不住，好想法就散了。这段拆开场、拆收尾，也拆怎么夸自己的方案又不踩别人的。留意同一个句子里既给新意、又给对方留面子的做法。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 提案陈述"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Phil：你有没有在工作里推销过一个想法？紧张吗？","Phil: Have you ever had to pitch an idea at work? Was it stressful?"],[0,"Beth：推销的关键差不多就是练。跟工作外的人讲，看他们听不听得懂。","Beth: I think the key to pitching is almost practising. So talking to people outside of work and seeing if they can understand you."],[0,"Neil：确实紧张，因为在看到对方的反应之前，哪怕你自己觉得这想法很棒，心里还是没底。","Neil: It is stressful because I think until you see the reaction of the person who you're pitching your idea to, even if you think it's brilliant, you have a big, big doubt."],[0,"Phil：假设你在一个会上，老板让你们团队出点子。你的提案怎么开头？","Phil: So, let's imagine you're in a meeting at work where your boss has asked your team to suggest ideas. How do you start your pitch?"],[0,"Pippa：开头就得把人抓住，所以要用最短的时间把想法说清楚。你可能听过电梯提案这个说法，就是在很短的时间里把想法讲明白。想象你进了电梯，上楼那点时间，你边坐边跟人讲完。","Pippa: So you want to grab people's attention from the start, so you want to summarise your idea in as short a time as possible. So you might have heard of the idea of an elevator pitch, and this just means explaining your idea in a short amount of time. So imagine getting in the lift or the elevator and going up, and you explain your idea in that kind of short period that you're talking to someone in the lift."],[0,"Phil：对。可以做成自问自答。比如，你有没有发现……然后接一句，我找到办法了。","Phil: Yeah. So you might do that as a question and answer. So for example, 'have you ever noticed...?' something. 'Well, I've found the solution'."],[0,"Pippa：对。另一种是直接把目标摆出来。你可以说，我想让……然后讲你要做什么。这样人家一下就明白你想干什么。","Pippa: Yes. Another way you can do it is to kind of state a clear ambition. So you can say, 'I want to make...' and then state what you want to do. So you're very clear about what you're trying to do."],[0,"Phil：如果场合比较松，可以说，这事我琢磨了很久……然后把关键问题点出来，再说，我的想法是……接着讲你的方案。","Phil: And then maybe if you're in a more informal context, you're kind of saying, 'I've been thinking a lot about...' and then the key issue, 'and my idea is to...' and then you explain your idea."],[0,"Pippa：开头说完了。那怎么收尾？","Pippa: So we've covered how to open a pitch. But how can you end things, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：这问题问得好，因为不能讲着讲着就没声了，得有个明确的收尾。可以想想这个想法能带来什么效果，能怎么服务客户。","Phil: Yeah, that's a really good question because you don't just want it to trail off. You want to have a clear end to it. So maybe think about the effect that this idea might have. Think about how it could serve your customers."],[0,"Pippa：所以你可以说，我觉得这会是一个服务客户的全新方式。","Pippa: So you might say something like, 'I think this will be an amazing new way to serve our customers'."],[0,"Phil：也可以聊行业或者整个社会的趋势。然后说，这个想法正好能抓住这个趋势，给出大家想要的东西。","Phil: Or you could talk about trends in your industry or in society in general. And, you know, 'this is an idea that could capture that trend' and could give people what they're looking for."],[0,"Pippa：还可以给想法加点紧迫感，说，如果我们动作快，我觉得真能做出成绩。这样人家能感觉到这事有劲。","Pippa: You could also introduce some urgency to your idea, so you could say, 'if we act fast, I think we could see real success'. So you're showing that your idea is exciting."],[0,"Phil：另一种收尾是请大家提问。可以探探对方的态度，问，你觉得呢？这个听着是你会感兴趣的东西吗？或者就说，关于这个想法，大家有什么问题我都欢迎。","Phil: Another way to end a pitch could be to invite questions. So you might want to gauge someone's opinion. Ask them, 'what do you think? Does it sound like something you'd be interested in?' Or just say, you know, 'I'd welcome any questions you might have about this idea.'"],[0,"Pippa：对，这个说法稍微正式一点。","Pippa: Yeah, that's a slightly more formal way of putting it."],[0,"Neil：要确保你提的东西真的解决了某个需求。还得注意别去说原来那个想法很糟，因为那可能就是在听你讲的那个人做的。","Neil: Make sure that what you're suggesting satisfies a need. You have to be careful not to say that the original idea is really bad, because it might be the work of the person you're pitching to."],[0,"Beth：我的建议是照着要求来，有点热情，然后条理清楚。","Beth: I would say stick to the brief, be enthusiastic and just be organised."],[0,"Pippa：贝丝和尼尔都提到要照着 brief 来。工作里让你提案，通常会给你一份 brief，就是一串要求，说明这个想法要满足什么。","Pippa: So Beth and Neil talked about sticking to a brief. So often when you're asked to pitch at work, you'll be given a brief, which is a list of guidelines for the idea, a list of requests for a certain idea."],[0,"Phil：对。提案时一定要让人看出你是怎么对上这份要求的。可以说，这能满足我们对……的需求，或者，调研显示客户想要更多……然后举例子。","Phil: Yeah. So it's really important when you're making your pitch that you show how you're meeting the brief. You say things like 'this will satisfy our need for...' or 'research shows our customers want more...' and then you give examples."],[0,"Pippa：对。还可以说，我一直在想我们现在这套东西缺了什么，我觉得这个正好补上。就是先讲现有的，再说明你的新在哪，但别去贬低别人的活儿或者想法。得客气，因为坐在你对面的人可能就是这个点子的主人。","Pippa: Yes. Another thing you can do is say, 'I've been thinking about what we're missing in our current offer, and I think this fills that gap'. So you can kind of talk about the stuff that exists already and show how your idea is new, but you don't want to put down other work or ideas. You want to be polite because you might be talking to the person whose idea it was."],[0,"Phil：对，你可以说，我们已经走了很远，但我觉得照这个路子走，也就到这儿了。","Phil: Yeah, you might say things like, 'we've come a long way, but I think working in this way can only get us so far'."],[0,"Pippa：对。也可以这么说，我想在之前那些成绩的基础上，做点不一样的。","Pippa: Yes. Another way you could phrase it is saying something like, 'I want to build on our previous successes with something a bit different'."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这事我琢磨了很久……我的想法是……","I've been thinking a lot about..., and my idea is to..."],[0,"我觉得这会是一个服务客户的全新方式。","I think this will be an amazing new way to serve our customers."],[0,"如果我们动作快，我觉得真能做出成绩。","If we act fast, I think we could see real success."],[0,"关于这个想法，大家有什么问题我都欢迎。","I'd welcome any questions you might have about this idea."],[0,"照着要求来","stick to the brief"],[0,"我一直在想我们现在缺了什么，我觉得这个正好补上。","I've been thinking about what we're missing in our current offer, and I think this fills that gap."],[0,"我们已经走了很远，但照这个路子走，也就到这儿了。","We've come a long way, but I think working in this way can only get us so far."],[0,"我想在之前那些成绩的基础上，做点不一样的。","I want to build on our previous successes with something a bit different."]]},{"cid":"bb06","title":"老板问你怎么达标，别只说目标","blocks":[[9,"老板让你拿个方案出来提高业绩，你张口就说我们要增长三成，这不算策略。这段讲怎么把目标拆成做什么、什么时候做、怎么做，以及怎么判断它到底有没有用。留意那些让句子变硬的词。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 计划与策略"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Pippa：你在工作中做长期规划吗？","Pippa: Do you make long-term plans at work?"],[0,"Neil：做个没细想的长期规划很容易，难的是做出真正想透了的细案。","Neil: It's quite easy to make long term plans that you haven't thought about very thoroughly. It's more difficult to make detailed plans that you've thought through really well."],[0,"Georgie：我自己做长期规划挺难的，因为我这人不太有条理。我看不到那么远，也排不出有条理的时间表，这方面不行。","Georgie: I find it quite hard to make long-term plans myself because I'm not very organised. I find it hard to see into the future and make a structured timetable of events. I'm not very good at that."],[0,"Pippa：假设上头让你拿一套策略，把你们团队的业绩提上去。可能老板想提高销量，或者提效率。这种计划该用什么词儿说？","Pippa: OK. Let's imagine you've been asked to come up with a strategy to improve results in your team at work. Maybe your bosses want to increase sales or improve productivity. What words and phrases can we use to talk about plans like this, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：先说要做什么，也就是你想干什么、能做到什么。比如你可以说，我们的目标是把成本降 25%。这个叫 objective，目标。也可以叫 success criteria，验收标准，就是达到了这些，你就知道策略成了。","Phil: Well, we've got the what. Which is thinking about what you want to do and what you can achieve. So, for example, you might say we're aiming to cut costs by 25%. And you could call this an objective. We also might call them success criteria. And these are the things that when you meet them, you'll know that your strategy has worked."],[0,"Pippa：对。还得说什么时候。时间线或者节点很有用。这种场合常听到季度这个说法，一年分成四个三个月。通常缩写成 Q1、Q2、Q3、Q4。比如有人会说，计划第一阶段在 Q2 落地，Q3 末评估效果。","Pippa: Yes. We also need to think about the when. So timelines or deadlines are useful. You'll often hear people in this context talking about quarters of the year. So, imagine the year broken up into three-month quarters. They're often abbreviated to Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4. So, for example, someone might say the first phase of our plan will be implemented in Q2 and we'll evaluate its impact at the end of Q3."],[0,"Phil：然后是怎么做，具体干哪些事去够这些目标。写这些的时候最好用确定的说法，说我们会做，而不是我们会试着做。","Phil: And then we have the how. And those are what specific things are you going to do to try and meet these targets. And it's quite good when you're specifying these to use definite language, say we will do something rather than we'll try to do something."],[0,"Pippa：对，这点很重要。策略不只是一个数字，它是你要做的所有事，是你为达到目标选的那条路。","Pippa: Yeah, I think that's really important. So, strategy is not just a target. It is all of the things that you want to do. Your approach to meeting those targets that you've got for yourself."],[0,"Phil：好，策略怎么定说完了。那怎么判断它有没有用，怎么改？","Phil: OK. We've talked about creating a strategy, but how can we decide whether the strategy is working and make changes?"],[0,"Pippa：一个办法是看数据。前面说的验收标准，可能都带着数字。比如目标是降本 25%，那就去量，看数据：过了一段时间，你到底降了几个点。","Pippa: Well, one way is to look at the evidence. So, we mentioned there might be success criteria, these might have numbers attached. So, say your target is we want to cut costs by 25%. You would measure, look at the evidence. What percentage have you cut costs by at the end of a certain amount of time."],[0,"Phil：对。这些有时候叫 key performance indicators，简称 KPI。就是拿来量的一些指标，好判断策略是走得好还是走得差。","Phil: Yeah. And sometimes these things might be called key performance indicators or KPIs. And they're just the things that are measured so you can assess how well or how badly a strategy is doing."],[0,"Pippa：可能一切顺利，目标达到了，说明策略有效。但要是没达到，没看到想要的结果，那就该谈谈调整了，看看策略里改哪块能好一些。这时候怎么说？有哪些选项？","Pippa: Yeah. So, it may be that everything's gone well and you've met your targets, your strategy is working. But if it's not, if you've not seen the results that you'd hoped for, then it's probably a good time to talk about changes, what you can change in your strategy that might make things better. How would we do this, Phil? What are some options?"],[0,"Phil：可以从优先级下手。你可以说，降本这条路好像走不通，要不咱们先把提高销量放在前面？","Phil: Well, you might talk about priorities. You might say, well maybe cutting costs isn't working. But why don't we prioritise increasing sales instead?"],[0,"Pippa：好，策略说完了。那长期规划呢？工作中该为未来规划到什么程度？","Pippa: OK, we've talked about strategies, but what about long term plans? How much should you plan for the future at work, Phil?"],[0,"Phil：这很看你所在的行业和做什么。有的行当大概不会怎么变，那你可以往很远处看。也可能你在一个变化特别快的领域，下一步会怎样根本没法预测。","Phil: Well, this is going to depend a lot on the industry you're in and the kind of work you do. It might be that something's probably not going to change that much. So, you can look way off into the future. Or you might be in a really fast moving field where it's just impossible to predict what happens next."],[0,"Pippa：也看你什么岗位、担什么责任。有人倒班，或者干的是特别日常的活，就是处理当天发生的事。比如医生，基本就是治当天进医院的人。而另一些人的工作本身就更偏策略和规划，他们的任务就是看未来，一点点把东西搭起来。","Pippa: Mhm, yeah. And it depends on your role and responsibilities. So, some people work shifts or in jobs which are much more day to day. They're really just dealing with what happens on the day. So, imagine a doctor for example. They really are just treating the people that walk into the hospital on that day. Whereas other people focus on strategy and planning a lot more in their job, their job is to look into the future and to build something over time."],[0,"Pippa：但哪怕你的活很日常，想想未来也有用。人容易只顾眼前，不做长期打算。那平时不干这个的人，怎么开始想长期规划？","Pippa: But I think it can be useful to think about the future even if your job is quite day to day. It can be tempting sometimes to just worry about what's in front of us and not make long term plans. So, how can people think about these long-term plans if they're not used to doing it at work?"],[0,"Phil：一个好办法是先想清楚你最终要什么。未来你想做成什么？你最希望自己已经做成了什么？然后写下来，尽量量化，说清楚，这就是我要奔的方向。","Phil: Well, what's probably a good idea is to think about what your ultimate goal is. What do you want to achieve in the future? What would you really like to have achieved? And maybe, yeah, try and write that down, quantify that and go, this is what I'm aiming at."],[0,"Pippa：还有一点，就是有没有什么将要发生的事会影响到你、你的岗位或者公司？会不会出现一个大转向，把你现在这类活甩开？未来有没有什么大事，是你得提前准备的？","Pippa: Another thing to think about is are there any events or changes coming up that might impact you, your job or your company? So will there be a big shift away from the kind of work that you do? Is there a big thing happening in the future that you need to prepare for?"],[0,"Phil：对。这些都想过了，最终目标也有了，威胁和机会也看过了，那就问自己，怎么从这个目标往回倒推？我要做成哪些事，才能保证达到那儿？","Phil: Yeah. So, when you've thought about all these things, you've got your ultimate goal. You've considered what kind of threats or what kind of opportunities there are for things that could change. Then think, OK, how do we work back from that goal? What are the things that I need to do to make sure that I can achieve it?"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我们的目标是把成本降 25%。","We're aiming to cut costs by 25%."],[0,"计划第一阶段在第二季度落地，第三季度末评估效果。","The first phase of our plan will be implemented in Q2 and we'll evaluate its impact at the end of Q3."],[0,"说我我们会做，而不是我们会试着做。","Say we will do something rather than we'll try to do something."],[0,"这些是验收标准，达到了就知道成了。","These are the success criteria — when you meet them, you know it's worked."],[0,"要不咱们先把提高销量放在前面？","Why don't we prioritise increasing sales instead?"],[0,"怎么从这个目标往回倒推？","How do we work back from that goal?"],[0,"你最终想要的是什么？","What's your ultimate goal?"],[0,"你能判断这套策略是走得好还是走得差。","You can assess how well or how badly a strategy is doing."]]},{"cid":"bb07","title":"提醒同事做错了，怎么开口不伤人","blocks":[[9,"看见同事做错了，说也不是，不说也不是。这段分三个场景走：大会上、邮件里、以及走到人家工位旁边。核心不是话术，是顺序——先问自己该不该说、什么时候说，再挑说法。留意那些半句就够用的开场白。","BBC Learning English · B1–B2 · 建议与劝告"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Phil：你有没有发现过同事哪儿做错了？","Phil: Have you ever noticed a colleague doing something wrong at work?"],[0,"Becca：在工作里提建议，有时候挺让人发怵的。但把你的想法说出来、让人听见，这很重要。","Becca: Sometimes it can be a little bit nerve-wracking to make a suggestion at work. But it's really important that you put your ideas forward and that you're heard."],[0,"Georgie：轻轻提一下比较好，别直接告诉人家该怎么做。","Georgie: It's good to gently suggest things rather than directly telling them what to do."],[0,"Phil：工作中提建议，得考虑些什么？","Phil: What might we need to consider when making suggestions at work, Pippa?"],[0,"Pippa：这块挺微妙，因为没人喜欢被教怎么干活。你也不希望被人当成那种老插手别人事、自己的活反而不上心的人。但帮别人一把也有好处，你也想跟同事处好，所以在给建议之前，最好先问自己几个问题。比如，你是跟谁提？你们公司等级是不是很严，严到你根本不会去跟老板讲自己的看法？对方比你资深，还是比你资浅？等级这事真得想。","Pippa: Well, this can be a tricky area because people don't sometimes like being told how to do their job. You don't want to get a reputation as somebody who's always getting involved in other people's work and not focusing on your own work. But also it can be helpful to help other people, and you want to work with your colleagues well, so you want to maybe think about a few different questions before you give some advice at work. So you might think, who are you making the suggestion to? So is this a really hierarchical workplace where you wouldn't tell your boss your opinion or some advice? So is this a more senior person, you or a more junior person than you? You need to think about the hierarchy, really."],[0,"Phil：对。还得看时机对不对。可能交期就在眼前，大家都很紧，这时候不是看别的东西的时候。也要看旁边有谁。当着人家整个团队的面去挑毛病，特别敏感。","Phil: Yes. Also think about, when you're making the suggestion, is it the right time? Maybe there's a deadline really close and everyone's very stressed and perhaps isn't time to look through something else. Also, think about who else is there. It can be particularly sensitive to criticise someone if the whole of their team is listening."],[0,"Pippa：对。还有怎么提、用什么话提，这也特别关键，直接决定人家是觉得你帮了忙，还是觉得你烦。","Pippa: Yes. And of course, we're very interested in how you make a suggestion, what kind of language you use, because that can really affect how someone reacts to your advice and whether they find it helpful or find it quite irritating."],[0,"Phil：先说开会。假设你在一场大会上，人不少，有认识的也有不认识的，还有些人级别比你高一点。正在讨论一项议题，你有建议。该怎么办？","Phil: OK. First, let's talk about meetings. Imagine you're in a big meeting with lots of people. Some you know, others you don't. And maybe some people there are a little bit senior. They might be more senior than you. An item is being discussed and you have a suggestion. What should you do?"],[0,"Pippa：讨论正开着，一般插进去提个建议是可以的，但还得看在场的人级别高不高，你自己觉得能不能开口。要是真想说话，就客气一点，先讨个许可，问，我能提个建议吗？也可以稍微道个歉，别人正在说、没料到你会接话的时候，说一句不好意思打断一下，或者我插一句。","Pippa: Well, I think in a meeting where things are being discussed, it's usually OK to get involved in the discussion to make a suggestion, but it may depend on the seniority of who's there, whether you feel like you can speak. But if you do feel that you want to say something, you could just be really polite and kind of ask permission. Say, 'could I make a suggestion?' Or you can sort of apologise a little bit, say 'sorry to interrupt' or 'butt in' if other people are talking and they're maybe not expecting to hear from you."],[0,"Phil：还有一种更绕的说法，不直接提，而是问，这个事值不值得考虑一下？","Phil: Another nice way, a kind of indirect way of making a suggestion: You can say things like, 'would it be worth thinking about this?'"],[0,"Pippa：再说邮件。可能像你说的，你对会上讨论的某件事有想法，想接着往下说。也可能你在一封邮件里被抄上了，对某个同事有点建议。邮件里的话，是不是该跟开会时说得不一样？","Pippa: OK, so let's talk about emails. Perhaps, as you said, Phil, you have suggestions about something that was discussed in a meeting and you want to follow up on it. Or maybe you're included in an email about something and you have some advice for a colleague. Should your language be different in an email, Phil, to how you would speak in a meeting?"],[0,"Phil：邮件确实会正式一点。而且你得留神别人怎么理解你的话，因为邮件里没有那么多线索能看出你真实的意思，有时候容易被误会。","Phil: I think email language does tend to be a little bit more formal. You've also got to be a little bit careful about how what you say is interpreted, because there aren't as many clues to give away what you're actually thinking. So, things can be misunderstood sometimes."],[0,"Pippa：对。开头可以很正式、很清楚。比如，关于会上讨论的那件事，我有个建议。这样引出你的建议挺好。","Pippa: Yeah. You could just start by being really formal and really clear about what you're saying. So you could say, 'I have a suggestion regarding what we were discussing in the meeting.' That would be a good way to introduce your suggestion."],[0,"Pippa：对。还可以加一两句，让人看出你是想帮忙，不是在指挥。比如，这个你可能早就想到了，不过……然后接着讲。结尾也常说，需要的话我很乐意再聊聊。很乐意一起喝杯咖啡说说。这样显得你友好、敞开，不是硬要插一手别人的活。","Pippa: Yeah. And it might be worth adding a couple of phrases that show that you're trying to be helpful rather than telling someone what to do. So you could say something like, 'you've probably already thought of this, but...' and then continue your suggestion. And also it's often good to end by saying 'happy to...' chat more about this if it would be helpful. 'Happy to...' grab a coffee and talk about it. So you're showing that you're trying to be friendly and open and you're not just kind of trying to get involved in someone else's work."],[0,"Phil：会和邮件都说了。那如果你在办公室，看见某人做一件事，你觉得有更好的做法，想给点建议呢？这就比较敏感了，因为没人喜欢被说活儿干错了、或者被教该怎么做。","Phil: OK, we've talked about meetings and emails, but what if you're in the office and you notice someone doing something and you think there's probably a way they could do it better and you want to give them advice? Now, this can be quite a sensitive situation because no one likes being told they're doing their job wrong or what to do."],[0,"Pippa：这时候最好的办法，还是回到开头那几个问题：你跟谁提？什么时候提？怎么提？尤其是跟谁。对方比你资深，还是在公司干了很多年、经验很足、其实挺懂自己在干什么的人？还是刚来的、资历浅、你的帮忙对他真有用的人？","Pippa: Yeah. So, I think the best approach here is to return to the questions we asked at the start of the programme. So, who are you making the suggestion to? When are you doing it? And how are you doing it? So, particularly who is it? So is this somebody more senior than you or somebody with lots of experience that's worked at the company for a really long time, that maybe does actually know a lot about what they're doing? Or is it someone new, someone more junior, who would really benefit from your help?"],[0,"Phil：对。快开口的时候有几个好用的小句子。一个是，我刚才无意中看到……意思就是我看见你这么做了，接下来就要说也许有个更好的办法。","Phil: Yeah, and there's some helpful little phrases that we can use when you're about to make your suggestion. There's one 'I couldn't help noticing that...' and it basically means I saw that you're doing it this way and you're then going to suggest maybe there's a better way to do something."],[0,"Pippa：对。还有一个类似的说法，我插一句……你得记住，你多半是在人家干到一半的时候打断人家。所以这句我插一句，意思就是我就想就你这个做法快说一句。既然打断了，就得清楚你确实打断了人家的节奏。","Pippa: Hmm. Yeah. Another phrase that's similar to this is to say 'I just wanted to jump in...' So, you've got to remember that you're probably interrupting somebody in the middle of what they're doing. And so saying, 'I just wanted to jump in', that's just saying, oh, I'm just going to quickly say something about the way you're doing it. So, if you're interrupting someone, be mindful that you are interrupting their workflow."],[0,"Phil：还有一种做法，先问一句，随便聊聊人家手上的活。比如，这是咱们说的那个项目吧，进展怎么样？等他说着，你再提建议就容易多了，因为你听到了他在说什么。","Phil: Another thing you can do is you can start by asking a question to have more of a general chat about what someone's working on. 'Oh, is that that project that we're talking about, how's it going?' And then as they're telling you how it's going, you can make suggestions easily then because you can hear what people are saying."],[0,"Pippa：对。机会可能就这么来了，人家说，嗯还行，就是这一步特别费时间。你就可以接，其实这块我有个办法，能稍微换个做法。","Pippa: Yeah. You might get a really good window because they might be saying, 'oh yeah, it's OK, but it's taking a really long time to do this task'. And then you could say, 'well, actually, I've got a suggestion of how you could do that slightly differently'."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我能提个建议吗？","Could I make a suggestion?"],[0,"不好意思打断一下，我插一句行吗？","Sorry to interrupt — can I just butt in?"],[0,"这个事值不值得考虑一下？","Would it be worth thinking about this?"],[0,"关于会上讨论的那件事，我有个建议。","I have a suggestion regarding what we were discussing in the meeting."],[0,"这个你可能早就想到了，不过……","You've probably already thought of this, but..."],[0,"方便的话一起喝杯咖啡聊聊。","Happy to grab a coffee and talk about it."],[0,"我刚才无意中看到……","I couldn't help noticing that..."],[0,"我插一句……","I just wanted to jump in..."]]},{"cid":"bd01","title":"决定说出口，别留半句含糊","blocks":[[9,"Anna 休完假回到办公室，全组人都在等她开口，Tom 尤其等得心焦。她只说了一句「我想清楚了，答案是 yes，我接受」，却始终没讲清接受的是什么。听她怎么用一串含糊的说法把决定抛出来，也看 Tom 怎么把这话接成了自己想要的意思。","BBC · B1 · 宣布决定"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Tom：不知道啊 Denise，我跟 Anna 挺配的，我觉得我俩会是天造地设的一对。Darcy 先生和 Darcy 太太……听着就不错……","Tom: I dunno Denise, I'd be good for Anna, I think we would have been a perfect pair. Mr and Mrs Darcy… it sounds good…"],[0,"Anna：我回来了！","Anna: I'm back!"],[0,"Tom：Anna！我……我们没想到你回来。","Tom: Anna! I… we weren't expecting you."],[0,"Anna：看得出来——Tom，你也许该收拾一下桌子。","Anna: Yes I can see – perhaps you could tidy up your desk Tom."],[0,"Tom：真逗啊 Anna——还想着当老板呢！这趟出去还好吧？有没有腾出点自己的空间？","Tom: Very funny Anna – still trying to be the boss! So did you have a good trip? Did you get some 'head space'?"],[0,"Anna：好吧，确实；我想了很多。Tom，我确实静下来过，也有机会……把这事反复琢磨了一下……","Anna: OK, well it's true; I have done a lot of thinking. Tom, I did have some head space and a chance to… chew things over…"],[0,"Tom：对！对！然后呢？","Tom: Yes! Yes! And?"],[0,"Anna：然后我已经拿定主意了。答案是 yes，我接受。真没什么可犹豫的……我应该试一试……我需要这份经验……再说，最坏又能坏到哪儿去？","Anna: And I've come to a final decision. The answer is 'yes'. I accept. There's no doubt really… I should give it a go… I need the experience… and besides, what's the worst thing that can happen?"],[0,"Tom：哦 Anna，我太高兴了。你不会为这个决定后悔的。","Tom: Oh Anna. I'm so happy. You won't regret your decision."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"你有没有腾出点自己的空间好好想想？","Did you get some head space?"],[0,"我一直在反复琢磨这件事。","I've been chewing things over."],[0,"我已经拿定主意了。","I've come to a final decision."],[0,"我应该试一试。","I should give it a go."],[0,"你不会为这个决定后悔的。","You won't regret your decision."]]},{"cid":"bd02","title":"老板当场提拔你，怎么先拖一拖","blocks":[[9,"老板把前任经理的位子直接摆到 Anna 面前，一句「千载难逢」压下来，还提醒她别拖太久。Anna 心里没底：资历不如同事，责任又太大。看她怎么既不点头也不摇头，把决定往后推，同时把话按住别让消息漏到当事人耳朵里。","BBC · B1 · 升职谈判"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Anna：顶掉 Paul 我心里过不去。他一直对我挺好的。","Anna: I feel bad about replacing Paul. He's been good to me."],[0,"Anna：谢谢。可为什么是我？我干得了吗？我没 Tom 那么有经验。","Anna: Thanks. But why me? Can I do the job? I'm not as experienced as Tom."],[0,"Anna：嗯……","Anna: Hmmm."],[0,"Mr Socrates：那么 Anna……你怎么说？愿意接 Paul 的位子，当 Tip Top Trading 的新老板吗？来吧 Anna。这次提拔是对你在公司成绩的认可。这是千载难逢的机会。","Mr Socrates: So Anna… what do you say? Will you replace Paul as the new boss of Tip Top Trading? Come on Anna. This promotion recognises your achievements at the company. It's an opportunity of a lifetime."],[0,"Anna：我知道。","Anna: I know."],[0,"Mr Socrates：你会是我的左膀右臂。","Mr Socrates: You'll be my right-hand man."],[0,"Anna：我明白了。","Anna: I see."],[0,"Anna：呃，Socrates 先生。这消息让我有点措手不及。谢谢您这么说，不过能不能给我点时间考虑一下您的提议？","Anna: Erm, Mr Socrates. This news has come as a bit of a shock. Thank you for your kind words but please could I have some time to consider your offer?"],[0,"Mr Socrates：哦……行吧 Anna。但别拖太久。我这人有说变就变的毛病。","Mr Socrates: Oh… OK Anna. But don't leave it too long. I have a habit of changing my mind."],[0,"Anna：好的，Socrates 先生……我是说 Brad……我尽快给您回电话。再见。","Anna: OK, Mr Socrates… I mean Brad… I'll call you back soon. Bye."],[0,"Tom：哦……该不会是 S 先生把 Paul 的位子给你了吧？","Tom: Oh… has Mr S offered you Paul's job by any chance?"],[0,"Anna：是！","Anna: Yes!"],[0,"Tom：然后你说你要考虑考虑？","Tom: And you said you'd think about it?"],[0,"Anna：对。我不确定自己能不能担那么大的责任。","Anna: Yes. I'm not sure if I can take on that much responsibility."],[0,"Tom：这有什么难的。我闭着眼都能干。","Tom: It's easy peasy. I could do it standing on my head."],[0,"Denise：可人家没把位子给你啊 Tom。","Denise: But he's not offering you the job Tom."],[0,"Anna：拜托别跟 Paul 提这事……先别说……他现在很难受。","Anna: Please don't mention this to Paul… not yet… he's very upset."],[0,"Tom：我什么都不知道！","Tom: I know nothing!"],[0,"Anna：你什么都不知道？不知道什么？","Anna: You know nothing? About what?"],[0,"Tom：我是说，我会守口如瓶……一个字都不说……等一切正式了再说。你放心我。","Tom: I mean, I'll remain tight lipped… I won't say a word… until it's all official like. You can count on me."],[0,"Anna：「你放心我」！？","Anna: 'You can count on me'!?"],[0,"Tom：啊？","Tom: Uh?"],[0,"Anna：「你放心我」。有人送我那束花，卡片上就是这句话。是你吧？！","Anna: 'You can count on me'. That was the message with that bunch of flowers someone sent me. It was you wasn't it?!"],[0,"Tom：这个……呃……算是吧……是我，Anna。我控制不住。我……我……喜欢你 Anna。","Tom: Well… err… I suppose… yes… it was me Anna. I couldn't help it. I… I… love you Anna."],[0,"Anna：你知道吗 Tom……我也挺喜欢你的……我觉得你……挺可爱的。来，亲我一下。","Anna: Do you know what Tom… I quite like you too… I think you're… sweet. Now come on and give me a kiss."],[0,"Paul：哎呀，我是不是该晚点再来？！","Paul: Oh crumbs, shall I come back later?!"],[0,"Tom：不用，没事 Paul。我们就是……多了解了解对方。其实 Anna……我想问你件事。","Tom: No it's ok Paul. We're just… getting to know each other a bit better. In fact, Anna… I'd like to ask you something."],[0,"Denise：哎，Tom 怎么单膝跪下了？","Denise: Oh, why is Tom getting down on one knee?"],[0,"Paul：估计是隐形眼镜掉了一只。","Paul: I expect he's dropped one of his contact lenses."],[0,"Tom：不是那回事。Anna，我想问你件事……呃……你愿不愿意……嫁给我？","Tom: No it's not that. Anna, I'd like to ask you something… err… will you… will you marry me?"],[0,"Anna：什么？！","Anna: What?!"],[0,"Anna：哦 Tom，我不知道该说什么。这太突然了。能让我想想吗？","Anna: Oh Tom, I don't know what to say. It's come as a bit of a shock. Can I have some time to think about it?"],[0,"Tom：那好吧。","Tom: I suppose."],[0,"Paul：行，你慢慢想，我这儿有个好消息。有人给我一份新工作。","Paul: Well, while you think about that, I've got some good news. I've been offered a new job."],[0,"Denise：太好了 Paul。什么工作？","Denise: That's fantastic news Paul. What is it?"],[0,"Paul：去一家叫 Better Biscuits 的公司当首席品尝师。","Paul: It's to be Head Taster at a company called Better Biscuits."],[0,"Anna：真是好消息 Paul。","Anna: That's fantastic news Paul."],[0,"Tom：是啊，恭喜 Paul。这活儿正合你的胃口。","Tom: Yeah, well done Paul. That's right up your street."],[0,"Denise：那 Anna，这是不是意味着你要接 Paul 的位子了？","Denise: So Anna, does that mean you'll do Paul's job now?"],[0,"Tom：别回答这个。先回答我的求婚。","Tom: Don't answer that. Answer my proposal first."],[0,"Denise：不行，我觉得她该先把工作的事定下来。","Denise: No, I think she should sort out her work first."],[0,"Tom：可我都等了好几个月才开口。","Tom: But I've been waiting to ask her for months."],[0,"Paul：我看还是让 Anna 自己说她想怎么样。","Paul: I think it's up to Anna to say what she wants."],[0,"Anna：都安静！各位，我没法现在就答复你 Tom，也没法答复 Socrates 先生。所以我决定了，我要休个短假，好好想想。","Anna: Quiet! Look everyone, I can't decide what to say to you Tom, or Mr Socrates. So I've decided I'm going to take a short holiday to have some time to think."],[0,"Tom：好主意。咱们去哪儿？","Tom: Good idea. Where shall we go?"],[0,"Anna：我一个人去。回来以后我给你们答复。","Anna: On my own. When I return I will give you my answers."],[0,"Paul：哎呀。我看我还是先去拿块饼干吧。","Paul: Crumbs. I think I'd better get a biscuit."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这次提拔是对你在公司业绩的认可。","This promotion recognises your achievements at the company."],[0,"这是千载难逢的机会。","It's an opportunity of a lifetime."],[0,"你会是我的左膀右臂。","You'll be my right-hand man."],[0,"这消息让我有点措手不及。","This news has come as a bit of a shock."],[0,"能不能给我点时间考虑您的提议？","Could I have some time to consider your offer?"],[0,"别拖太久，我这人有说变就变的毛病。","Don't leave it too long. I have a habit of changing my mind."],[0,"我会守口如瓶。","I'll remain tight lipped."]]},{"cid":"bd03","title":"同事约饭，别理解成让你下厨","blocks":[[9,"Anna 上班第一天，一心想给同事留个好印象，主动去跟资深客户经理 Tom 打招呼。Tom 正赶着一笔大单，随口一句 can you do lunch tomorrow 就把她打发了。看她怎么自我介绍，也看这句天天挂在嘴边的口语怎么被听岔成一场办公室闹剧。","BBC · B1 · 同事午餐"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Anna：挺兴奋，也有点担心。我特别想给人留个好印象。","Anna: Excited, but a bit worried. I really want to make a good first impression."],[0,"Tom：行行，不行，行行，好，行。这单我拿下，没问题。好，回见哥们儿，拜！","Tom: Yah, yah, no, yah, yah, OK, yah. I'll seal the deal, yah, no worries. OK, see ya mate, bye!"],[0,"Anna：你好，我们好像还没见过。","Anna: Hello, I don't think we've met."],[0,"Tom：没见过。","Tom: No."],[0,"Anna：您一定是 Tom 吧。我是 Anna，刚进团队。","Anna: You must be Tom. I'm Anna. I've just joined the team."],[0,"Tom：嗯哼。","Tom: Uh huh."],[0,"Anna：很高兴认识你。你在这儿干很久了吗？","Anna: Nice to meet you. Have you worked here long?"],[0,"Tom：不好意思，我这会儿特别忙——手上正有个大单要成。不过咱们改天聚聚。呃……明天一起吃个午饭？","Tom: Sorry, I'm quite busy right now – I've got a big deal just coming through. But let's get together sometime. Um... can you do lunch tomorrow?"],[0,"Anna：你要我来做午饭？这个，我不太——","Anna: You want me to do lunch? Well, I'm not very –"],[0,"Tom：抱歉，重要客户。那就明天十二点半，午饭？","Tom: Sorry, important client. Lunch tomorrow at 12.30 then?"],[0,"Anna：早上好 Paul！","Anna: Good morning Paul!"],[0,"Paul：早上好 Anna，你没事吧？","Paul: Good morning Anna, are you OK?"],[0,"Anna：挺好的，厨房就在那边过去是吧？","Anna: Fine, the kitchen's through there, isn't it?"],[0,"Paul：呃，是的。","Paul: Er, yes."],[0,"Denise：Anna！","Denise: Anna!"],[0,"Anna：哦嗨，Denise！","Anna: Oh hi, Denise!"],[0,"Denise：你在干什么？","Denise: What are you doing?"],[0,"Anna：给 Tom 做午饭。","Anna: Cooking lunch for Tom."],[0,"Denise：你干什么？","Denise: You what?"],[0,"Anna：Tom 让我十二点半把午饭准备好。","Anna: Tom asked me to have lunch ready for 12.30."],[0,"Denise：他真的这么说了？","Denise: Did he indeed?"],[0,"Tom：呃，Anna。","Tom: Er, Anna."],[0,"Anna：嗨 Tom！","Anna: Hi Tom!"],[0,"Tom：你在干什么？","Tom: What are you doing?"],[0,"Anna：春卷，然后是豆豉酱脆皮鸭。","Anna: Spring rolls, followed by crispy duck in black bean sauce."],[0,"Tom：不是，我是说，你干嘛要做饭？","Tom: No, I mean, why are you cooking?"],[0,"Anna：我现在不开始，十二点半就赶不上给你吃了。","Anna: Well, if I don't start now, it won't be ready for you by 12.30."],[0,"Tom：哦，你误会我了 Anna。我说 can you do lunch，不是问你会不会做午饭，是问你有没有空跟我一起去吃午饭。找个咖啡馆什么的。","Tom: Oh, you misunderstood me, Anna. When I said 'Can you do lunch?' it didn't mean 'Can you make lunch?' It meant 'Are you available to come to lunch with me?' In a cafe or something."],[0,"Anna：哦！","Anna: Oh!"],[0,"Paul：嗯……什么东西这么香，不过这是怎么回事？","Paul: Mmm... something smells good, but what's going on here?"],[0,"Denise：Anna 以为她的活儿是给大家做饭！","Denise: Anna thinks it's her job to cook for people!"],[0,"Anna：不不，是我误会了！","Anna: No, no, I misunderstood!"],[0,"Tom：Anna 就是有点搞混了。","Tom: Anna just got a bit confused."],[0,"Paul：哎，没关系，看着挺香。","Paul: Well, never mind, it looks tasty."],[0,"Anna：大家想吃的话，量够的。","Anna: There's enough for everyone if you want some."],[0,"Paul：这主意好极了，咱们来个办公室野餐！","Paul: I think that's a splendid idea, we can have an office picnic!"],[0,"Anna：好！","Anna: Yes!"],[0,"Paul：嗯，这酱看着就好吃。","Paul: Mmm, that sauce looks delicious."],[0,"Anna：是，我最喜欢这个。","Anna: Yes, it's my favourite."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我们好像还没见过。","I don't think we've met."],[0,"您一定是 Tom 吧。","You must be Tom."],[0,"我刚进团队。","I've just joined the team."],[0,"你在这儿干很久了吗？","Have you worked here long?"],[0,"明天有空一起吃个午饭吗？","Can you do lunch tomorrow?"],[0,"我这儿正有个大单要成。","I've got a big deal just coming through."],[0,"他真的这么说了？","Did he indeed?"]]},{"cid":"bd04","title":"客户订单漏了，怎么当场分工救火","blocks":[[9,"客户 Nice'n'Cheesy 的订单卡在办公室一直没动，周末展会就要用货，老板 Paul 把 Anna 叫进办公室，要她「不惜一切」搞定。可明天还有新品发布，Tom 手上又是一笔糊涂账。看她怎么定优先级，怎么当场把活派下去。","BBC · B1 · 加班赶单"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Anna：谁能接一下那个电话？我这边还通着。","Anna: Could someone answer that please? I'm on the other line."],[0,"Denise：我可不行，我已经在电话上了。","Denise: Well I can't, I'm already on the phone."],[0,"Tom：是啊，跟你朋友 Marge 聊呢。我这儿也忙着……呃……写商业方案。","Tom: Yeah, talking to your friend Marge. And I'm busy… errr… writing a business proposal."],[0,"Paul：谁能接一下电话……哦，你们都忙。那还是我来吧。喂？是？真的！这事我很抱歉。我们马上派人过去。对，今天上午。再见。Anna，你现在有空来我办公室谈谈吗？","Paul: Could someone just answer that phone… oh, you're all busy. I suppose I'd better do it. Hello? Yes? Really! I'm sorry about that. We'll send someone round right away. Yes, this morning. Bye. Anna, are you free to talk in my office now?"],[0,"Anna：有空 Paul。出什么事了？","Anna: Yes Paul. What's wrong?"],[0,"Paul：等等——我先咬口饼干——好多了。刚才那是 Nice'n'Cheesy。他们对我们的订单处理速度很不满意。他们周末办展会，要用我们的塑料葡萄。","Paul: Hold on – I just need a quick bite on a biscuit – that's better. Now, that was Nice'n'Cheesy. They're not happy about how slowly we are processing their order. They need our plastic grapes for an exhibition they're doing at the weekend."],[0,"Anna：可我以为 Tom 已经处理好了？","Anna: But I thought Tom had sorted that out?"],[0,"Paul：显然没有。我要你不惜一切把这事解决掉。","Paul: Clearly not. I need you to pull out all the stops and sort this out."],[0,"Anna：把什么不惜一切？","Anna: Pull out what stops?"],[0,"Paul：我是说，尽你所能把这单做完，拜托了。","Paul: I mean do all you can to get this order completed, please."],[0,"Anna：可明天还有茄子发布。","Anna: But we've got the aubergine launch tomorrow."],[0,"Paul：那个交给我和 Denise 来安排。会……很稳妥的。","Paul: Leave that to me and Denise to organise. It'll be in… safe hands."],[0,"Anna：哦，谢了。Tom，我需要你帮忙。是 Nice'n'Cheesy 那单，得赶紧处理。","Anna: Oh thanks. Tom, I need your help. It's the order for Nice'n'Cheesy, we need to process it urgently."],[0,"Tom：那单？我老早以前就发出去了，单子一起寄的。","Tom: The order? I sent that out ages ago, with the paperwork."],[0,"Denise：你说的是这份单子吗 Tom，就在你桌上？","Denise: You mean this paperwork Tom, on your desk?"],[0,"Tom：糟了！我肯定是忘了。我事情实在太多了。","Tom: Oh no! I must have forgotten. I've had so much to do."],[0,"Anna：反正客户不满意了，我们得全力以赴，把葡萄送到他们手上。","Anna: Well, they're not happy, so we've got to pull out all the stops and get them their grapes."],[0,"Tom：行，那茄子怎么办？","Tom: OK but what about the aubergines?"],[0,"Anna：先别管茄子了。这事现在就得动手，是我们的头等大事。你去仓库取塑料葡萄，我来处理这份单子，十五分钟后楼下见。","Anna: Forget about the aubergines. We've got to get onto this now. It's our number one priority. You go and get the plastic grapes from the warehouse, I'll sort out this paperwork, and I'll meet you downstairs in 15 minutes."],[0,"Tom：干嘛，咱们去哪儿？","Tom: Why, where are we going?"],[0,"Anna：打车去 Nice'n'Cheesy 的办公室，把葡萄亲手送过去。","Anna: We're getting a taxi to the offices of Nice'n'Cheesy so we can hand deliver the grapes."],[0,"Tom：哦对，可这不是快午饭了吗？","Tom: Oh right, but isn't it nearly lunchtime?"],[0,"Anna：没时间吃午饭了 Tom。这活儿现在就得干！","Anna: There's no time for lunch, Tom. We need to do this now!"],[0,"Denise：哦 Anna，你太厉害了。","Denise: Oh Anna, you're amazing."],[0,"Anna：……所以我们真的很抱歉……","Anna: …so we're really sorry…"],[0,"Tom：对，真的很抱歉……","Tom: Yeah, really sorry…"],[0,"Anna：……耽误了这么久，以后不会再发生。也希望这批葡萄你们满意……","Anna: …about the delay, and it won't happen again. And we hope you're pleased with the grapes…"],[0,"Tom：……还有价格！","Tom: …and the price!"],[0,"Jane：价格是很有竞争力，如果你们能保证多一点客户服务意识，我相信我们还会再向你们采购。","Jane: Yes, the price is very competitive and if you can guarantee a bit more 'customer care', then I'm sure we'll be buying from you again."],[0,"Anna：当然。非常感谢，再次抱歉。希望很快再见。再见！","Anna: Yes, of course. Thanks very much and sorry again. We hope to see you again soon. Bye!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"不惜一切代价，全力以赴","pull out all the stops"],[0,"这是我们的头等大事。","This is our number one priority."],[0,"这单得赶紧处理。","We need to process it urgently."],[0,"那单我老早以前就发出去了。","I sent that out ages ago."],[0,"这事现在就得着手。","We've got to get onto this now."],[0,"那事交给我。","Leave that to me."],[0,"我们马上派人过去。","We'll send someone round right away."]]},{"cid":"bd05","title":"「请你让位」：裁员话术怎么听","blocks":[[9,"发布会搞砸了，Paul 正要发火，一通电话却把他自己按住了：上级 Mr Socrates 说要搞「战略评估」，让他 step aside。办公室里没一个人听得懂这套说法。看这些委婉词背后到底是什么，也看 Anna 怎么接住一个更莫名其妙的问题。","BBC · B1 · 让位与晋升"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Paul：这种行为绝对不能容忍。","Paul: That behaviour just isn't on."],[0,"Tom：抱歉 Paul……不过挺逗的不是吗？","Tom: Sorry Paul… but it was quite funny wasn't it?"],[0,"Paul：一点也不好笑。","Paul: No it wasn't."],[0,"Anna：对不起 Paul，Tom 只是生 Dave 的气。我以为他喜欢我，结果看见他跟财务的 Julie 在一起。","Anna: Sorry Paul, Tom was just angry with Dave. I thought he liked me but we saw him with Julie from accounts."],[0,"Paul：真的？他看着挺正派的……算了，别再犯了，行吗？另外，那块砸碎的玻璃你得赔。","Paul: Really? He seemed such a decent chap… anyway, don't do it again. OK? In the meantime, you're going to have to pay for that broken window."],[0,"Tom：什么……哎？可，可是……","Tom: What… hey? Bbbut…"],[0,"Paul：好了，抱歉，我接个电话。喂，我是 Paul Smith。啊，Socrates 先生……是……啊，您已经听说了……","Paul: Now, excuse me, I need to take this. Hello, Paul Smith speaking. Ah, Mr Socrates… yes… ah, you've heard…"],[0,"Tom：哎哟，走吧，咱们还是撤吧。","Tom: Crikey, come on we'd better go."],[0,"Denise：那一下扔得漂亮 Tom！看来对 Dave 挺有触动。你看，他还给 Anna 送花了。","Denise: That was a good shot Tom! Looks like it's made an impact on Dave. Look, he's sent Anna some flowers."],[0,"Anna：哦，上面有张卡片。写着「你放心我」，可没署名。","Anna: Oh there's a note on it. It says 'You can count on me' but no name."],[0,"Denise：他写这么一句挺奇怪的。","Denise: That is a strange thing for him to write."],[0,"Anna：嗯，是挺怪，而且这不是他的字。","Anna: Hmm, it is and it's not his handwriting."],[0,"Tom：说不定是个暗恋者？会是谁呢？","Tom: Maybe a secret admirer eh? I wonder who it could be?"],[0,"Denise：你没事吧 Paul？你脸色白得跟纸一样。","Denise: Are you OK Paul? You look as white as a sheet."],[0,"Paul：其实不太好。Socrates 先生说他正在做战略评估。","Paul: I'm not actually. Mr Socrates says he's having a strategic review."],[0,"Anna：做什么？","Anna: A what?"],[0,"Anna：听起来挺严重的。","Anna: That sounds serious."],[0,"Paul：作为评估的一部分，他说要精简人员，还让我……让位。","Paul: And as part of his review, he says he wants to downsize and he's asked me to… step aside."],[0,"Anna：为什么？你挡着谁了？","Anna: Why? What are you in the way of?"],[0,"Anna：哦。我不明白 Paul。为什么？","Anna: Oh. I don't understand Paul. Why?"],[0,"Paul：他说公司需要新方向，需要更有冲劲的领导。","Paul: He says the company needs new direction and more dynamic leadership."],[0,"Tom：老天 Paul，还有谁比你更有冲劲！","Tom: Crumbs Paul, you can't get more dynamic than you!"],[0,"Anna：Tom！可是 Paul，你一直是个好老板。","Anna: Tom! But Paul, you've been a great boss."],[0,"Paul：谢谢 Anna。大概是经济环境的问题，我们赚得不够，裁人免不了。","Paul: Thanks Anna. I guess it's the economic climate, we're not making enough money so cutting staff is inevitable."],[0,"Tom：是啊，可你把 Denise 的岗位砍了。","Tom: Yeah but you cut Denise's job."],[0,"Paul：对，可我们后来又把她请回来了，部门要正常运转离不开她。","Paul: Yes but we had to get her back because she was necessary for the smooth running of the department."],[0,"Denise：没错。","Denise: That's right."],[0,"Paul：可 Socrates 先生说我是「富余人员」。","Paul: But Mr Socrates says I'm 'surplus to requirement'."],[0,"Anna：哦，这听着可不妙……是吧？","Anna: Oh, that doesn't sound good… does it?"],[0,"Paul：对了 Anna，Socrates 先生想知道你收到他的特别消息没有？","Paul: Anyway Anna, Mr Socrates wants to know if you got his special message?"],[0,"Anna：特别消息？那束花！？","Anna: Special message? The flowers!?"],[0,"Denise：真奇怪。Socrates 先生干嘛给你送花？","Denise: That's strange. Why is Mr Socrates sending you flowers?"],[0,"Anna：行，我得给 Socrates 先生打个电话，问问他为什么给我送花。","Anna: Right, I'm going to have to call Mr Socrates and find out why he's sent me flowers."],[0,"Mr Socrates：Socrates……谁找我？","Mr Socrates: Socrates… who wants me?"],[0,"Anna：呃……您好 Socrates 先生……我是 Anna。","Anna: Erm… hello Mr Socrates… it's Anna here."],[0,"Mr Socrates：Anna！我最喜欢的姑娘。叫我 Brad 就行。你打来我真高兴。","Mr Socrates: Anna! My favourite girl. Please call me Brad. So glad you called."],[0,"Anna：我想跟您说说您送我的那束花。我很受宠若惊，不过我觉得……","Anna: I needed to speak to you about the flowers you sent me. I'm very flattered but I don't think…"],[0,"Mr Socrates：花？！抱歉亲爱的，我没给你送过花，不过我给你发了封邮件——你看了吗？","Mr Socrates: The flowers?! Sorry honey, I haven't sent you any flowers but I have sent you an email – have you read it yet?"],[0,"Anna：没有。里面说什么？","Anna: No. What did it say?"],[0,"Mr Socrates：我说的是，既然我要把 Paul 开掉，你想不想升一级？","Mr Socrates: I was saying that as I'm giving Paul the chop, would you like a promotion?"],[0,"Anna：升职？","Anna: A promotion?"],[0,"Mr Socrates：对。你一直是团队里表现最出色的一个，那么，你想不想当 Tip Top Trading 伦敦办公室的新经理？","Mr Socrates: Yes. You have been an outstanding member of the team so how would you like to be the new manager of Tip Top Trading's London office?"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这种行为绝对不能容忍。","That behaviour just isn't on."],[0,"你脸色白得跟纸一样。","You look as white as a sheet."],[0,"他要精简人员。","He wants to downsize."],[0,"他让我让位。","He's asked me to step aside."],[0,"你属于富余人员。","You are surplus to requirement."],[0,"我要把 Paul 开掉。","I'm giving Paul the chop."],[0,"你一直是团队里表现出色的一个。","You've been an outstanding member of the team."]]},{"cid":"bd06","title":"办公室谣言四起，怎么开会稳住","blocks":[[9,"Paul 休假，Anna 代理管事，却和 Tom 在老板的记事本里翻到一行字：Socrates、IPC、final。Tom 立马编出一套全公司要被裁的说法，半天之内人人自危。看 Anna 怎么把话压住，又怎么在事实没弄清之前先稳住人心。","BBC · B1 · 讲道理"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Tom：这事很怪，肯定不是好事。不过 Socrates 应该就是指 Socrates 先生。","Tom: It's very odd and it can't be good. But Socrates must mean Mr Socrates."],[0,"Anna：对——可 IPC 是什么？什么意思？","Anna: Yes – but IPC? What's that mean?"],[0,"Tom：还有 final 听着特别……最终。嗯……我想到了！IPC——肯定是「即将裁撤岗位」的缩写——他们要把我们全炒了！","Tom: Yeah and final sounds very… final. Hmm… I've got it! IPC – it must be code for imminent post closures – they're going to sack us all!"],[0,"Anna：嘘。小声点。别跟所有人说。咱们先弄清楚，什么都先别说，行吗？","Anna: Sshh. Keep your voice down. Don't tell everyone. Let's check things out first, don't say anything yet. OK?"],[0,"Tom：行。我一个字都不说。","Tom: OK. Mum's the word."],[0,"Anna：你妈都知道了？！","Anna: Your mum knows?!"],[0,"Tom：不不不，这是咱俩的小秘密。回头见。","Tom: No, no, no, it's our little secret. See you later."],[0,"Denise：没事吧 Tom？","Denise: Everything OK Tom?"],[0,"Tom：哦，没事，都挺好。其实 Denise，不好。我觉得明天 Socrates 先生会把我们全开了。","Tom: Oh yeah, everything's cool. Actually Denise, it's not. I think we're all going to be sacked tomorrow by Mr Socrates."],[0,"Denise：什么？！不会吧！我周六还约了做头发，这下我拿什么付？我可怎么办？有了，我给 Marge 打电话。","Denise: What?! No! I've got a hairdresser's appointment on Saturday, how am I going to pay for it now? What am I going to do? I know, I'll call Marge."],[0,"Tom：嘿 Brian、Pete……咱们明天全得被炒。","Tom: Hey Brian, Pete… we're all going to be sacked tomorrow."],[0,"Anna：天哪，这话真难开口，不过还是说吧。不好意思，大家能过来一下吗？","Anna: Gosh. This is hard but here goes. Excuse me, could everyone gather round please."],[0,"Denise：是说裁员的事吗？","Denise: Is this about the sackings?"],[0,"Anna：不是 Denise。关于裁员的那些传言都不是真的。","Anna: No Denise. Any rumours about sackings are not true."],[0,"Tom：对，没错。谁跟你说的 Denise？","Tom: Yeah that's right. Who told you that Denise?"],[0,"Denise：哼……","Denise: Hmmm…"],[0,"Anna：请别听信传言。我正在核实情况，一有消息我马上告诉大家。","Anna: Please don't listen to rumours. I am trying to establish the facts and if I get any information I will let you know straight away."],[0,"Denise：可我听说 Socrates 先生明天要来，他肯定是来裁人的。","Denise: But I heard Mr Socrates is coming tomorrow, surely he's going to sack us."],[0,"Anna：别理这些传言，也请大家别再往下传。","Anna: Ignore the rumours and please don't pass them on."],[0,"Anna：好，对。大家照常干活就行。谢谢。","Anna: Right, yes. Could you please just carry on with your work as normal. Thank you."],[0,"Tom：那 Anna，你打算怎么弄清事实？","Tom: So Anna, how are you going to find out the facts?"],[0,"Anna：我得给 Paul 打电话——私下打 Tom——我不想再有传言传出去。","Anna: I'm going to have to call Paul – in private Tom – I don't want any more rumours getting out."],[0,"Tom：哦对，当然。你是得核实一下，对吧？","Tom: Oh yeah, absolutely. You need to establish the facts right?"],[0,"Paul：喂，我是 Paul。","Paul: Hello, Paul speaking."],[0,"Anna：哦嗨 Paul。我是 Anna。不好意思打扰你。你好点了吗？","Anna: Oh hi Paul. It's Anna. Sorry to bother you. Are you feeling better?"],[0,"Paul：好多了，谢谢，不过这段时间得离饼干远点！对了，一切都好吗？","Paul: Much better thanks but keeping clear of biscuits for a while! Anyway, is everything OK?"],[0,"Anna：不太好。公司在传裁员。Tom 在你记事本上看到明天那条，写着 Socrates、IPC。","Anna: Not exactly. There are rumours spreading about job cuts. Tom saw a note in your diary for tomorrow that said 'Socrates, IPC'."],[0,"Paul：嗯。真的？哦对。我是说，哦不！不是裁员——IPC 是明天开的国际塑料大会！Socrates 先生专程飞过来参加。我的天，我居然把这事忘了。","Paul: Hmm. Really? Oh yes. I mean, oh no! It's not job cuts – it's IPC - the International Plastics Conference tomorrow! And Mr Socrates is flying in for it. Oh golly gosh, I'd forgotten about that."],[0,"Anna：明白了。那你为什么写 final？","Anna: I see. And why did you write final?"],[0,"Paul：因为有个最佳塑料创新奖——我们靠 Imperial Lemon 进了决赛。那是我给自己提个醒，要写获奖致辞。我的天，我一个字都没写。","Paul: Because there's an award being given for the Best Plastic Innovation – and we're in the final with our Imperial Lemon. It was a reminder to me to write an acceptance speech. Oh golly gosh, I haven't written a thing."],[0,"Anna：哎呀。那咱们怎么办？","Anna: Oh dear. What are we going to do?"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我一个字都不说。","Mum's the word."],[0,"小声点。","Keep your voice down."],[0,"我正在核实情况。","I am trying to establish the facts."],[0,"关于裁员的传言都不是真的。","Any rumours about sackings are not true."],[0,"请别再往下传。","Please don't pass them on."],[0,"大家照常干活就行。","Could you please just carry on with your work as normal."],[0,"不是裁员。","It's not job cuts."]]},{"cid":"bd07","title":"同事当场发火要辞职，怎么接话","blocks":[[9,"Anna 说的 yes 指的是升职，Tom 却一直当成求婚答应了。真相说破的这一刻，他当场翻脸，把话说得极重，还甩下一句不干了。看 Anna 用哪几句话试图把人留住，也看这些话为什么没能马上奏效。","BBC · B1 · 同事发火"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"Anna：糟了！我说的 yes 是答应升职。天哪，我得赶紧把这事说清楚。Tom，Tom，你等一下。","Anna: Oh no! I meant yes to the promotion. Gosh I've got to sort this out. Tom, Tom, hold on please."],[0,"Tom：可不能耽搁 Anna。咱们把日子定下来，把大家都请来——连 Paul 也请。","Tom: We can't hang about Anna. Let's fix a date, invite everyone – even Paul."],[0,"Anna：不行不行，我们不能。","Anna: No, no, we can't."],[0,"Tom：你说得对，不请 Paul——他就知道说饼干。","Tom: You're right, not Paul – he just talks about biscuits."],[0,"Anna：不是。我是说，不行，我们不能结婚。我说的 yes 是升职。我不能嫁给你。","Anna: No. I mean 'no', we can't get married. I meant yes to the promotion. I can't marry you."],[0,"Tom：什么？那你说 yes 的时候，意思是 no？","Tom: What? So when you said 'yes' you meant 'no'?"],[0,"Anna：是。","Anna: Yes."],[0,"Tom：明白了。行，那就这样。Anna，我把对你的心思说得清清楚楚，你……你……就这么把我的话摔回我脸上。我受够了……受够你了……也受够这家公司了。我不干了！","Tom: I see. Right, that's it. Anna, I've made it very clear what I think about you and you… you… just throw it back in my face. I've had enough… enough of you… enough of this company. I quit!"],[0,"Anna：发脾气——这严重吗？","Anna: A tantrum – is that serious?"],[0,"Anna：我想我能。Tom，拜托，别这么急。咱们谈谈。这事能商量出办法，就是别急着做决定——求你了。你是我最好的——也是唯一的——销售。","Anna: I think I can. Tom, please, don't be too hasty. Let's talk about this. We can work something out, just don't rush into making a decision – please. You're my best – my only – sales executive."],[0,"Tom：抱歉 Anna——我是自由的人。风往哪儿吹，我就往哪儿去。你的机会用完了，现在轮到我了。我走了。","Tom: Sorry Anna – I'm a free spirit. I must go where the wind takes me. You've had your chance, now it's mine. I'm off."],[0,"Tom：……呃，抱歉，我忘了拿我那个专用杯子。拜。","Tom: …erm, sorry, I just forgot to take my special mug. Bye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我觉得 Tom 理解反了。","I think Tom's got the wrong end of the stick."],[0,"就这么把我的话摔回我脸上。","Just throw it back in my face."],[0,"我受够了。","I've had enough."],[0,"我不干了！","I quit!"],[0,"别这么急。","Don't be too hasty."],[0,"别急着做决定。","Don't rush into making a decision."],[0,"这事能商量出办法。","We can work something out."]]}]},{"bookId":"biz5","title":"真实通话","sub":"TalkBank 真实录音精编（非母语者，有口误）","chapters":[{"cid":"tk01","title":"首次通话：名字拼错，绕了三圈","blocks":[[9,"这是 1986 年的真实电话录音转写，两端都不是英语母语者，所以句子常常说一半、断掉、再重来。Jørgen 第一次打给这家客户，先自报家门，被总机转了进去；对方听不清他的名字，两个人又为一个字母一个字母拼出来的名字来回绕。注意他是怎么在对方明显没听懂的情况下，把事情一点一点说清楚的。","TalkBank 真实通话 · B1–B2 · 冷call开场"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"1986 年，Jørgen Gade 第一次打给一家欧洲客户，他要找的人，他只在传真上见过名字。","1986. Jørgen Gade calls a European customer for the first time, looking for a man whose name he has only seen on a fax."],[0,"Operator：WJ，下午好。691 2101。","Operator: WJ, good afternoon. 691 2101."],[0,"Jørgen：下午好，我是丹麦 INBEE 公司的。","Jørgen: Good afternoon. This is from INBEE Products in Denmark."],[0,"Jørgen：请帮我接一下布拉赫先生。","Jørgen: Can I speak to Mr. Brack, please?"],[0,"Operator：布拉赫先生？","Operator: Mr. Brack?"],[0,"Jørgen：对。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Operator：好，请稍等。","Operator: Okay, just one moment please."],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢。","Jørgen: Thank you."],[0,"Operator：我给您转过去，稍等。","Operator: I connect you one moment."],[0,"Mr. Brack：我是布拉赫。","Mr. Brack: Mr. Brack."],[0,"Jørgen：我是，呃，约根·盖德，从——","Jørgen: This is, eh, Jørgen Gade from the—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：啊，下午好，呃——","Mr. Brack: Ah, good afternoon, eh—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：稍等，稍等一下，我去拿个东西。","Mr. Brack: Just, just a minute, I'll just get eh something."],[0,"Mr. Brack：不好意思，我没听清您贵姓，先生——","Mr. Brack: I'm sorry, I didn't get your name, Mister—"],[0,"Jørgen：约根·盖德。","Jørgen: Mister Jørgen Gade."],[0,"Mr. Brack：约根·盖德。好，盖德先生，有什么事我能帮您？","Mr. Brack: Jörgen Gade. Yes, what can I do for you, Mister Gade?"],[0,"Jørgen：是这样——我们公司在阿森斯。","Jørgen: And that is— this is from Assens."],[0,"Jørgen：呃，布拉赫先生——本人在吗？","Jørgen: Eh, Mr. Brack— is he at home?"],[0,"Mr. Brack：就是我，在。","Mr. Brack: Myself, yes."],[0,"Jørgen：好，布拉赫。","Jørgen: Yes. Brack."],[0,"Mr. Brack：B-R-A-C-K？","Mr. Brack: B-R-A-C-K?"],[0,"Jørgen：不是。B-E-R-E-T-H。","Jørgen: No. B-E-R-E-T-H."],[0,"Mr. Brack：请稍等。","Mr. Brack: One moment please."],[0,"Mr. Brack：不好意思，我们这儿没这个人。","Mr. Brack: I'm sorry, we have nobody of that name."],[0,"Jørgen：可是您看，我这儿有份传真上的名字。","Jørgen: But you see, I have a reference from a fax."],[0,"Jørgen：是小写的，B、R。","Jørgen: That is with small letters, B, R."],[0,"Mr. Brack：啊，G-E-I-R 是吉拉尔代先生。","Mr. Brack: Ah, G-E-I-R is Mr. Girardet."],[0,"Mr. Brack：那个 B-R 是给他做事的秘书。","Mr. Brack: And the B-R is the secretary who worked for him."],[0,"Jørgen：好。我上周末跟 B-R 先生通过话。","Jørgen: Okay. I have been speaking to Mr. B-R last weekend."],[0,"Mr. Brack：不对，您说的是吉拉尔代先生。","Mr. Brack: No, you spoke to Mr. Girardet."],[0,"Jørgen：对。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：是为了我们挤出机上的一些喷嘴。","Jørgen: And that is about some nozzles for our extruders."],[0,"Jørgen：我给他写了封信。","Jørgen: And I have written a letter to him."],[0,"Mr. Brack：您能把信的编号给我吗，或者什么我能查的——","Mr. Brack: Can you give me the reference of your letter, or something I can—"],[0,"Jørgen：可以，呃，你们传真号，是二一。","Jørgen: Yes, eh, your fax number, that is two one."],[0,"Mr. Brack：好。","Mr. Brack: Very good."],[0,"Jørgen：我们的信是寄到这儿来的，在——","Jørgen: And our letter has been sent here the—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：好，十月十号。","Mr. Brack: Okay, on the tenth of the tenth."],[0,"Mr. Brack：您想要对十月十号那封信的答复。","Mr. Brack: And you want a reply to your letter, the tenth of the tenth."],[0,"Jørgen：对。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Mr. Brack：好。丹麦现在几点？","Mr. Brack: Yes. What time is it in Denmark now?"],[0,"Jørgen：两点一刻。","Jørgen: That is quarter past two."],[0,"Mr. Brack：好。盖德先生，您在办公室能待多久？","Mr. Brack: Okay. How long are you in the office for, Mr. Gade?"],[0,"Jørgen：哦，我在这儿，呃，大概也就一刻钟。","Jørgen: Oh, I will be here, eh, only a quarter I think."],[0,"Jørgen：但关键是，接下来八天我休假，您明白吧。","Jørgen: But the point is, in the next eight days I have holiday, you understand."],[0,"Jørgen：我可以下周一再给 B-R 先生打电话。","Jørgen: And I can call Mr. B-R again, eh, next Monday."],[0,"Jørgen：您能帮我转告他吗？","Jørgen: Will you say that to him?"],[0,"Mr. Brack：我会转告他，好。","Mr. Brack: I'll tell that to him, yes."],[0,"Jørgen：好。","Jørgen: Good."],[0,"Mr. Brack：不过那个人不叫 B-R，是 G-E-I-R。因为 B-R 是他的秘书。","Mr. Brack: But the person is not B-R, it's G-E-I-R. Because the B-R is his secretary."],[0,"Jørgen：啊，这样——好，我明白了。","Jørgen: Ah, so— yes, I understand."],[0,"Mr. Brack：别担心，这些我都能查出来。","Mr. Brack: Don't worry, I can find all that."],[0,"Mr. Brack：那您走一周，但是希望回来的时候能看到答复？","Mr. Brack: So you're away for one week, but you would like to have the reply when you get back?"],[0,"Jørgen：对，不过我可以下周一给他打。","Jørgen: Yes, but I can call him next Monday."],[0,"Mr. Brack：下周一您在休假。","Mr. Brack: Next Monday you're on holiday."],[0,"Jørgen：对，那是再下一个周一，呃，晚一周。","Jørgen: Yes, but that will be Monday after, eh, week later."],[0,"Mr. Brack：晚一周。好。好，盖德先生，我们会联系您。","Mr. Brack: Week later. Okay. Okay, Mr. Gade, you'll hear from us."],[0,"Jørgen：非常感谢。","Jørgen: Thank you very much."],[0,"Mr. Brack：好，再见。","Mr. Brack: Okay, goodbye."],[0,"Jørgen：再见。","Jørgen: Goodbye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我是丹麦 INBEE 公司的约根·盖德。","This is Jørgen Gade from INBEE Products in Denmark."],[0,"请帮我接一下布拉赫先生。","Can I speak to Mr. Brack, please?"],[0,"不好意思，我没听清您贵姓。","I'm sorry, I didn't get your name."],[0,"我们这儿没这个人。","We have nobody of that name."],[0,"您能帮我转告他吗？","Will you say that to him?"],[0,"我们会联系您。","You'll hear from us."]]},{"cid":"tk02","title":"客户回电：喷淋还是浸没冷却","blocks":[[9,"真实录音转写，双方都不是母语者，重复、改口、说到一半停住都很常见。昨天吉拉尔代发了一封关于喷嘴的电传，今早布拉赫主动打回来，先确认 Jørgen 有没有技术上的疑问，再追问两台设备到底是不是同一回事。注意布拉赫是怎么把「我只是好奇」问得像关心而不是审问的。","TalkBank 真实通话 · B1–B2 · 技术澄清"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"第二天一早，布拉赫先生主动打回来，为昨天那封电传里没说清的地方补一句话。","The next morning Mr. Brack calls back to clear up something in yesterday's telex."],[0,"Jørgen：喂。","Jørgen: Hello."],[0,"Mr. Brack：早上好，约根·盖德先生。我是，呃，瑞士的布拉赫。","Mr. Brack: Good morning, Mr. Jørgen Gade. It's, eh, it's Brack from Switzerland."],[0,"Jørgen：是。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Mr. Brack：昨天有点小误会，因为我现在看到，吉拉尔代先生给您发了一封关于喷嘴的电传。","Mr. Brack: There have been a slight misunderstanding yesterday, because now I see that Mr. Girardet sent you a telex for the nozzles."],[0,"Mr. Brack：您有什么要问的吗？","Mr. Brack: Have you any questions to ask?"],[0,"Jørgen：没有。","Jørgen: No, I haven't."],[0,"Jørgen：我们看过了，还得想办法弄点钱——我们不能说不，不能说——","Jørgen: We have a look at it, and we must see to find some money to— we can't say no, we can't say it—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：好。不是，我只是，呃，从技术上问一句。","Mr. Brack: Okay. No, it was just, eh, from a technical point of view."],[0,"Jørgen：好，我明白。","Jørgen: Yes, I understand."],[0,"Mr. Brack：我们就是好奇：这些是替换件吗？因为您看，您有一台是从马耳他来的。","Mr. Brack: We were curious to know: are these replacement parts? Because you see, you had one came from Malta."],[0,"Jørgen：对，没错。","Jørgen: Yes, that's correct."],[0,"Mr. Brack：这两条线很像。不过，这两台——啊，名字不一样。","Mr. Brack: Now, the two lines were similar. However, the two— ah, two different names."],[0,"Mr. Brack：那台，呃，875106，上面一个喷嘴都没有。","Mr. Brack: The line, eh, 875106, didn't have any nozzles on it."],[0,"Jørgen：哦，我明白了。对，我把马耳他那台的号给您了。","Jørgen: Oh, I understand. Yes, I have taken the Malta number to you."],[0,"Jørgen：还有，呃，水箱——我是从我们那台挤出机上取的。","Jørgen: And, eh, the water box— have I taken from our extruder."],[0,"Mr. Brack：对。","Mr. Brack: That's right."],[0,"Mr. Brack：那您是想改另一台，让它跟带喷嘴的那台一样？还是这两台——","Mr. Brack: Now, do you want to transform the other line, to make it like the one with the nozzles? Or are these—"],[0,"Jørgen：哦，我不太确定。","Jørgen: Oh, I'm not quite sure."],[0,"Jørgen：我试着，呃，出去看看——您看，只有旧的那台才有喷嘴——","Jørgen: I will try to, eh, go out and— you see, there's only nozzles in the old—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：其实这两台是同一年出的，只是那一台——","Mr. Brack: Well, actually they both came from the same year, but the one—"],[0,"Jørgen：好，我明白。","Jørgen: Yes, I understand."],[0,"Mr. Brack：不过不是，我只是好奇。呃，想知道您是不是要把那些换掉——","Mr. Brack: But no, it was just a matter of curiosity. Eh, to know whether you're replacing the ones—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：您看这两台的区别：一台有——因为有喷嘴，可以喷，把水打上去——","Mr. Brack: You see the difference between the two: one had— because you had the nozzles, and you could blow, force the water onto—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：旧的那台只是浸没冷却。","Mr. Brack: Now the older one had just immersion cooling."],[0,"Jørgen：嗯。","Jørgen: Hmm."],[0,"Mr. Brack：线缆走在滑架上，但整根是泡在水里的。这就是——","Mr. Brack: The cables went on skids, but they were fully immersed. That's—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：我们以为您可能想——我们不太确定您要的是哪种。","Mr. Brack: And we thought perhaps you wanted to— and we weren't quite sure what you wanted."],[0,"Jørgen：不，我明白。我们再看看这个，所以——我也不太确定。","Jørgen: No, I understand. But we take a look at this and so— I'm not quite sure."],[0,"Mr. Brack：好。生产线跑得还顺吗？","Mr. Brack: Yes. Are the lines running well?"],[0,"Jørgen：顺，挺好。没问题。","Jørgen: Yes, very good. No problems."],[0,"Mr. Brack：很好。活多吗？","Mr. Brack: Very good. Have you a lot of work to do?"],[0,"Jørgen：多，我们活儿不少。","Jørgen: Yes, we have a lot to do."],[0,"Mr. Brack：订单多？","Mr. Brack: A lot of orders?"],[0,"Jørgen：我们周末也上班，接下来三四个月吧，我想。","Jørgen: And we work also in the weekend, for the next three, four months I think."],[0,"Mr. Brack：啊，周末也干。听着不错。","Mr. Brack: Ah, the weekend. That's good to hear."],[0,"Jørgen：你们公司活也多吗？","Jørgen: And your company has also lot to do?"],[0,"Mr. Brack：哦，是啊，生意挺好。","Mr. Brack: Oh yes, things are going very well."],[0,"Jørgen：不过，呃，我回来——等我们看明白问题在哪儿——","Jørgen: But, eh, I came back— when we have seen what the problem is—"],[0,"Mr. Brack：好。多谢。","Mr. Brack: Okay. Thanks a lot."],[0,"Jørgen：好。","Jørgen: Okay."],[0,"Mr. Brack：再见。","Mr. Brack: Goodbye."],[0,"Jørgen：再见。","Jørgen: Bye bye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"您有什么要问的吗？","Have you any questions to ask?"],[0,"就是好奇问一句。","It was just a matter of curiosity."],[0,"生产线跑得还顺吗？","Are the lines running well?"],[0,"我们不太确定您要的是哪种。","We weren't quite sure what you wanted."],[0,"这听着不错。","That's good to hear."],[0,"生意挺不错。","Things are going very well."]]},{"cid":"tk03","title":"传真没收到：总机说人走了","blocks":[[9,"真实录音转写，说话人都不是英语母语者，句子常有重复和断裂。Jørgen 打给客户追一份传真，结果原来对接的人已经不在，只能跟一位新同事从头讲一遍：订单号、日期、发过几次。注意他被转来转去的过程中，每次重新开口都把关键信息重复一遍。","TalkBank 真实通话 · B1–B2 · 追传真"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"1988 年，Jørgen 打电话追一份传真，结果他认识的那个人已经不在了。","1988. Jørgen calls to follow up a fax, and the person he knows is no longer there."],[0,"Operator：WJ，下午好。691 2101。","Operator: WJ, good afternoon. 691 2101."],[0,"Jørgen：下午好，我是 INBEE 公司的，在——","Jørgen: Good afternoon. This is from the INBEE Products in—"],[0,"Jørgen：请帮我接一下萨曼莎·拉尔夫。","Jørgen: Can I speak to Samantha Ralph, please?"],[0,"Operator：哦，她已经不在——","Operator: Oh, she's no longer with the—"],[0,"Jørgen：她不在了？","Jørgen: She's not?"],[0,"Operator：对。","Operator: Yeah."],[0,"Jørgen：她给我发过一份传真，是二十——","Jørgen: She has sent me a telefax from the twenty—"],[0,"Jørgen：还有别人我能问一下吗？","Jørgen: Is there another I could speak to?"],[0,"Operator：呃，请稍等。","Operator: Eh, just a second please."],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢。","Jørgen: Thank you."],[0,"Clerk：下午好，有什么可以帮您？","Clerk: Good afternoon. Can I help you?"],[0,"Jørgen：下午好，我是 INBEE 公司的，我叫约根·盖德。","Jørgen: Good afternoon. This is from INBEE Products. My name is Mr. Jørgen Gade."],[0,"Jørgen：呃，萨曼莎·拉尔夫给我发过一份传真，是——","Jørgen: Eh, Samantha Ralph has sent me a fax from the—"],[0,"Clerk：嗯。","Clerk: Yeah."],[0,"Jørgen：还有，呃，这份传真我们又发了一次。","Jørgen: And, eh, we have sent this fax once more."],[0,"Jørgen：是我们的订单号，呃，一八六五七。","Jørgen: That is our order number, eh, one eight six five seven."],[0,"Clerk：好。","Clerk: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：是这个月二十一号的。","Jørgen: That is from the twenty first, in this month."],[0,"Clerk：好。","Clerk: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：我就是想问一下——你们收到我们这份东西了吗？","Jørgen: I would just hear— have you got this message from us?"],[0,"Clerk：应该收到了。您先别挂，稍等一下好吗？","Clerk: I am sure we have. Can you hold the line one moment?"],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢。","Jørgen: Thank you."],[0,"Jørgen：喂？我这边没看到今天有传真进来。","Jørgen: Hello? I can't see that the fax has come in today."],[0,"Clerk：喂。呃，可能还没发出去吧。","Clerk: Hello. Eh, maybe it hasn't been sent yet."],[0,"Jørgen：这份传真我们又发了一遍，就是那个时间发的。","Jørgen: We have sent this fax once again. That was the time when we sent it."],[0,"Clerk：明白了，明白了。您是二十一号发的。","Clerk: I see, I see. It was on the twenty first that you actually sent this."],[0,"Jørgen：对。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Clerk：我知道了。您先别挂，稍等一下？","Clerk: I see. Can you hold the line one moment?"],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢。","Jørgen: Thank you."],[0,"Clerk：喂。能给我们留个电话、传真号，或者别的联系方式吗——","Clerk: Hello. Can we have your telephone number, your fax number, or something—"],[0,"Jørgen：可以。我有电话，你们可以直接打到我办公室。","Jørgen: Yes. I have telephone number. You could call me directly, here to my office."],[0,"Jørgen：是，呃，四，五，三，四，五，一，二，三，四。","Jørgen: That is, eh, four five, three, four five, one two, three four."],[0,"Clerk：四，五，三，四，五，一，二，三，四。","Clerk: Four five, three, four five, one two, three four."],[0,"Jørgen：对。我叫约根·盖德。","Jørgen: Yes. And my name is Mr. Jørgen Gade."],[0,"Clerk：我们下午三点一刻给您回电话。我们这会儿正赶上午休。","Clerk: We'll come back to you in fifteen, this afternoon. It's our dinner break at the moment."],[0,"Jørgen：好。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Clerk：今天下午早点给您回。","Clerk: We will come back to you early this afternoon."],[0,"Jørgen：好，非常感谢。","Jørgen: Okay. Thank you very much."],[0,"Clerk：非常感谢。","Clerk: Thank you very much."],[0,"Jørgen：再见。","Jørgen: Bye bye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"她已经不在公司了。","She's no longer with the company."],[0,"还有别人我能问一下吗？","Is there another I could speak to?"],[0,"您先别挂，稍等一下。","Can you hold the line one moment?"],[0,"我这边没看到今天有传真进来。","I can't see that the fax has come in today."],[0,"我们这会儿正赶上午休。","It's our dinner break at the moment."],[0,"今天下午早点给您回。","We'll come back to you early this afternoon."]]},{"cid":"tk04","title":"说不清接线：画张图传真过去","blocks":[[9,"真实录音转写，意大利和丹麦两端都不是英语母语者，加上是在电话里描述机器接线，几乎每句话都在打转。Jørgen 要说清电机里四根线怎么接，讲了半天对方还是听不懂，最后他提了一个很朴素的解决办法。注意「实在说不清」的时候，老练的人是怎么收场的。","TalkBank 真实通话 · B1–B2 · 技术沟通"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"1989 年，一台从意大利买的机器装到了丹麦，电机怎么接线，谁也说不清。","1989. A machine bought from Italy is now in Denmark, and nobody can explain how the motor is wired."],[0,"Fecchini：Braillefour，你好。","Fecchini: Braillefour."],[0,"Jørgen：早上好，我是丹麦 INBEE 公司的，在阿森斯。","Jørgen: Good morning. This is from INBEE Products in Denmark, in Assens."],[0,"Jørgen：请帮我接一下恩佐·费基尼。","Jørgen: Please, can I speak to Enzo Fecchini?"],[0,"Fecchini：Braillefour，我是费基尼。","Fecchini: Braillefour, Fecchini."],[0,"Jørgen：早上好，费基尼。我是丹麦 INBEE 公司的约根·盖德。","Jørgen: Good morning, Fecchini. That is Jørgen Gade from INBEE Products in Denmark."],[0,"Fecchini：好，你好。呃，约根。","Fecchini: Yes, hello. Eh, Jörgen."],[0,"Jørgen：你跟我们总机通过话了吧？","Jørgen: You have spoken to our telephone operator?"],[0,"Fecchini：对，没错。","Fecchini: Yes, that's right."],[0,"Fecchini：呃，希尔先生打过电话来——他收到了一些消息。先说，呃，你们那台电机——","Fecchini: Eh, Mr. Shear has phoned to— and, eh, he receive some information. First of all, eh, the motor you have—"],[0,"Jørgen：嗯。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Fecchini：呃，几根，一共几根电缆，呃——","Fecchini: Eh, how many, how many cables is it, eh—"],[0,"Jørgen：不是，是从孔里出来的线。呃，我想是四根。","Jørgen: No, that is the wire out of the hole. Eh, I think there is four wires."],[0,"Fecchini：好。那是在一根电缆里，还是两根电缆？","Fecchini: Yes. But in one cable or in two cables?"],[0,"Jørgen：呃，这很难解释。因为——","Jørgen: Eh, it is very difficult to explain. Because—"],[0,"Fecchini：电机不在你跟前？","Fecchini: You don't have the motor in front of you?"],[0,"Jørgen：不在，但我昨天看过。那四根线，呃，有两根是接在一起的。","Jørgen: No, but I have seen it yesterday. And, eh, the four wires— two has been connected together."],[0,"Jørgen：这真的很难解释。不过要是有两根线——","Jørgen: It's very difficult to explain. But if you have two wires—"],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：两根铜线——它们在一块儿，是绕在一起转的。","Jørgen: Two copper wires— they was together, it was turning around together."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯，不好意思。","Fecchini: Yes, excuse me."],[0,"Jørgen：没事，没事。","Jørgen: No, no problems."],[0,"Jørgen：另外两根也是——你看，它是，唉，这叫我怎么解释呢？","Jørgen: And the other two, it was also— you see, it was, oh, how shall I explain it?"],[0,"Jørgen：我寄一张小图给你会不会更好？","Jørgen: Would it be better if I send you a little drawing?"],[0,"Fecchini：呃，好，因为，呃——","Fecchini: Eh, yes, because, eh—"],[0,"Jørgen：对了，你办公室附近有传真机吗？","Jørgen: Actually, have you a fax near your office?"],[0,"Fecchini：这个，你要是发传真，呃——","Fecchini: Well, if you send a fax, eh—"],[0,"Jørgen：你办公室附近有传真吗？","Jørgen: Have you a fax near your office?"],[0,"Fecchini：不太近。","Fecchini: Not very near."],[0,"Jørgen：没有啊，没有。","Jørgen: No, no."],[0,"Fecchini：这儿——呃，你看，要不我直接告诉你供应商怎么说的。首先是，我们——","Fecchini: In here— eh, you see, maybe I just tell you what the supplier said. First of all, we—"],[0,"Jørgen：两根电缆，对。","Jørgen: Two cables, yes."],[0,"Fecchini：呃，一根电缆，一根粗的。里面包含，呃，三根细的——另外还有，呃，两根细线，可能是接刹车的。","Fecchini: Eh, one cable, one big one. Eh, which comprises, eh, three little— and plus, eh, two little wires which could be for the brake."],[0,"Jørgen：接刹车，对。","Jørgen: For brake, yes."],[0,"Fecchini：对。不过刹车有时候不——","Fecchini: Yes. Despite the brake sometimes does not—"],[0,"Fecchini：还有，呃，另一根电缆，里面也是三根线，是接转速表的。","Fecchini: And, eh, another cable with, eh, also three wires, which is for the tacho."],[0,"Jørgen：接转速表，对。","Jørgen: For the tacho, yes."],[0,"Fecchini：对。所以，呃，第一根我说过了——要是没有刹车，那两根细线就不用接。","Fecchini: Yes. So, eh, concerning the first one, I said— if there is no brake, eh, just two little wires, it is not necessary to be connected."],[0,"Jørgen：啊，我明白了。好。","Jørgen: Ah, I understand. Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：不过费基尼，我觉得最好的办法是：我画张小图，把电缆传真给你。","Jørgen: But Fecchini, I think the best solution of this: I'll make a little drawing and send you by fax, the cables."],[0,"Jørgen：呃，要是有刹车，它是驱动刹车的——还有，呃，我把手上所有的资料都发给你——","Jørgen: Eh, if there is a brake, it drives the brake— and, eh, I will send you all the information I have about—"],[0,"Jørgen：我也把这个小标签一起拍下来发给你。","Jørgen: I'll also take the little label for this and send to you."],[0,"Fecchini：好。","Fecchini: Okay."],[0,"Jørgen：这样行吗？","Jørgen: Will that be okay?"],[0,"Fecchini：行，我觉得这样挺好，我们就可以具体商量怎么做了。","Fecchini: Yes, I think it will be nice, so we can discuss exactly what to do."],[0,"Jørgen：当然，费基尼。","Jørgen: Of course, Fecchini."],[0,"Jørgen：好，非常感谢你帮忙。","Jørgen: Yes, and thank you very much for your help."],[0,"Fecchini：呃——写我收，标急件，这样能快点到。","Fecchini: Eh— to my attention, and urgent, so it comes very fast."],[0,"Jørgen：好，非常感谢。","Jørgen: Okay. Thank you very much."],[0,"Fecchini：谢谢你。","Fecchini: Thanks for you."],[0,"Jørgen：再见。","Jørgen: Bye bye."],[0,"Fecchini：再见，约根。","Fecchini: Bye bye, Jörgen."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这叫我怎么解释呢？","How shall I explain it?"],[0,"我寄一张小图给你会不会更好？","Would it be better if I send you a little drawing?"],[0,"你办公室附近有传真机吗？","Have you a fax near your office?"],[0,"这个不用接。","It is not necessary to be connected."],[0,"写我收，标急件。","To my attention, and urgent."],[0,"这样我们就能具体商量怎么做了。","So we can discuss exactly what to do."]]},{"cid":"tk05","title":"追传真：新电机不用装风扇","blocks":[[9,"真实录音转写，双方都不是母语者，寒暄和技术问题混在一起，句子很松散。意大利那边打回来问传真收到没有，顺手把两件事讲清楚：旧电机为什么带风扇、新电机为什么不带，以及那四根线还是没解决。注意 Jørgen 是怎么把「上一台机器留下的老习惯」讲成一个理由的。","TalkBank 真实通话 · B1–B2 · 跟进传真"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"1989 年，费基尼打回来问一份传真，顺便说清了两件技术上的事。","1989. Fecchini calls back to ask about a fax, and two technical points come up on the way."],[0,"Fecchini：下午好，约根·盖德。","Fecchini: Good afternoon, Jørgen Gade."],[0,"Jørgen：下午好，我就是。","Jørgen: Good afternoon, speaking."],[0,"Fecchini：你好吗？","Fecchini: How are you?"],[0,"Jørgen：哦，这边挺好。我们最近特别忙。","Jørgen: Oh, it's going very well here. We are very busy at the moment."],[0,"Jørgen：像我之前跟你说过几次的，我们这会儿在盖新厂房，往新厂房里投了不少钱。所以现在特别忙。","Jørgen: As I have told you, eh, some times before, we are at the moment building up a new factory, and we have invested many money in the new factory. So we are very busy at the moment."],[0,"Fecchini：好啊。总比没活干强，呃。","Fecchini: Good. It's better than, eh, than not enough work."],[0,"Jørgen：是啊，那是。","Jørgen: Yes, it does."],[0,"Jørgen：呃，费基尼，我今天早上把传真发过去了。","Jørgen: Eh, Fecchini, I have sent the fax this morning."],[0,"Fecchini：传真你发了？","Fecchini: Have you sent the fax?"],[0,"Jørgen：关于电机那件事。","Jørgen: About the motor."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：你那边可能也收到了吧？","Jørgen: And you have maybe also receive it?"],[0,"Fecchini：呃，还没有。","Fecchini: Eh, not yet."],[0,"Jørgen：还没有？","Jørgen: Not yet?"],[0,"Fecchini：还没有。不过我这就去看——我直接过去拿，这样马上就能拿到。","Fecchini: Not yet. But I'm going to, eh, to see— I'm going to find, eh, directly to the— and so I will get it straight away."],[0,"Jørgen：好。费基尼，你办公室不是有传真机吗？","Jørgen: Yes. Fecchini, isn't it so that you have a fax in your office?"],[0,"Fecchini：这个，我们没——我这儿没有传真机。呃，就近，我身边没有。","Fecchini: Well, we don't— I don't have a fax here. Eh, near, near me, you see."],[0,"Jørgen：好。","Jørgen: Okay."],[0,"Fecchini：我们有，嗯，那边有几台传真机，不过，呃，都不太近。","Fecchini: We have, well, we've several faxes in the— but, eh, they're not very near."],[0,"Jørgen：是啊。","Jørgen: No."],[0,"Jørgen：费基尼，还有我早上跟你说过的：旧电机上有个小冷却风扇。","Jørgen: Fecchini, also as I have told you this morning: the old motor have a little cooling fan."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：不过我们今天把这个毛病聊了很久。我们觉得原因是这样：首先，那台挤出机原来在马耳他，在中东那边。我们在那儿有个厂，很多年前就有了。","Jørgen: But we have speaking very much about the problems today. We think the problem is because, first, the extruder was in Malta, in the Middle East. We have a factory there from many years ago."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：我们买这台机器的时候，是交到马耳他的。","Jørgen: And when we buy this machine, it was delivered to Malta."],[0,"Jørgen：我们觉得旧电机带个小风扇，是因为马耳他那个地方太热。","Jørgen: And we think that the old motor have a little cooling fan— it was because there was very warm in Malta, this area."],[0,"Jørgen：新的那台——你们交给我们的新电机——就没有冷却风扇。","Jørgen: And the new one— the new motor you have delivered to us— it has not a cooling fan."],[0,"Jørgen：因为我们这边没那么热，在——","Jørgen: Because we have not so very hot here in—"],[0,"Fecchini：对，没必要。","Fecchini: Yes, not necessary."],[0,"Jørgen：对。","Jørgen: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：还有，请你在传真上写清楚：新电机上不需要装冷却风扇——","Jørgen: And will you please state that on the fax: that it is not necessary to have a cooling fan on the new—"],[0,"Fecchini：好，我明白。","Fecchini: Okay, I understand."],[0,"Jørgen：第二个问题是：从孔里出来的那四根线，我们该怎么接。","Jørgen: And the problem number two: that is the four wires we have out of the hole. How we shall connect them."],[0,"Fecchini：对，怎么接，是。","Fecchini: Yes, how, yes."],[0,"Jørgen：也许你能从供应商那儿找张小图，帮上忙。","Jørgen: Maybe you could find a little drawing from your supplier to help."],[0,"Fecchini：当然。好，该办的我们会办。","Fecchini: Sure. Yes. We are going to do the necessary."],[0,"Jørgen：很好，费基尼。","Jørgen: Very good, Fecchini."],[0,"Fecchini：我一有消息就告诉你。","Fecchini: And I let you know as soon as I can."],[0,"Jørgen：很好。","Jørgen: Very good."],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢你帮忙。","Jørgen: Thank you for your help."],[0,"Jørgen：祝你今天顺利。","Jørgen: Have a good day."],[0,"Fecchini：再见。","Fecchini: Bye bye."],[0,"Jørgen：再见。","Jørgen: Bye bye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"总比没活干强。","It's better than not enough work."],[0,"你办公室不是有传真机吗？","Isn't it so that you have a fax in your office?"],[0,"我马上去拿。","I'll get it straight away."],[0,"该办的我们会办。","We are going to do the necessary."],[0,"我一有消息就告诉你。","I'll let you know as soon as I can."],[0,"祝你今天顺利。","Have a good day."]]},{"cid":"tk06","title":"四根线怎么接：谁也说不清","blocks":[[9,"真实录音转写，丹麦、英国、意大利三方，谁都不是母语者，同一个技术问题传来传去，越传越乱。Jørgen 早上刚跟英国的希尔通过话，转头又打给意大利的费基尼，把「电工说两根是主电路、两根是励磁」这个说法搬出来核对。注意他拒绝对方「再寄一台电机」的时候，话说得有多直接。","TalkBank 真实通话 · B1–B2 · 接线争议"],[3,"对话","Transcript"],[0,"同一台电机，同样四根线。丹麦电工、英国中间人、意大利供应商，三方说法都不一样。","The same motor, the same four wires. The Danish electrician, the British agent and the Italian supplier all say something different."],[0,"Operator：喂。","Operator: Hello."],[0,"Jørgen：喂。呃，不是，我明白。不过我这儿还有个名字：恩佐·费基尼，也许。","Jørgen: Hello. Eh, no, I understand. But I have also another name here: Enzo Fecchini, maybe."],[0,"Operator：对，那是——","Operator: Yes, that's—"],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢。","Jørgen: Thank you."],[0,"Fecchini：Braillefour，我是费基尼。","Fecchini: Braillefour, Fecchini."],[0,"Jørgen：早上好，费基尼。我是 INBEE 公司的约根·盖德。","Jørgen: Good morning, Fecchini. That is Jørgen Gade from INBEE Products."],[0,"Fecchini：早上好，约根·盖德。","Fecchini: Good morning, Jörgen Gade."],[0,"Jørgen：费基尼，我今天早上跟马克·希尔通过话，就是这台电机的事。","Jørgen: Fecchini, I have spoken to Marc Shear this morning about this motor."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：他也帮了我，还回了电话。","Jørgen: And he has also tried to help me and called back."],[0,"Jørgen：他说，从孔里出来的那四根，你们也许根本不用接。","Jørgen: And he said maybe you should not use these four that is coming out of the hole."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：但我今天早上又去找了我们的电工，跟他们聊了。","Jørgen: But I have returned to our electrician this morning and spoken to them."],[0,"Jørgen：从孔里出来的这四根线——我们电工认为这些是用来接——你知道——","Jørgen: And these four wires that is coming out of the hole— our electrician think that these are using for the— you know—"],[0,"Jørgen：呃，四根线里头，两根可能是接主电路的，另外两根是接励磁的。","Jørgen: Eh, when you have four wires, two of them are for the main connection maybe, and two of them are for the field."],[0,"Fecchini：嗯。","Fecchini: Yes."],[0,"Jørgen：所以问题还是这四根从孔里出来的线——我们实在看不出来该怎么接。","Jørgen: So our problem is still these four wires that is coming out of the hole in the— we have very difficult to see how we shall connect them."],[0,"Fecchini：是啊。","Fecchini: Yeah."],[0,"Jørgen：所以也许你去找一下马克——呃，马克·希尔，看他能不能给我们发张小图：这四根线怎么接。","Jørgen: So maybe you will go to Marc— eh, Marc Shear, and do maybe he can send us, eh, a little drawing: how we connect these four wires."],[0,"Fecchini：是啊。呃，你觉得这——这四根线是从电机里出来的——既然电机已经收到了，呃，那就试着装一下，它们总归是从某个地方出来的。","Fecchini: Yeah. Eh, do you think this— these four wires, they out of the motor— since you have received the motor, eh, try to install the motor and they come out from somewhere."],[0,"Jørgen：我们收到电机的时候，孔里就是这四根线。所以问题就在这儿。没人想过别的办法。","Jørgen: When we receive this motor, that have we the four wires out of the hole. So therefore we have the problems. Nobody has tried to make another solution about it."],[0,"Fecchini：对，对，我明白。","Fecchini: Yes, yes. I understand."],[0,"Fecchini：呃，也许现在，对，有一种可能，就是电机——你看——大概就是这么回事。","Fecchini: Eh, maybe now, yes, there is the possibility that the motor— you see— this is probably the case."],[0,"Jørgen：对，当然。","Jørgen: Yes, of course."],[0,"Fecchini：呃，这样，你知道我们能怎么办吗？我们再给你发一台电机。","Fecchini: Eh, now, you know what we can do? We can send you another motor."],[0,"Jørgen：不用，没必要。","Jørgen: No, that is not necessary."],[0,"Fecchini：没必要。","Fecchini: It's not necessary."],[0,"Jørgen：不用不用。你只要跟我说清这四根从孔里出来的线——问题就在这儿。","Jørgen: No, no, no. But if you only could tell me about these four wires out of the hole— that is our problem."],[0,"Jørgen：这样所有问题就都解决了。","Jørgen: So all the problems will solve."],[0,"Fecchini：好。那我再跟马克说一次，跟他讲，让他画张图，因为这四根线怎么接——","Fecchini: Yes. Well, I'll talk again to Marc and I'll tell him, and try to make a drawing because connection of these four wires—"],[0,"Jørgen：不过他说过也许你们不用——我觉得那不对。那完全错了。这四根线必须接。这是绝对的。","Jørgen: But he has told me that maybe you will not— but I think that is not true. That is totally wrong. You have to connect these four wires. That is absolutely necessary."],[0,"Fecchini：那电工试过不接这四根线就把电机接上，结果电机不——","Fecchini: So that the electrician has tried to connect the motor without these four wirings, and the motor is not—"],[0,"Jørgen：不行，因为，呃，按电工的说法，它们——","Jørgen: No, because, eh, in electricians' language they—"],[0,"Fecchini：这是接励磁的。","Fecchini: This is for the field."],[0,"Jørgen：F-E-L-D，对。","Jørgen: F-E-L-D, yes."],[0,"Fecchini：我明白了。","Fecchini: I see."],[0,"Jørgen：耽误你时间，真不好意思。","Jørgen: I'm very sorry to take your time."],[0,"Fecchini：没问题，你看。我们就是来帮你的——帮我们的客户。","Fecchini: No problem, you see. We are here to help you— to help our customers."],[0,"Fecchini：我们希望大家都能——越快越好。","Fecchini: And we like that every— as fast as possible."],[0,"Jørgen：对，当然。","Jørgen: Yes, of course."],[0,"Fecchini：那我再跟他说一次，有消息告诉你。","Fecchini: Well, I'll talk to him again. And I'll let you know."],[0,"Jørgen：很好，谢谢。","Jørgen: Very good, thank you."],[0,"Jørgen：谢谢帮忙。","Jørgen: Thanks for help."],[0,"Jørgen：再见。","Jørgen: Bye bye."],[0,"Fecchini：再见。","Fecchini: Bye bye."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"他也帮了我，还回了电话。","He has also tried to help me and called back."],[0,"我们实在看不出来该怎么接。","We have very difficult to see how we shall connect them."],[0,"没人想过别的办法。","Nobody has tried to make another solution about it."],[0,"你知道我们能怎么办吗？","You know what we can do?"],[0,"这是绝对必须的。","That is absolutely necessary."],[0,"耽误你时间，真不好意思。","I'm very sorry to take your time."]]}]},{"bookId":"biz6","title":"商务邮件","sub":"Enron 真实邮件 38 封，按办事功能分章","chapters":[{"cid":"em01","title":"约会议 · 改期（7 封）· 把会约下来，时间要动怎么开口","blocks":[[3,"会后第一封：谢谢要说具体","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 约会议"],[9,"上周在客户那边开完会，作者隔几天补一封感谢信。这种信最容易写成客套空话，这封难得地说了三件具体的事：谢对方抽时间、谢对方在会上支持、谢对方的意见帮忙澄清了顾虑。收尾那句括号里的玩笑，是全文最见分寸的地方。",""],[0,"想占用您几分钟，说一句上周在 Bloomfield 见到您很荣幸，也谢谢您在百忙之中抽空来开会。","I want to take a few minutes to say that it was a pleasure to meet you last week in Bloomfield and to thank you for taking the time from your busy schedule to attend the meeting."],[0,"会上您的支持我真心感谢，您的意见也帮我们把几个顾虑说清楚了很多。","I sincerely appreciate your support at the meeting and your comments helped a great deal in clarifying some of the concerns."],[0,"我知道您和 Rick Moore 在对接，相信这些事你们很快能敲定。","I know you and Rick Moore are working together and trust that you can finalize issues as soon as possible."],[0,"再次感谢您的时间和帮助，期待再见到您（希望下次气氛能轻松点）。","Thank you again for your time and support and I look forward to seeing you again (in a better atmosphere)."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"上周见到您很荣幸。","It was a pleasure to meet you last week."],[0,"谢谢您在百忙之中抽时间","thank you for taking the time from your busy schedule"],[0,"会上您的支持，我真心感谢。","I sincerely appreciate your support at the meeting."],[0,"您的意见帮我们把一些顾虑澄清了不少","your comments helped a great deal in clarifying some of the concerns"],[0,"期待再见到您（希望下次气氛好一点）。","I look forward to seeing you again (in a better atmosphere)."],[3,"迟交的材料补上，顺手约个见面","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 约会议"],[9,"对方等的一份提案拖了很久，作者这次一边补交、一边道歉，还顺势提出见面——因为人正好在对方的城市，机会难得。看它怎么把「迟了」和「想见你」放进同一封信，还不显得理直气壮。",""],[0,"接着之前和 Jon、Eric 的那通电话，附上这份拖了很久的提案。","Further to the conference call with Jon and Eric, please find the very overdue proposal attached."],[0,"文件拖到现在才发出来，实在抱歉。","Please accept our apologies for the delay in getting this document out to you."],[0,"我周四之前都在休斯敦。方便的话，想趁这个机会跟您见一面，做个自我介绍，也把文件过一遍。","I will be in Houston until Thursday. If possible, I would like to take this opportunity to meet with you to introduce myself and go through the document."],[0,"等您的回音，希望这周晚些时候能见到您。","I look forward to hearing from you and hopefully meeting you later this week."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"接着我们那通电话，提案见附件。","Further to the conference call, please find the proposal attached."],[0,"拖了很久的那份提案","the very overdue proposal"],[0,"延迟了，请接受我们的歉意。","Please accept our apologies for the delay."],[0,"想借这个机会跟您见一面。","I would like to take this opportunity to meet with you."],[0,"期待您的回音。","I look forward to hearing from you."],[3,"想约一小时电话会，先道个歉","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 约会议"],[9,"作者刚把一堆条款修改意见发出去，现在要拉对方开个电话会逐条过。信里两处自我降压特别值得学：一句 if any，先承认可能一条问题都没有；一句 apologize in advance，为可能重复了别人的活先赔个不是。",""],[0,"我觉得该约一小时电话会，过一遍这些修改里到底哪些（如果有的话）在英国法下有问题。","I think we should schedule one hour for a conference call to discuss which of these revisions, if any, present problems under English law."],[0,"如果我提的哪条修改您早就分析过、也因为英国法的原因否掉了，那我先道个歉。","I apologize in advance if I have suggested any revisions that you have already analyzed and rejected for English law reasons."],[0,"请告诉我您什么时候方便聊这些。","Please let me know when you would be available to discuss these."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我觉得该约一小时电话会。","I think we should schedule one hour for a conference call."],[0,"这些修改里有哪些（如果有的话）会有问题","which of these revisions, if any, present problems"],[0,"如果……那我先道个歉","I apologize in advance if ..."],[0,"请告诉我您什么时候方便。","Please let me know when you would be available."],[3,"给客户三个时段，让他自己挑","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 约会议"],[9,"招标方筛出三家候选，要在同一天分别见两小时，于是把三个时段一次摊给对方挑，顺手把地点、酒店都安排好。这种给选项而不是给通知的写法，等于把主动权递出去，对方也就不好意思拖。",""],[0,"我们想在 4 月 6 日周五跟您以及另外两家入围单位见面，每家两小时左右。","We wish to meet with you as well as two other shortlisted entities on Friday, April 6, for approximately two hours each."],[0,"想请您看看这几个时间：上午 8:30、11:00，以及下午 1:30。","Times we would like you to consider are: 8:30 am, 11 am, and 1:30 pm."],[0,"方便的话明天告诉我，这几个时段您哪几个可以。","Please let me know tomorrow if possible how many of these time slots are possible for you."],[0,"见面地点在圣迭戈市中心的 Latham & Watkins 律所。需要住的话，附近方便的酒店是 Marriott Marina San Diego。","The meetings will take place at the law offices of Latham & Watkins in downtown San Diego. A convenient hotel, if you need one, is the Marriott Marina San Diego."],[0,"这周晚些时候，我会把议程草稿，以及跟最终筛选有关的关键问题和清单发给大家。","Later in the week, I will circulate a draft agenda and list of key issues and questions pertinent to our final selection process."],[0,"期待当面见您，也把团队里几位关键人物介绍给您。","I look forward to meeting you in person and to introducing you to key people in the team."],[0,"再次感谢贵方的提案。","Thank you again for your proposal."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我们想安排在 4 月 6 日周五与您见面。","We wish to meet with you on Friday, April 6."],[0,"想请您考虑这几个时间……","Times we would like you to consider are ..."],[0,"这几个时段您哪几个可以","how many of these time slots are possible for you"],[0,"需要的话，方便的酒店是……","A convenient hotel, if you need one, is ..."],[0,"我会把议程草稿发给大家。","I will circulate a draft agenda."],[0,"期待当面见您。","I look forward to meeting you in person."],[3,"跨区会议通知：议程加请假","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 约会议"],[9,"一封标准会前通知：先说议程里要讨论什么，再说这个工作组打算怎么扩、为此请了谁，最后把材料什么时候发、来不了怎么办交代清楚。整封没有一句废话，是可以直接套的模板。",""],[0,"各位会看到，议程里有一项是讨论这个工作组的范围。","You will note that the agenda includes an item to discuss the scope of the working group."],[0,"这个工作组应当继续作为各职能交流想法的场所，同时也将提议把它扩到成员目前所在的其它东亚地区。","While the working group should remain a forum for the exchange of ideas across functions within the group, it will be proposed that the group be expanded to cover the other east Asian regions in which members of the group currently operate."],[0,"为此，我们请了 Mike Dahlke（韩国）、David Merrill（东南亚）和 Rob McGrory（澳大利亚）参加这次会议。","To this end, Mike Dahlke (Korea), David Merrill (SE Asia) and Rob McGrory (Australia) have been invited to join the meeting."],[0,"拨入方式，以及上次会议的纪要，会在电话会前发给大家。","Call in details and minutes from the last meeting will be circulated prior to the conference call."],[0,"如果无法出席，或者对议程草稿有什么意见，请告诉我。","Please let me know if you are unable to attend the meeting or have any comments in relation to the draft agenda."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"各位会看到，议程里有一项是讨论……","You will note that the agenda includes an item to discuss ..."],[0,"为此，我们请了……参加这次会议。","To this end, ... have been invited to join the meeting."],[0,"会在电话会之前发给大家","will be circulated prior to the conference call"],[0,"如果无法出席，请告诉我。","Please let me know if you are unable to attend the meeting."],[0,"对议程草稿有什么意见","any comments in relation to the draft agenda"],[3,"会已定，时间冲突请告诉我","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 改期"],[9,"项目快到签约，邮件一天几十封，作者干脆定了个会，把人按进同一个房间对齐。信里那句 be on the same page 是这类场合的高频说法；最后一句给改期留了门，但门只是虚掩着。",""],[0,"这两天关于这个项目的邮件太多了，而且我们已经接近签约，我建议开个会，确保大家信息对齐。","With the amount of email traffic within the last couple of days concerning the project and the fact we are close to contract execution, I would suggest we have a meeting to be sure everyone is on the same page."],[0,"会我定在 3 月 12 日周一中午 1 点。","I have scheduled this meeting for Monday, March 12 at 1:00 pm."],[0,"有问题，或者时间上冲突，请告诉我。","If there are questions or conflicts of schedule, please let me know."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这两天邮件来回这么多……","With the amount of email traffic over the last couple of days ..."],[0,"确保大家口径一致","to be sure everyone is on the same page"],[0,"我建议我们开个会。","I would suggest we have a meeting."],[0,"我们快签约了","we are close to contract execution"],[0,"时间上有冲突请告诉我。","If there are conflicts of schedule, please let me know."],[3,"想接 offer，只能到七月","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 改期"],[9,"一个学生接了暑期实习，却因为校内职务只能干到 7 月 20 日，比项目要求的 12 周短。结构很值得抄：先交代自己的情况，再问这样会不会有问题，然后表明很想接，最后补一句不行也理解——台阶先给对方。",""],[0,"Lexi，","Lexi,"],[0,"暑假实习这个岗位，我有个顾虑。","I have a concern regarding the summer internship position."],[0,"我在学校担任姐妹会主席，因为这个职务，7 月 23 日之前必须回到 Norman，所以暑期工作最晚只能做到 7 月 20 日。","I am president of my sorority at OU and because of my obligations to it, I have to be back in Norman by the 23 of July, making my last day of a summer job the 20th of July."],[0,"我看到这个暑期分析师项目是 12 周，我没办法做满。","I did notice that the summer analyst program is 12 weeks long and I wouldn't be able to work a full 12 weeks."],[0,"我能到岗的时间是 5 月 14 日到 7 月 20 日。不知道这样会不会有问题，还是想先问一下您。","The dates I am available are May 14-July 20. I don't know if this presents a problem, but I wanted to check with you."],[0,"如果这样安排可以，我很想接这个 offer；但如果不行，我也完全理解。","I would really like to take the offer if these circumstances were okay. But I do understand otherwise."],[0,"如果能尽快给我个回音，真的非常感谢！！","If you could let me know as soon as possible I would appreciate it!!"],[0,"多谢！","Thanks so much."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"关于……我有个顾虑","I have a concern regarding ..."],[0,"不知道这样会不会有问题，但我想先跟您确认一下。","I don't know if this presents a problem, but I wanted to check with you."],[0,"如果这样行得通，我很想接这个 offer。","I would really like to take the offer if these circumstances were okay."],[0,"但如果不行，我也理解。","But I do understand otherwise."],[0,"能尽快告知的话，非常感谢。","If you could let me know as soon as possible I would appreciate it."]]},{"cid":"em02","title":"催办 · 跟进（8 封）· 催人，但不显得在指责","blocks":[[3,"催进度：话说得轻，问得清楚","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"前一天电话里说好「他会回你」，第二天早上作者就来问结果。全信只有一句追问——Any news on this?——却比写三段催办都管用，因为它把「我在等」换成了「昨天讲好的那件事，进展如何」。",""],[0,"早上好！","Good Morning!"],[0,"昨天电话里您提到，John Pattillo 会回复您，说他打算怎么向 FEDEX 还价。这事有信儿了吗？","Per our conversation yesterday, you had noted that John Pattillo would be getting back to you with his decision as to how he would approach FEDEX with a counteroffer. Any news on this?"],[0,"另外，谢谢您一直留语音、发邮件，让我知道进展。","Also, thanks for leaving voicemail and email messages to keep me in the loop."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"昨天咱们电话里说的……","Per our conversation yesterday, ..."],[0,"您提到……会回您","you had noted that ... would be getting back to you"],[0,"这事有信儿了吗？","Any news on this?"],[0,"让我知道进展","keep me in the loop"],[0,"关于他打算怎么去谈……","as to how he would approach ..."],[3,"说好这周付款，钱还没到","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"取消订单的费用早就谈定，对方也承诺这周电汇过来，钱却没到。作者没有质问，只把「当初说好的」和「现在什么进度」摆在一起，末尾还顺手祝了句感恩节快乐——催款催到这个份上，脸面都还留着。",""],[0,"本月初谈定取消订单和相关费用的时候，我们以为你们会按承诺，这周就把 32.32 万美元的取消费电汇过来。","When the cancellation deal and charges were negotiated and finalized earlier this month, we anticipated that you would, as promised, be able to forward a wire transfer of the $323,200.00 cancellation fee this week."],[0,"如果抄送在这封信里的同事这周还在上班，或者能联系上贵司，麻烦告知文件是否收到，以及变更通知和取消费现在是什么进度。","If any of those copied on this memo are working this week, or are electronically in contact with your offices, I would appreciate notification that the documents were received, and what is the status of the change notice and cancellation payment."],[0,"谢谢，祝大家感恩节快乐！","Thank You and Happy Thanksgiving to all!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"当初……谈定的时候，我们以为……","When ... were negotiated and finalized, we anticipated that ..."],[0,"按承诺","as promised"],[0,"把电汇打给……","forward a wire transfer to ..."],[0,"文件收到了麻烦告知一声。","I would appreciate notification that the documents were received."],[0,"……现在是什么进度","what is the status of ..."],[3,"修完之后追一句：问题解决没","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"设备刚修完，服务方主动发一封回访，问问题是不是真解决了，还留了「随时回信吐槽」的口子。下面附了客户的原话回复。两段加起来不到十句，是售后邮件最省力的写法。",""],[0,"前段时间硬件服务团队为您的一台设备做了维修。","Recently the Hardware Services Team performed work on a piece of equipment for you."],[0,"这封只是跟进一下，确认您的问题解决了没有。","This is just a follow up to insure that your problem was resolved."],[0,"我们的目标是把服务做到最好，所以如果您有任何能帮我们改进的意见，直接回这封邮件就行。","It is our goal to provide you with the best service possible, so please feel free to respond to this email if you have any comments that may help us provide you better service in the future."],[0,"有任何问题，或者没彻底解决，随时联系我。","If you have any questions, or if the problem is not completely resolved, please feel free to contact me."],[0,"你们团队的支持我们非常满意，问题很快就修好了。","We are extremely pleased with the support we receive from your team. The problem was fixed very quickly."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"就是跟进一下，看您的问题解决没有。","This is just a follow up to insure that your problem was resolved."],[0,"我们的目标是把服务做到最好。","It is our goal to provide you with the best service possible."],[0,"直接回这封邮件就行","please feel free to respond to this email"],[0,"如果问题没有彻底解决","if the problem is not completely resolved"],[0,"你们团队的支持让我们非常满意。","We are extremely pleased with the support we receive from your team."],[3,"还没答案，也得先回一封","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"对方问的事，作者手上还没有答案。很多人这时候干脆不回，等有结果再说；这封反着来——先认「我还没有答案」，再说「一有结果就跟进」，最后留一句「需要更多信息、要开会都行」。三句话，把沉默变成交代。",""],[0,"关于有没有给客户报价的书面指引或政策，我这边暂时还没有答案，不好意思。","Unfortunately, I do not yet have an answer as to the existence of written guidelines or policy addressing the provision of quotes to customers."],[0,"一有结果我就跟进告诉您。","I will follow up when I have the response."],[0,"如果需要更多信息，或者要开个电话会，跟我说。","Please let me know if you need more information or if we need to conference."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"关于……我这边还没有答案，不好意思","Unfortunately, I do not yet have an answer as to ..."],[0,"一有结果我就跟进。","I will follow up when I have the response."],[0,"需要更多信息跟我说一声。","Please let me know if you need more information."],[0,"需要的话我们开个电话会","if we need to conference"],[3,"稿子转给你看，我还没过目","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"一份对外函件的草稿要请人过目，作者坦白说自己都还没看就先转出来了——为了快。这种「先说清为什么这么仓促」的交代，比事后解释有用得多。",""],[0,"附上和解函第 3、4 条所说的那封函件的草稿。","Attached is the proposed draft of the letter contemplated in Sections 3 and 4 of the settlement letter."],[0,"请尽早过目，看看这样能不能接受。","Please review at your earliest possible convenience and let me know if it is in acceptable form."],[0,"为了让你尽快看到，我没来得及自己先过一遍就发过来了。","In order to expedite your review, I am sending this without first having the opportunity to review it myself."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"附上这封函件的草稿。","Attached is the proposed draft of the letter."],[0,"请尽早过目。","Please review at your earliest possible convenience."],[0,"看看这样行不行","let me know if it is in acceptable form"],[0,"为了让你尽快审阅……","In order to expedite your review, ..."],[3,"草稿发你，随便拍砖","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"把一份合同草稿发给业务方，请对方看合不合用，还留下一句近乎口语的邀请：随便拍砖。这类邮件最难的是让对方真的愿意提意见——作者的做法是把「我会改」写进去：你们提的尽量改，改完再发一版。",""],[0,"随信附上项目工作说明，和/或人员服务说明，视情况适用。","Attached to this, as applicable, will be a Project Work Description and/or a Staffing Services Description."],[0,"人员服务说明我过一阵发出来，里面会更具体地写清服务内容和费率。","I will circulate the staffing description in the near future. It will contain a more specific description of staffing services as well as pay rates."],[0,"请看看这份草稿合不合你们的用。随便拍砖！","Please review this draft to determine if it fits your needs. Feel free to throw darts!"],[0,"有意见或问题，直接回邮件告诉我。","Let me know by return email if you have comments or questions."],[0,"能按你们意见改的我尽量改，然后发一版修订稿。","I will resolve as many as possible based upon your comments and circulate a revised draft."],[0,"谢谢。","Thank you."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"请看看这份草稿合不合你们的用。","Please review this draft to determine if it fits your needs."],[0,"尽管挑毛病！","Feel free to throw darts!"],[0,"有意见或问题直接回邮件。","Let me know by return email if you have comments or questions."],[0,"能按你们意见改的我尽量改。","I will resolve as many as possible based upon your comments."],[0,"我会发一版修订稿。","I will circulate a revised draft."],[0,"过一阵，近期","in the near future"],[3,"电话刚挂，资料就发过去","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"刚通完电话，作者立刻把谈到的方案发过去，还说明纸质版明天到。这封信的重点不在附件，而在最后两句：一句说自己多想接着做这件事，一句把下次见面挂在对方的日程上。跟进邮件写到这个温度，就不像催了。",""],[0,"谢谢昨天的电话，跟您聊得挺好。","Thanks for your call yesterday. It was good to talk to you."],[0,"附上我给这个联盟写的初步方案。这份是给您的，纸质版我也寄了，明天到。","Attached is the preliminary program I wrote for the alliance. This one is for you, and I'm sending a hard copy to you that will arrive tomorrow."],[0,"我希望借着这个，或者别的机会，能重新全身心扑回这件事上。","My hope is that with this, or with another opportunity, I'll be able to jump back into this issue with both feet."],[0,"等您的回音；等您日程腾出来能来圣迭戈，我们再见面。","Looking forward to hearing from you, and seeing you once you can free up your schedule to come to San Diego."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"谢谢昨天的电话，聊得挺好。","Thanks for your call yesterday. It was good to talk to you."],[0,"附上我给……写的初步方案。","Attached is the preliminary program I wrote for ..."],[0,"纸质版我也寄了，明天到。","I'm sending a hard copy that will arrive tomorrow."],[0,"全身心扑回这件事","jump back into this issue with both feet"],[0,"等您腾出时间","once you can free up your schedule"],[3,"初稿分工：谁看哪条点名说","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 催办"],[9,"一份对外材料的初稿要几个人分头看，作者没有群发一句「大家看看」，而是点了名字、指了条目：你查第 6 条全不全，你查第 2 条准不准。末尾交代自己周四前不在、但会看消息，把「找不到我」这个坑先填上。",""],[0,"各位，附上这份对外材料的第一版。","Gentlemen, attached is a first cut on the offering memo."],[0,"这份材料，需要你们看一下摘要里有没有实质性的错误表述。","For the memo, I need you to review the brief for any material mis-statements."],[0,"Bill，第 6 条看有没有漏。Dean，第 2 条看准不准、全不全。","Bill, please review item 6 for completeness. Dean, please review item 2 for accuracy and completeness."],[0,"有问题发邮件找我。我周四之前不在，但会看消息。","If you have questions, I can be reached by email. I will be out of pocket until Thursday but will check messages."],[0,"多谢帮忙！","Thanks for the help!"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"附上……的第一版","attached is a first cut on ..."],[0,"帮我看一下摘要里有没有实质性错误。","I need you to review the brief for any material mis-statements."],[0,"第 6 条看看有没有漏","please review item 6 for completeness"],[0,"我周四之前不在","I will be out of pocket until Thursday"],[0,"但会看消息","but will check messages"],[0,"多谢帮忙！","Thanks for the help!"]]},{"cid":"em03","title":"询价 · 报价 · 议价（5 封）· 问价、报价、价格谈不拢时怎么写","blocks":[[3,"回标报价：一页把话说全","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 报价"],[9,"客户发来招标文件，这是一封标准的回标信：一句说明来意，一句指向附件里的条款、数量和价格，再补一句可以谈的弹性，最后谢机会、留联系方式。全信五句，每句一个功能，没有一句寒暄废话。",""],[0,"针对贵方 6 月 25 日的招标，我们正式报价。","We would like to extend an offer in response to your RFP dated June 25."],[0,"条款、数量和价格见附件。","Please see the attached document outlining the terms, volumes, and pricing."],[0,"在合适的合同安排下，我们愿意给贵方留出把浮动价换成固定价的余地。","We are willing to provide you with the flexibility to exchange the floating price for a fixed price, under appropriate contractual agreements."],[0,"谢谢给我们供货的机会，期待跟您细谈这份报价。","Thank you for giving us the opportunity to supply your needs. I look forward to discussing this offer with you."],[0,"有任何问题或意见，随时联系我。","Please feel free to contact me with any questions or comments."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"针对贵方 6 月 25 日的招标，我们正式报价。","We would like to extend an offer in response to your RFP dated June 25."],[0,"条款、数量、价格见附件。","Please see the attached document outlining the terms, volumes, and pricing."],[0,"给贵方留出……的余地","provide you with the flexibility to ..."],[0,"谢谢给我们供货的机会。","Thank you for giving us the opportunity to supply your needs."],[0,"期待跟您细谈这份报价。","I look forward to discussing this offer with you."],[0,"有任何问题随时联系我。","Please feel free to contact me with any questions."],[3,"改完的稿子：改了哪、为什么","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 报价"],[9,"把一份条款清单改写成可以直接签的文本，改完还得跟同事交代：谁的修改我全收了，哪一句我动了、为什么动。最见功力的是那句「我觉得不影响实质，但还是听你的」——既表了态，又把决定权交回去。",""],[0,"我试着把条款清单改成了能直接执行的版本。","Here is my attempt to turn the term sheet into something executable."],[0,"William Harmon 的修改我全都接受了，只有修订条款下面第二段没动。","I have accepted all of William Harmon's changes except for the second paragraph under amended terms."],[0,"他写的是「逾期付款金额的计算方式……」，我改成了「逾期款项的利息计算方式……」，好跟上一段的说法对上。","He used the wording 'The payment late payment amount is calculated...'. I changed it to 'The payment interest on overdue amounts is calculated...' to be consistent with the reference in the above paragraph."],[0,"我觉得这不会改变任何实质内容，不过还是听你的。","I don't think this changes any substance, but I defer to you."],[0,"我还加了个简短的开头，加了一段关于后续付款的说明，重申这只适用于 10 月的采购。这两处也许都没必要，你说。","I also added a quick intro and a paragraph on future payments to reiterate this is only for October purchases. Neither may be necessary, let me know."],[0,"不知道你明天有没有空，但希望你上午能尽快回我。","I am not sure of your availability tomorrow, but I would love to hear from you ASAP in the morning."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我试着把条款清单改成了能直接用的版本。","Here is my attempt to turn the term sheet into something executable."],[0,"他的修改我全接受了，只有……没动","I have accepted all of his changes except for ..."],[0,"跟上一段的说法保持一致","to be consistent with the reference in the above paragraph"],[0,"我觉得不影响实质，但还是听你的。","I don't think this changes any substance, but I defer to you."],[0,"这两处也许没必要，你说。","Neither may be necessary, let me know."],[0,"希望你能尽快回我。","I would love to hear from you ASAP."],[3,"价格对不上，请帮忙核实","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 报价"],[9,"对方之前的成交价跟实际该有的数字差了五分钱美元，作者隔了个假期再来追问。这封信示范怎么礼貌地质疑一个价格：先说我听到的说法是什么，再请对方核实，最后交代清这是旧账里最后一笔没落定的。开头那句 On another, not so exciting, note 是换话题的标准过渡，值得背下来。",""],[0,"这单如果还有问题，请随时告诉我。","Please let me know if this deal continues to be a problem."],[0,"说件没那么让人兴奋的事，关于这单生意我还有个问题。","On another, not so exciting, note, I have another question about the EESI deal."],[0,"我刚跟 Judy 通过话，他们说价格应该是 145.00 美元，不是 145.05。","I just spoke with Judy and they say that the price is supposed to be $145.00 not $145.05."],[0,"这个能麻烦你查一下吗？","Can you check on that one?"],[0,"假期前那摊乱事里，就剩这一笔还悬着没落定。","It's the only one still hanging out there from the mess before the holidays."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这单如果还有问题，请随时告诉我。","Please let me know if this deal continues to be a problem."],[0,"说件没那么让人兴奋的事……","On another, not so exciting, note, ..."],[0,"价格应该是 145.00 美元，不是 145.05","the price is supposed to be $145.00 not $145.05"],[0,"这个能麻烦你查一下吗？","Can you check on that one?"],[0,"就剩这一笔还悬着没落定。","It's the only one still hanging out there."],[3,"先做成本方案，再谈怎么推","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 报价"],[9,"一项新技术要不要上、怎么报价，作者没有直接拍板，而是先请对方做个整体测算：成本多少、谁能装、要不要报批。顺手把分工也摆了出来——数据我们管，客户对接和安装归对方。看怎么连说两句 I think we should 还不显得强势。",""],[0,"这项技术你能先做个整体方案吗——成本多少、谁能来装、要不要报批等等。","Can you work up a game plan on this technology - (costs, who could install, do we need utility approval, etc.)."],[0,"我觉得应该把我们的要求提给 EES，把安装写成合同里我方对客户的一项选择权，把成本摊进每一单的报价里，再真正装一套试试。","I think we should present our requirements to EES, make the installation our contractual option with the customer, begin pricing the cost into each deal and get a real install done."],[0,"另外，数据这块（收集、分发、负荷预测）我们主动来管，客户对接和安装的责任交给 EES。","Also, I think we should offer to administer the data side (gathering, dissemination, load forecasting) and EES should have the customer contact/install responsibility."],[0,"等 IT 和技术上的问题都摸清楚了，我们再商量怎么通过 EES 推下去。","As soon as we have our hands around the IT/technical issues let's discuss and push through EES."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这项技术你能先做个整体方案吗？","Can you work up a game plan on this technology?"],[0,"把安装写成合同里我方对客户的选择权","make the installation our contractual option with the customer"],[0,"把成本摊进每一单的报价里","begin pricing the cost into each deal"],[0,"主动提出数据这块由我们管","offer to administer the data side"],[0,"等问题都摸清楚了，我们再商量。","As soon as we have our hands around the issues, let's discuss."],[3,"合同折扣上调，记得同步改","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 报价"],[9,"合同折扣率从 2.7% 上调到 3.5%，涉及所有在服务的账户，作者得让同事把系统里的数同步改掉。开头一句 for the record 先把话说正式，结尾给两条路：有疑问打电话，有困难务必直说。通知类邮件把「觉得不妥也得吭声」的门留着，是分寸所在。",""],[0,"我知道说这事可能有点小题大做，但正式记录一下：按 GSA 合同，所有金融和实物商品交易的电价折扣，从 2.7% 上调到 3.5%。","I know this may seem silly but for the record, the electricity discount for all financial and physical commodity deals per the GSA Contract increases to 3.5% from 2.7%."],[0,"也就是说，我们现在服务的所有账户，系统里的折扣率都要从老的 2.7% 改成新的 3.5%。","This means that for all the accounts which we currently service, we need to update the computer discount rate from the old rate (2.7%) to the new rate (3.5%)."],[0,"有疑问打电话给我；如果这样有困难，务必告诉我。","Please give me a call if you have questions and certainly let me know if this is a problem."],[0,"谢谢，也希望你假期过得轻松。","Thanks and I hope your holidays were relaxing."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我知道说这事可能有点多余，但正式记录一下……","I know this may seem silly but for the record, ..."],[0,"从 2.7% 上调到 3.5%","increases to 3.5% from 2.7%"],[0,"我们目前服务的所有账户","for all the accounts which we currently service"],[0,"把折扣率从老的换成新的","update the discount rate from the old rate to the new rate"],[0,"有疑问请打给我。","Please give me a call if you have questions."],[0,"如果这样有困难，务必告诉我","certainly let me know if this is a problem"]]},{"cid":"em04","title":"交期 · 物流（5 封）· 延期怎么交代，货到哪了怎么说","blocks":[[3,"没按约定交货，书面把话说明","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 交期"],[9,"12 月 6 日这天没给客户安排供气，作者到前一天很晚才发现。这封信的次序值得逐句看：先摆事实，交代自己何时知情，再引合同条款把性质说清，然后把「下一步怎么办」推回给客户，并要一个尽快答复。全程没有一个形容词，也没有一句道歉——先救火，责任后面再谈。",""],[0,"2001 年 12 月 6 日这天，我们没有给 Mesa 市安排供气。这件事我到 12 月 5 日很晚才知道。","For December 6, 2001, we did not schedule gas to the City of Mesa. I was unaware of this until late in the day on December 5."],[0,"所以按合同第 12 条，我的理解是：这一天我们没有提供足够的供气。","Therefore, it is my interpretation, under section 12 of the contract, that we are not providing sufficient gas supply to the City on this day."],[0,"既然 12 月 6 日没有安排供气，市里应该按合同条款自行决定下一步最合适的做法。","The City should determine its best course of action based on the terms of the contract, given the fact that we did not schedule gas for December 6th."],[0,"有新的货源或者其他安排，请尽快通知我。","Please notify me of any new supply or other course of action as soon as possible."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我是当天很晚才知道的。","I was unaware of this until late in the day."],[0,"按合同第 12 条，我的理解是……","it is my interpretation, under section 12 of the contract, that ..."],[0,"应该自行决定下一步怎么办","should determine its best course of action"],[0,"考虑到……这个事实","given the fact that ..."],[0,"有新的货源请尽快通知我。","Please notify me of any new supply as soon as possible."],[3,"能做，但费时间：先给结论","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 物流"],[9,"有人问「日本那边能不能做实体配送」，作者没有堆分析，先给结论：能做，但很费时间。中间那句「跟日本大多数事情一样」是典型的轻描淡写。最后不追问、不推销，只说「要再往下做随时说」。",""],[0,"附上一份汇总，讲在日本做林产品实体配送有哪些难点。","Attached is a summary of the challenges to physically delivering forest products in Japan."],[0,"简单说，这流程很麻烦，产业界、政府和准政府机构之间的关系盘根错节——日本大多数事都这样。","Briefly, it's a cumbersome process complicated by the inter-relationship between industry, government, and quasi-government entities — like most things in Japan."],[0,"一句话：我们能在日本做实体配送，但很费时间。","In short, it would be possible, but time consuming, for us to manage physical deliveries in Japan."],[0,"需要我们再往下做，跟我说；希望不久能再联系。","Let me know if you would like any more work on this issue, and I hope we'll be in touch before long."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"附上一份……难点的汇总。","Attached is a summary of the challenges to ..."],[0,"简单说，这流程很麻烦。","Briefly, it's a cumbersome process."],[0,"一句话：能做，但费时间。","In short, it would be possible, but time consuming."],[0,"需要再往下做，跟我说。","Let me know if you would like any more work on this issue."],[0,"希望不久能再联系。","I hope we'll be in touch before long."],[3,"周一要完成，赶不上请早说","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 交期"],[9,"项目上线在即，作者一封邮件把几摊事分派清楚：谁保证周一前装完、谁去跟进漏了演示的团队、安全问题要哪个口径。最值得抄的是收尾那句——如果你觉得这个排期赶不上，一旦发现就告诉我，等于提前给坏消息铺好了路。",""],[0,"Paul，麻烦你确保网络那边的同事周一之前把 Tibco 装完，包括 Terminal Server。","Paul, could you please insure that the network folks have the Tibco install complete by Monday, including Terminal Server."],[0,"Scotty，Calgary 和 Texas 没来参加演示，能麻烦你跟一下他们吗。","Scotty, can you follow up with Calgary and Texas since they missed the demo."],[0,"另外，这次上线安全问题想要哪个口径——只给指定的排期人员，还是整个物流部门？","Also, what level of security is desired for the rollout - selected schedulers or all of Logistics?"],[0,"如果你觉得这个排期赶不上，一旦发现就请告诉我。","If you do not feel like this schedule can be met, please let me know as you become aware."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"请确保……周一之前完成","could you please insure that ... complete by Monday"],[0,"他们没来参加演示，能麻烦你跟一下吗","can you follow up with ... since they missed the demo"],[0,"这次上线安全问题想要哪个口径","what level of security is desired for the rollout"],[0,"如果你觉得这个排期赶不上，一旦发现就请告诉我。","If you do not feel like this schedule can be met, please let me know as you become aware."],[3,"排期还在改，改完就发新版","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 交期"],[9,"一份流程图发出去之前，作者先声明「可能已经发过你了」，避免重复引起的尴尬；然后交代排期还在改、最新版在谁手上、改完会给新版。进度类的「暂无结论」邮件就该这么写：不装确定，只讲清楚下一步。",""],[0,"这份我可能已经发过你了。","I may have already sent this to you."],[0,"这是一份流程图，讲我们该怎么搭建、执行，以及后续跟进发现的问题。","It is a process flow for how we should structure, execute, and follow up findings."],[0,"有要改的跟我说。","Let me know if you have any changes."],[0,"另外跟你说一声，排期还在改。","Also, just to let you know, the schedule is still being revised."],[0,"最新一版在 Cassandra 手上，他们改完我就给你发一份新的。","The latest version is with Cassandra. I'll send you a new copy once they've revised it."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"这份我可能已经发过你了。","I may have already sent this to you."],[0,"有要改的跟我说。","Let me know if you have any changes."],[0,"跟你说一声……","just to let you know, ..."],[0,"排期还在改","the schedule is still being revised"],[0,"他们一改完，我就给你发一份新的。","I'll send you a new copy once they've revised it."],[3,"客诉已处理，各方都已告知","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 物流"],[9,"一位英国客户经由议员转来一封投诉信，作者写信给相关方统一口径：投诉一收到就处理了、是直接跟客户解决的、连转信的议员也书面交代过。看它怎么把一桩已了结的投诉讲得滴水不漏——每一步都点明谁做了什么。",""],[0,"你可能已经收到一封投诉信，是我们在英国的一位客户写的，投诉跟 Enron Direct 的一份供气合同有关。","You may have received a complaint letter with regards a gas supply contract with Enron Direct from one of our customers in the UK."],[0,"客户 Forrest 夫妇是通过英国下议院议员 Kenneth Clarke 先生把这封信转给我的。","The customer, Mr and Mrs Forrest wrote to me through Mr Kenneth Clarke who is a Member of the Parliament in the UK."],[0,"投诉一收到，Enron Direct 就着手处理了，问题是我们直接跟客户解决的。","Enron Direct has dealt with the complaint as soon as it was received and we sorted out the issue with the customer directly."],[0,"另外我们还给 Kenneth Clarke 先生写了封信，说明 Enron 采取的措施。","In addition we wrote a letter to Mr Kenneth Clarke explaining the actions taken by Enron."],[0,"这件事已经解决，各方也都告知过了。","The matter is resolved and all the different parties have been informed."],[0,"有任何问题直接找我，需要什么细节我都给你。","If you have any questions please come back to me and I will give all the details you need."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"你可能已经收到一封投诉信……","You may have received a complaint letter ..."],[0,"投诉一收到就处理了","dealt with the complaint as soon as it was received"],[0,"是我们直接跟客户把问题解决的","we sorted out the issue with the customer directly"],[0,"说明 Enron 采取的措施","explaining the actions taken by Enron"],[0,"事情已经解决，各方也都告知过了。","The matter is resolved and all the different parties have been informed."],[0,"有问题直接来找我","please come back to me"]]},{"cid":"em05","title":"确认 · 批准（6 封）· 一句话把事定下来","blocks":[[3,"把两份备忘录发过去，约下一步","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 确认"],[9,"对方之前要两份说明文件，写信人这次一并寄过去，还在信里把两份各自讲什么交代清楚。信很短，但「按要求寄文件—说明内容—约下一步—留个提问的口子」这套流程一步不落，是最值得整封背下来的一类邮件。",""],[0,"按您的要求，附上我们准备的两份并网协议备忘录——第一份讲一般的权利和责任，包括取得并网协议的几种途径。","Per your request, please find the 2 Memos we prepared on interconnection agreements - the first deals with general rights and responsibilities, including options for obtaining ICAs."],[0,"第二份则完全讲 ETI 具体怎么拿并网协议，以及每种做法的利弊。","The second Memo focuses entirely on the specifics of how ETI obtains ICAs, and the advantages and disadvantages of each option."],[0,"您看过之后，咱们再细谈下一步。","Once you have had a chance to review the Memos, we can discuss the next steps in more detail."],[0,"这期间有任何问题，随时问我们。谢谢。","Please feel free to let us know any questions in the meantime. Thanks."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"按您的要求，附上……","Per your request, please find…"],[0,"您看过之后，我们再谈下一步。","Once you have had a chance to review…, we can discuss the next steps."],[0,"这期间有任何问题，随时告诉我们。","Please feel free to let us know any questions in the meantime."],[0,"讲的是；涉及","deals with"],[3,"合同改好发你，希望周四能签","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 确认"],[9,"转让协议的修订稿刚发出去，写信人想要什么很明确：这周四签字。句子都短，口气也客气，但截止时间和「有问题提前说」两个钉子都钉住了。注意 hope 被用了两次，一次放低姿态，一次催进度。",""],[0,"各位：","Everyone,"],[0,"附上修改后的转让协议，希望你们看着没问题。","Attached is a revised assignment agreement which we hope you will find satisfactory."],[0,"我们希望这周四就能签。","Our hope is to have this agreement signed Thursday."],[0,"有米歇尔那边的传真，加上副本签署条款，签字应该好办。","Michelle's fax and counterpart execution clause should facilitate execution."],[0,"签字这块你们要是觉得会出问题，跟我说一声。","Let me know if you expect any problems with execution."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"希望你们觉得满意／没问题","which we hope you will find satisfactory"],[0,"我们希望周四把这份协议签掉。","Our hope is to have this agreement signed Thursday."],[0,"如果……会出问题，跟我说一声","Let me know if you expect any problems with…"],[0,"让签署顺利推进","facilitate execution"],[3,"文件发晚了，先道歉再请你转审","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 确认"],[9,"保密协议草稿拖了几天才转给合作方审。写信人开门就认账，接着预告「可能还要补意见」，最后请对方转给公司里该看的人。三段话干完四件事：道歉、交件、预警、交代流转。",""],[0,"附上我们跟 Enron Net Works 那边合作要用的保密协议草稿。","Attached is a draft of the proposed confidentiality agreement for work to be pursued with Enron Net Works."],[0,"这份文件拖到现在才转给 SunGard 审，实在抱歉。","I sincerely apologize for the delay in forwarding this document to SunGard for review."],[0,"等我再跟业务上几位负责人过一遍，可能还会补几条意见。","It is possible that a few additional comments will need to be added once I have discussed the document further with key business personnel."],[0,"请你们方便时看一下；贵公司里还有谁需要审这类协议、有权批这类协议，也请顺手转过去。","Please review the attached at your convenience and also forward, as necessary, to anyone else in your organization who is required to review and approve agreements of this nature."],[0,"谢谢你耐心等。","Thanks for your patience."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"拖了这么久才把……转过来，非常抱歉","I sincerely apologize for the delay in forwarding…"],[0,"请方便时看一下附件。","Please review the attached at your convenience."],[0,"需要的话转给贵公司里负责……的人","forward, as necessary, to anyone else in your organization who is required to…"],[0,"这类协议","agreements of this nature"],[0,"谢谢你耐心等。","Thanks for your patience."],[3,"协议寄回给我，由我们这边会签","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 确认"],[9,"对方公司先签，再由写信人这边会签。信里把「谁签、地址怎么填、寄给谁」一条条讲明白，一句废话没有，最后留了个万能收尾：你们两位谁有疑问都可以直接找我。",""],[0,"下面是 TFS 公司的 BETA 协议和费用协议，涉及几款欧洲产品。","Below you will find a BETA and Fee Agreement for TFS, Inc. in relation to certain European products."],[0,"这两份协议写明 TFS 是经纪方，所以要由 TFS 的主管来签。","These agreements reflect that TFS, Inc. be the Broker and thus, need to be signed by the appropriate officer of TFS, Inc."],[0,"签好之后（BETA 里 TFS 的地址也要填对），寄回给我，由 Enron 这边会签。","Once they have been signed (and the accurate address for TFS, Inc. completed in the BETA), they should be returned to my attention for countersignature by Enron."],[0,"这件事你们两位谁有疑问、或者还需要什么，跟我说。","Please let me know if either of you should have any questions or need anything further with regard to this matter."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"下面是……","Below you will find…"],[0,"寄回给我（由我这边处理）","returned to my attention"],[0,"供会签","for countersignature"],[0,"你们两位谁有疑问都请告诉我。","Please let me know if either of you should have any questions."],[0,"关于这件事","with regard to this matter"],[3,"保密协议改完，只有一条不让","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 确认"],[9,"电话里没谈拢，写信人干脆把改好的红线稿发过去：意见都标了，唯独独家条款保留原样，还把理由讲透——产品太重要，对方自己也在评估，应该能理解。这是「先改完，再讲道理」的写法。",""],[0,"谢谢你今天早些时候跟我通电话。","Thanks for talking earlier today."],[0,"双边协议这事，我还是希望你们的业务同事说明一下理由；同时 Williams 那版我已经看完了，意见都标上了。","While I still would like to have your business people confirm their rationale for having a bi-lateral agreement, I have looked over the Williams form and noted my comments."],[0,"红线修改版附在下面。","I have attached the redlined version below."],[0,"独家条款我保留了：协议期内独家，终止后还有一年——CommodityLogic 开发的这个产品太重要了。","I have retained the concept of exclusivity for the term of the agreement and for one year following termination as the product developed by CommodityLogic is of significant importance."],[0,"Williams 现在正在评估要不要用，我想你们的业务同事看得出这产品有没有前景，也理解 CommodityLogic 的顾虑。","Since Williams is currently evaluating the product for potential use, I believe your business personnel can appreciate the viability of this product and understand CommodityLogic's concerns."],[0,"希望这份协议能尽快谈定。","I am hopeful that we can reach resolution on this agreement promptly."],[0,"谢谢。","Thanks."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我把……看过一遍，意见标在上面了","I have looked over… and noted my comments"],[0,"红线修改版","the redlined version"],[0,"我保留了独家条款","I have retained the concept of exclusivity"],[0,"能理解……的可行性","can appreciate the viability of…"],[0,"希望我们能尽快谈成。","I am hopeful that we can reach resolution promptly."],[0,"我还是希望……确认一下……","I still would like to have… confirm…"],[3,"邀你去演讲，也要个准信","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 确认"],[9,"外方组织者邀请对方来讲一场，把「讲哪场、你自己来还是派同事来」说得很松，转头又老实交代自己排期太紧，请对方尽快答复。客气话和催命的句子隔了半行，读的时候注意那个 unfortunately 是怎么插进去的。",""],[0,"伊丽莎白：","Dear Elizabeth,"],[0,"附上「信用风险的度量、管理与建模」那场活动的演讲邀请。","Attached is the invitation to speak at \"Measuring, managing and modelling credit risk\"."],[0,"文件打不开的话跟我说。","If you have any problems opening the file please get in touch."],[0,"我建议的是会前研讨会的第 5 场，不过第 3 场也还空着。","I have suggested talk 5 in the pre-conference seminar, however, talk 3 is also available."],[0,"你来讲、你同事来讲，讲一个还是两个都讲，我都非常欢迎。","I would be more than happy for you or your colleague to speak on either or both of these subjects."],[0,"可惜我这边时间卡得特别紧，能不能来讲，请你尽快给个准信，非常感谢。","I am unfortunately working to a very tight schedule so if you could let me know ASAP if you could speak I would very much appreciate it."],[0,"多谢","Many Thanks"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"文件打不开请联系我。","If you have any problems opening the file please get in touch."],[0,"你或你同事……我都非常欢迎","I would be more than happy for you or your colleague to…"],[0,"可惜我这边时间非常紧","I am unfortunately working to a very tight schedule"],[0,"请尽快告诉我……非常感谢","if you could let me know ASAP… I would very much appreciate it"],[0,"多谢","Many thanks"]]},{"cid":"em06","title":"婉拒 · 坏消息（2 封）· 给不了、做不到，怎么说","blocks":[[3,"数据缺口补不上，只能这样推定","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 坏消息"],[9,"对方在追一份合同可用量的数据。写信人先道谢、再认同对方的顾虑，然后解释自己为什么拿不到（人不在，也不知道存在哪），最后给一个替代口径，顺带提了个小请求。通篇没有一句「我不知道」就完了。",""],[0,"谢谢你的意见。","Thanks for the input."],[0,"你跟德国那边继续往前推，我很感激；这事会影响我们谈判筹码，我很清楚。","I appreciate you moving forward with Germany and I most definitely recognize the issue concerning leverage."],[0,"德国那边有时候不太明白我们拿到这些数据有多重要。","Germany sometimes does not recognize the importance of us obtaining said data."],[0,"我基本可以肯定贝基 9 月以后更新过，但她人不在，我拿不到她的原始数据，也不知道她存在哪儿。","I am quite positive that Becky had an update since Sep01, but since she is out, I don't have access to her source data, and not sure where she stores the information."],[0,"所以我只能推定，德国最近发来的那批数字里应该就包含缺的那块。","Thus, I presume the latest numbers sent from Germany should contain the numbers in the gap."],[0,"你要是能把合同约定可用量的电子版发我，那就太好了。","If you could send an electronic copy of the contractual availability, that would be appreciated."],[0,"谢谢，","Thanks,"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"感谢你在……上继续推进","I appreciate you moving forward with…"],[0,"关于……的问题，我很清楚","I most definitely recognize the issue concerning…"],[0,"她人不在（休假、外出）","since she is out"],[0,"我推定；估计……","I presume…"],[0,"如果能发……过来，非常感谢。","If you could send…, that would be appreciated."],[3,"已经逾期了，还是想请你宽限","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 坏消息"],[9,"截止日已经过了，写信人还是把这封信发了出去：先说原因，再承认自己迟了，然后明确要延到哪天，最后一句把姿态放低。信不是商务往来，是向老师请假，但「认错—给理由—提方案—道谢」这四步，写交期延后、资料迟交全能套。",""],[0,"因为家里出了急事、孩子身体不好，我想申请把期中考试的完成时间延到 2001 年 11 月 7 日。","Due to a family crisis concerning my son's health, I am requesting an extension on completing the mid-term exam until 11/7/01."],[0,"我知道截止日已经过了，只是工作和孩子的情况夹在一起，这封信才拖到现在。","I realize the deadline had already passed but between work and my son's condition I was delayed in sending this e-mail."],[0,"这次延期要是能通融，我非常感谢。","I appreciate any help you can provide in this extension."],[0,"此致","Sincerely,"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"我想申请把……延到……","I am requesting an extension on… until…"],[0,"我知道截止日已经过了","I realize the deadline had already passed"],[0,"这封信才拖到现在","I was delayed in sending this e-mail"],[0,"如能帮忙，非常感谢。","I appreciate any help you can provide."]]},{"cid":"em07","title":"道歉 · 补救（6 封）· 认错、补救、划清界线","blocks":[[3,"时间表定太满，只能往后挪","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 道歉"],[9,"组里的人等一份草稿。写信人先自嘲时间表定得太满，再交代进度（材料看完了、问题还没答），给出新的交付时间，最后留一句「谁那边不方便就说」。道歉里一句借口都没有，是这封信最值钱的地方。",""],[0,"唉，当初排这个时间表，我明显是太想当然了。抱歉。","Well, I was clearly too ambitious in setting out the schedule. My apologies."],[0,"昨晚总算把材料啃完了，但问题还没开始答。","I managed to trudge through the reading and the document last night, but didn't get to answering the question."],[0,"这个周末看样子会很忙。","It appears that this will be a busy weekend."],[0,"我感觉要拖到周六下午，才能把初稿发给大家看。","I've a feeling that I won't get my proposed answer to folks until Saturday afternoon for your review."],[0,"要是这样谁那边不方便，跟我说一声。","If that poses a problem for anyone, please let me know."],[0,"汇总的活儿还是我来干，大家写好自己那部分就尽管发出来。","I still intend to be the compiler of wisdom, so folks should feel free to distribute when they've got something drafted."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"时间表我当初定得太满。","I was clearly too ambitious in setting out the schedule."],[0,"抱歉。","My apologies."],[0,"如果这样对谁有影响，请告诉我。","If that poses a problem for anyone, please let me know."],[0,"我感觉要拖到……才能……","I've a feeling that I won't get… until…"],[0,"尽管……；不用客气","feel free to…"],[0,"硬着头皮啃完","trudge through"],[3,"晚了，先补四份再催你意见","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 道歉"],[9,"一批文件说明拖了期。写信人先道歉，把这次的补上，交代后面几份什么时候到，然后话锋一转开始催对方回意见；连对方传真发黑这种小事，也用一句 It's just that 说得不刺人。",""],[0,"抱歉，拖了。","Sorry for the delay."],[0,"这是接下来的四份说明。","Here are the next four descriptions."],[0,"这几份我先给我们项目组的 David Forster 过一遍，再发给你。","I have sent these to David Forster in our Project group to review first before I send them to yourself."],[0,"今天要是收不回来，我周末也发给你，保证周一你手上就有。","If I don't get them back today I will send them over the weekend so they are there for you on Monday."],[0,"其余那些说明，你今天能不能把意见回给我。","Could you please send me comments back on all the other descriptions today."],[0,"你那边的传真机还好吧？上次那份传过来底色发黑，批注看着有点费劲。","Is your fax machine at your end OK? It's just that the other fax you sent came through a dark background making the comments a little hard to read."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"抱歉，拖了。","Sorry for the delay."],[0,"保证你周一就能拿到","so they are there for you on Monday"],[0,"能否把……的意见回给我","Could you please send me comments back on…"],[0,"主要是因为……（委婉说理由）","It's just that…"],[0,"你那边的传真机还正常吗？","Is your fax machine at your end OK?"],[3,"电话是我们弄断的，但话得说清","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 道歉"],[9,"对方的电话线被误断了，写信人先认错、说明现状，然后笔锋一转：你对我同事那种态度我不接。道歉和划界限写在同一封信里，最后还搬出公司价值观收尾——这种写法不好学，但特别值得看。",""],[0,"您的电话被误断了，我道歉。","I apologize that your phone was disconnected in error."],[0,"现在电话已经通了，语音信箱还需要您自己设一下。","At this time your phone is working and your Voice Mail box needs to be set up."],[0,"不过我想补一句：您对我同事那种不尊重、那些不合理的要求，我不接受。","I would like to add however, I do not appreciate your disrespect and unreasonable demands placed on my employees."],[0,"问题不是他们造成的，他们能做的只是把您的情况转给对口部门。","They were not the cause of this problem and can only relay your information to the appropriate group."],[0,"我们公司的价值观是尊重、诚信、沟通、卓越。希望您抽空看一看。","Enron has values of Respect, Integrity, Communication and Excellence. I would appreciate you taking the time to review them."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"……被误断了，我道歉。","I apologize that… was disconnected in error."],[0,"不过我想补一句，我不接受……","I would like to add however, I do not appreciate…"],[0,"压在我同事身上的要求","demands placed on my employees"],[0,"问题不是他们造成的。","They were not the cause of this problem."],[0,"希望您抽空看一下。","I would appreciate you taking the time to review them."],[3,"回晚了，还得麻烦你再讲一遍","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 道歉"],[9,"对方圣诞节前来过电话，留言没记清楚，写信人拖了很久才回。除了道歉，他还得请对方把问题重说一遍——这种请求最容易写得生硬，看他怎么用一句 I would be happy to 把话拉回来。后半段聊天气，是给这封道歉信松绑的。",""],[0,"您圣诞节前来过电话，留言我收到了。拖了这么久才回，抱歉。","I received the message you called before Christmas. I apologize for the extended delay."],[0,"一直想跟您联系上。","I wanted to follow up with you."],[0,"可惜帮忙记话的人没记清楚，能不能麻烦您把问题再说一遍？我去帮您查。","Unfortunately, the message-taker was not efficient, thus if you could specify again your question I would be happy to research it out for you."],[0,"麻烦告诉我。","Please let me know."],[0,"圣诞和新年过得怎么样？","How was your Christmas and New Year's holidays?"],[0,"我回宾州老家过的节，跟家人朋友又聚了一次，挺好的。","I returned home for the holidays to Pennsylvania. It was wonderful to visit again with family and friends."],[0,"不过一下飞机，最高才 6 度，真有点扛不住。","But I will have to admit it was quite shocking to arrive off the plane to a high of 6 degrees."],[0,"看来我已经很习惯旧金山这种不冷不热的天气了。","I guess I have become quite acclimated to the temperate climate here in San Francisco."],[0,"期待继续跟您合作。","Looking forward to continue working with you."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"拖了这么久，抱歉。","I apologize for the extended delay."],[0,"一直想跟进一下您的事。","I wanted to follow up with you."],[0,"能否把问题再说一遍，我很乐意……","if you could specify again your question I would be happy to…"],[0,"我大概是习惯……了","I guess I have become quite acclimated to…"],[3,"以为发了其实没发，赶紧补上","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 道歉"],[9,"文件本该上周就到对方手上，写信人翻记录才发现根本没发。全信只有三句：交件、请对方确认后签、然后老实交代。没有「系统问题」「最近太忙」这类借口，短得让人挑不出话。",""],[0,"这是一份协议函的草稿，用来修订线上电子交易协议。","Here is a draft of a letter agreement amending the online Electronic Trading Agreement."],[0,"你看行就说一声，我让人签好一份传真给你。","Please let me know if it is ok and I will have a copy executed and faxed over to you."],[0,"拖了这么久，抱歉——我本以为上周就发你了，可怎么也找不到记录，看来是没发。","My apologies for the delay - I thought I had sent this to you last week but I can't find any record of it so I must not have done it."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"你觉得行就说一声，我就……","Please let me know if it is ok and I will…"],[0,"让人把一份签好","have a copy executed"],[0,"找不到记录，看来是没做。","I can't find any record of it so I must not have done it."],[0,"拖了，抱歉。","My apologies for the delay."],[3,"稿子拖太久，道歉放头尾","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 道歉"],[9,"一份加了批注的草稿压了很久才回给对方。写信人把道歉放在开头，中间交代改了什么、请对方看哪里、还留了「附件打不开告诉我」，结尾再道一次歉。首尾各一次，是英文邮件里很常见的夹心式道歉。",""],[0,"黛布拉、阿莉莎：","Debra and Alisha,"],[0,"这份草稿拖了这么久才回给你们，我很抱歉。","I apologize for the extended length of time it has taken for me to return this draft to you."],[0,"改动我尽量都标出来了，都是上次跟黛布拉沟通、后来又跟 KU 法务谈过之后改的。","I have tried to highlight the changes that resulted from my last communication with Debra and subsequent discussion with KU's legal counsel."],[0,"请看一下附件和附的封面页。","Please review the addendum and the attached cover page."],[0,"有任何问题随时打给我，我跟你细说。","If you should have any questions, feel free to give me a call and I will be happy to discuss them with you."],[0,"附件打不开跟我说一声。","Please let me know if you are unable to open this attachment."],[0,"再次为拖延致歉。","Again, I apologize for the delay."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"拖了这么久才……，非常抱歉","I apologize for the extended length of time it has taken for me to…"],[0,"改动我尽量都标出来了","I have tried to highlight the changes"],[0,"有任何问题随时打给我。","If you should have any questions, feel free to give me a call."],[0,"附件打不开请告诉我。","Please let me know if you are unable to open this attachment."],[0,"再次为拖延致歉。","Again, I apologize for the delay."]]},{"cid":"em08","title":"请人评审 · 给意见（5 封）· 请人看稿，话要说得让人愿意看","blocks":[[3,"帮完一个忙，再提一个请求","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 请人评审"],[9,"对方刚帮着处理完一批合同，写信人又来要一份法务审查备忘录。开口先谢，用 but 一转，然后解释为什么现在特别需要——最近折腾新交易，反倒看出旧合同的毛病。把「这活儿该干」的理由摊在对方面前，比单纯说 please 有用。",""],[0,"米德兰那几份合同多谢你帮忙，不过信贷部还有个请求。","Thanks for helping with Midland contracts, but Credit has one more request."],[0,"方便的时候，希望你就现有的 MCV 合同出一份法务审查／风险备忘录，我们归档用。","When possible, we would appreciate a Legal Review/Risk Memo on the existing MCV contracts to add to our file."],[0,"最近折腾新交易、新合同，反倒让大家对现有合同有点不放心，特别是商务条款、担保权、终止权，还有那份同意协议。","The recent laboring on the new deal and contract has raised concerns about the contract, especially commercial terms, collateral rights, termination rights and the Consent Agreement."],[0,"另外我了解到，西尔维娅还想接着做新合同和以后要用的《主担保协议》，所以把拟签的这份也审一遍，我觉得有好处。","Also, it is my understanding that Sylvia would like to continue working on the new contract and Master Collateral Agreement for future transactions, so I believe that a review of the proposed contract is beneficial as well."],[0,"再次感谢；这件事有任何反馈，我都非常感激。","Thanks again for the help and I would greatly appreciate any feedback on this issue."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"信贷部还有个请求。","Credit has one more request."],[0,"方便的时候，希望……","When possible, we would appreciate…"],[0,"据我了解……","it is my understanding that…"],[0,"这件事有任何反馈，我都非常感谢。","I would greatly appreciate any feedback on this issue."],[0,"再次感谢帮忙。","Thanks again for the help."],[3,"按你的意见改好了，另加两点","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 请人评审"],[9,"对方提的修改全部吸收，写信人只在措辞上动了动，还特意说明「本意没动」——这句话等于告诉对方我没偷偷改你的意思。随后把自己这边新增的两项要求摆出来，一条一条，不含糊。",""],[0,"下面附上更新后的 BETA，你之前提的修改都放进去了。","I have attached below a copy of the updated BETA reflecting the changes you proposed earlier."],[0,"你的方案我加了点措辞，但本意没动。","I have added some language to your proposals, but have kept the intention intact."],[0,"我这边只剩两点补充：一是要 Natsource LLC 出一封确认函，说明 Natsource 开出的信用证对 Natsource-Tullet 同样适用（实质就是担保函）；二是如果信用证已经开了，就得改一下，让 Enron 在 Natsource-Tullet 名下也能凭它收款。","The only additional comments that I will make are that Enron will require (a) a confirmatory letter from Natsource LLC that the LC posted by Natsource will be applicable to Natsource-Tullet (in essence a guarantee letter) and (b) if an LC has already been posted, it will need to be modified so that it will reflect the ability of Enron to realize under it for Natsource-Tullet."],[0,"要是还没开证，后面这点就在开证时一并处理。","If no LC has been issued, this latter point will need to be handled in any LC issued."],[0,"请看下附件，还有别的再跟我说。","Please take a look at the attached and let me know if anything further."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"你先前提出的修改都反映进去了","reflecting the changes you proposed earlier"],[0,"我在你的方案上加了些措辞，但本意没变。","I have added some language to your proposals, but have kept the intention intact."],[0,"我这边只剩几点补充……","The only additional comments that I will make are…"],[0,"请看一下附件，有别的再告诉我。","Please take a look at the attached and let me know if anything further."],[0,"实质上","in essence"],[3,"两件事问到哪一步了，请回","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 请人评审"],[9,"三句话催两件事：给合作方的意见发出去没有，备忘录谈到哪了。最后一句把「为什么急」说明白——不是催你个人，是整体排期卡住了。催进度还能写得这么不伤面子，靠的就是这两句固定问法。",""],[0,"唐：","Don,"],[0,"给 NPC 的并网协议意见，你那边走到哪一步了？发出去了吗？","Where are you with providing comments back to NPC on the interconnection agreement? Did this get issued?"],[0,"还有跟 NPC 的那份备忘录，现在什么情况？","Also, where do we stand on the MOU with NPC?"],[0,"这两件事得往前推，不然整体排期要受影响。","It's important relative to our schedule that these items keep moving."],[0,"请回复，","Please advise,"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"……你做到哪一步了？","Where are you with…?"],[0,"……现在是什么状况？","where do we stand on…?"],[0,"从排期上看，……很重要。","It's important relative to our schedule that…"],[0,"请指示；请回复。","Please advise."],[3,"都照你改，只有一条要商量","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 请人评审"],[9,"对方把整份保密协议改了一遍。写信人逐条看完，基本全收，只对开头一处定义提出反建议，自己拟了措辞，还点明「你改的那句比实际要谈的范围大了一点」。最后把后续动作讲清楚：你点头，我就并进终稿送签。",""],[0,"查克：","Chuck,"],[0,"约翰·阿拉里奥把你对保密协议的修改意见转给我了，让我看看。","John Allario forwarded the comments you made to the NDA for my review and comment."],[0,"修改我基本都同意，只有开头那段关于业务关系的改动除外。","I agree with all revisions, but the change to the business relationship provision in the introductory paragraph."],[0,"我建议把“项目”写成：“……双方各自的关联公司愿意就可能的业务往来，互相提供与使用 EnronOnline 平台或软件有关的信息（下称‘项目’）……”","I would propose that we state the \"Project\" to be \"... each of Enron's and Amerada's affiliates are prepared to furnish each other with information in connection with a possible business transaction or relationship based upon use of the EnronOnline platform or software (the \"Project\")...\""],[0,"你改的那句，比实际打算谈的范围大了一点。","The statement made in your revision is a bit beyond what is actually intended to be discussed."],[0,"你看看这样改行不行，说说你的想法。","Please consider this change and let me know your thoughts."],[0,"如果这样没问题，我就把它和你其他意见一起并进终稿，然后盯着把终稿送去签。","If this is acceptable, I will incorporate it into final agreements, together with your other comments, and see that final agreements are forwarded for signature."],[0,"谢谢。","Thanks."],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"修改我基本都同意，只是……","I agree with all revisions, but…"],[0,"我建议我们写成……","I would propose that we state…"],[0,"比实际打算的范围大了一点","is a bit beyond what is actually intended"],[0,"说说你的想法","let me know your thoughts"],[0,"如果这样可以，我就把它并进……","If this is acceptable, I will incorporate it into…"],[0,"确保……送去签署","see that… are forwarded for signature"],[3,"稿子发你审，意见请转给同事","Enron 真实邮件 · B1–B2 · 请人评审"],[9,"写信人马上休假，还是把改好的文件发出来，把签字日期、参考文件、意见交给谁全交代清楚。全信没有一句客套，但事情交代得干干净净——休假前的交接可以照这个写。",""],[0,"附上修改后的项目启动文件。","Attached please find the revised Inception Document."],[0,"请审阅。","Please review the document."],[0,"我们 4 月 24 日星期二会把这份文件发出去签。","We will be circulating the Inception Document for signature on Tuesday, April 24th."],[0,"项目计划和工期估算的细节，见附件里的 Project 文件。","Please refer to the attached Microsoft Project file for the detail of project plan and timeline estimate."],[0,"意见请直接发给 Dave Nommensen，我要休假了。","Please send your comments to Dave Nommensen since I will be on vacation."],[0,"谢谢，","Thanks,"],[4,"最该记住的表达","Key expressions"],[0,"兹附上……","Attached please find…"],[0,"我们将在……把……发出去签","We will be circulating… for signature on…"],[0,"……的细节请见附件","Please refer to the attached file for the detail of…"],[0,"我休假，意见请发给 X。","Please send your comments to X since I will be on vacation."]]}]}];
